              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Impact\n\nSince 2006 / pylint 0.15.2, pylint caches its stats as pickles in `PYLINT_HOME` and reload them on the next run with `pickle.load`. Someone without access to the configuration or linted code, but with access to the cache directory (predictable `PYLINT_HOME` on a multi-user host) can write a crafted pickle that will runs arbitrary code when pylint access its stat cache.\n\n### Patches\n\nFrom pylint 4.0.9, the result cache is now stored as JSON instead of pickle, preventing code-execution. \n\n### Workarounds\n\nUntil upgrading do not point `PYLINT_HOME` to an untrusted, shared, or group-writable directory. The default value, `~/.cache/pylint`, is writable only by the user running pylint.\n\n### Credits\n\n- Reported privately via Tidelift coordinated disclosure (Dan Lenz).",
                "text": "### Impact\n\nSince 2006 / pylint 0.15.2, pylint caches its stats as pickles in `PYLINT_HOME` and reload them on the next run with `pickle.load`. Someone without access to the configuration or linted code, but with access to the cache directory (predictable `PYLINT_HOME` on a multi-user host) can write a crafted pickle that will runs arbitrary code when pylint access its stat cache.\n\n### Patches\n\nFrom pylint 4.0.9, the result cache is now stored as JSON instead of pickle, preventing code-execution. \n\n### Workarounds\n\nUntil upgrading do not point `PYLINT_HOME` to an untrusted, shared, or group-writable directory. The default value, `~/.cache/pylint`, is writable only by the user running pylint.\n\n### Credits\n\n- Reported privately via Tidelift coordinated disclosure (Dan Lenz)."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-114608](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-114608)**.\n\n## [GHSA-22qq-2fwx-7p67](https://osv.dev/GHSA-22qq-2fwx-7p67)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Since 2006 / pylint 0.15.2, pylint caches its stats as pickles in `PYLINT_HOME` and reload them on the next run with `pickle.load`. Someone without access to the configuration or linted code, but with access to the cache directory (predictable `PYLINT_HOME` on a multi-user host) can write a crafted pickle that will runs arbitrary code when pylint access its stat cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e \n\u003e From pylint 4.0.9, the result cache is now stored as JSON instead of pickle, preventing code-execution. \n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e \n\u003e Until upgrading do not point `PYLINT_HOME` to an untrusted, shared, or group-writable directory. The default value, `~/.cache/pylint`, is writable only by the user running pylint.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e - Reported privately via Tidelift coordinated disclosure (Dan Lenz).\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | pylint | 4.0.7 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-22qq-2fwx-7p67 | pylint | 4.0.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-114608\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-114608](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-114608)**.\n\n## [GHSA-22qq-2fwx-7p67](https://osv.dev/GHSA-22qq-2fwx-7p67)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Since 2006 / pylint 0.15.2, pylint caches its stats as pickles in `PYLINT_HOME` and reload them on the next run with `pickle.load`. Someone without access to the configuration or linted code, but with access to the cache directory (predictable `PYLINT_HOME` on a multi-user host) can write a crafted pickle that will runs arbitrary code when pylint access its stat cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e \n\u003e From pylint 4.0.9, the result cache is now stored as JSON instead of pickle, preventing code-execution. \n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e \n\u003e Until upgrading do not point `PYLINT_HOME` to an untrusted, shared, or group-writable directory. The default value, `~/.cache/pylint`, is writable only by the user running pylint.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e - Reported privately via Tidelift coordinated disclosure (Dan Lenz).\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | pylint | 4.0.7 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-22qq-2fwx-7p67 | pylint | 4.0.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-114608\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
