y:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-114605\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-114605](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-114605)**.\n\n## [GHSA-45c3-73f7-pv4m](https://osv.dev/GHSA-45c3-73f7-pv4m)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e A maliciously crafted DNS message may cause dns.name.from_wire_parser() to use excessive CPU for DNS name decompression.  Applications that process untrusted DNS wire form messages with dnspython may be degraded or DoS'd by the extra CPU use required.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e This problem is fixed in dnspython 2.9.0.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e There are no known workarounds.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Credit\n\u003e Evgenios Gkritsis, Department of Informatics, University of Piraeus \u0026 Athena Research Center, Greece\n\u003e Constantinos Patsakis, Department of Informatics, University of Piraeus \u0026 Athena Research Center, Greece\n\u003e George Stergiopoulos, Department of Informatics, Athens University of Economics and Business, Greece\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | dnspython | 2.7.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-45c3-73f7-pv4m | dnspython | 2.9.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-114605\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
