              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Summary\n\n`launch-editor` checked `fs.existsSync(fileName)` before passing a supplied path to an editor command. On Windows, an attacker can bypass this check with a crafted path ending in `\\\\..:line:column`. This removes the requirement that the attacker be able to place a file with a malicious filename.\n\nCombined with the `%` escaping issue described in [GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv](https://github.com/vitejs/launch-editor/security/advisories/GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv), this bypass can lead to OS command injection when an attacker controls the file argument.\n\n### Impact\n\nOnly apps that runs on Windows is affected.\n\n### Details\n\nThe earlier advisory assumed that `fs.existsSync()` required an attacker-controlled filename to exist. This advisory covers a bypass of that requirement.\n\nA crafted value ending in `\\\\..:1:1` is interpreted differently by `launch-editor-middleware`, `launch-editor`, and Windows:\n\n1. `launch-editor-middleware` calls `path.resolve()` while the final path component is `..:1:1`, so it is not treated as a parent-directory component.\n2. `launch-editor` treats `:1:1` as a line-and-column suffix and removes it, leaving a path ending in `\\\\..`.\n3. On Windows, `fs.existsSync()` accepts the resulting path as the existing parent directory even though the attacker-controlled preceding component does not exist.\n4. Because the existence check passes, the crafted filename reaches the Windows shell command.",
                "text": "### Summary\n\n`launch-editor` checked `fs.existsSync(fileName)` before passing a supplied path to an editor command. On Windows, an attacker can bypass this check with a crafted path ending in `\\\\..:line:column`. This removes the requirement that the attacker be able to place a file with a malicious filename.\n\nCombined with the `%` escaping issue described in [GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv](https://github.com/vitejs/launch-editor/security/advisories/GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv), this bypass can lead to OS command injection when an attacker controls the file argument.\n\n### Impact\n\nOnly apps that runs on Windows is affected.\n\n### Details\n\nThe earlier advisory assumed that `fs.existsSync()` required an attacker-controlled filename to exist. This advisory covers a bypass of that requirement.\n\nA crafted value ending in `\\\\..:1:1` is interpreted differently by `launch-editor-middleware`, `launch-editor`, and Windows:\n\n1. `launch-editor-middleware` calls `path.resolve()` while the final path component is `..:1:1`, so it is not treated as a parent-directory component.\n2. `launch-editor` treats `:1:1` as a line-and-column suffix and removes it, leaving a path ending in `\\\\..`.\n3. On Windows, `fs.existsSync()` accepts the resulting path as the existing parent directory even though the attacker-controlled preceding component does not exist.\n4. Because the existence check passes, the crafted filename reaches the Windows shell command."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-112942](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-112942)**.\n\n## [GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm](https://osv.dev/GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e `launch-editor` checked `fs.existsSync(fileName)` before passing a supplied path to an editor command. On Windows, an attacker can bypass this check with a crafted path ending in `\\\\..:line:column`. This removes the requirement that the attacker be able to place a file with a malicious filename.\n\u003e \n\u003e Combined with the `%` escaping issue described in [GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv](https://github.com/vitejs/launch-editor/security/advisories/GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv), this bypass can lead to OS command injection when an attacker controls the file argument.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Only apps that runs on Windows is affected.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e \n\u003e The earlier advisory assumed that `fs.existsSync()` required an attacker-controlled filename to exist. This advisory covers a bypass of that requirement.\n\u003e \n\u003e A crafted value ending in `\\\\..:1:1` is interpreted differently by `launch-editor-middleware`, `launch-editor`, and Windows:\n\u003e \n\u003e 1. `launch-editor-middleware` calls `path.resolve()` while the final path component is `..:1:1`, so it is not treated as a parent-directory component.\n\u003e 2. `launch-editor` treats `:1:1` as a line-and-column suffix and removes it, leaving a path ending in `\\\\..`.\n\u003e 3. On Windows, `fs.existsSync()` accepts the resulting path as the existing parent directory even though the attacker-controlled preceding component does not exist.\n\u003e 4. Because the existence check passes, the crafted filename reaches the Windows shell command.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | launch-editor | 2.14.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | launch-editor | 2.14.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm | launch-editor | 2.14.2 |\n| GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm | vite | 6.4.4, 7.3.7, 8.1.6, 8.2.4, 8.3.3 |\n| GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm | vite-plus | 1.1.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112942\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112942\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-112942](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-112942)**.\n\n## [GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm](https://osv.dev/GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e `launch-editor` checked `fs.existsSync(fileName)` before passing a supplied path to an editor command. On Windows, an attacker can bypass this check with a crafted path ending in `\\\\..:line:column`. This removes the requirement that the attacker be able to place a file with a malicious filename.\n\u003e \n\u003e Combined with the `%` escaping issue described in [GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv](https://github.com/vitejs/launch-editor/security/advisories/GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv), this bypass can lead to OS command injection when an attacker controls the file argument.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Only apps that runs on Windows is affected.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e \n\u003e The earlier advisory assumed that `fs.existsSync()` required an attacker-controlled filename to exist. This advisory covers a bypass of that requirement.\n\u003e \n\u003e A crafted value ending in `\\\\..:1:1` is interpreted differently by `launch-editor-middleware`, `launch-editor`, and Windows:\n\u003e \n\u003e 1. `launch-editor-middleware` calls `path.resolve()` while the final path component is `..:1:1`, so it is not treated as a parent-directory component.\n\u003e 2. `launch-editor` treats `:1:1` as a line-and-column suffix and removes it, leaving a path ending in `\\\\..`.\n\u003e 3. On Windows, `fs.existsSync()` accepts the resulting path as the existing parent directory even though the attacker-controlled preceding component does not exist.\n\u003e 4. Because the existence check passes, the crafted filename reaches the Windows shell command.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | launch-editor | 2.14.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | launch-editor | 2.14.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm | launch-editor | 2.14.2 |\n| GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm | vite | 6.4.4, 7.3.7, 8.1.6, 8.2.4, 8.3.3 |\n| GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm | vite-plus | 1.1.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112942\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112942\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
