              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-111064](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-111064)**.\n\n## [GHSA-5wr8-gcqf-gqf3](https://osv.dev/GHSA-5wr8-gcqf-gqf3)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The keepalive timeout was not used during the initial portion of a request.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e An attacker could keep an idle connection open indefinitely before sending any data.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workaround\n\u003e \n\u003e Use a reverse proxy (as recommended for all production deployments) with sensible keepalive limits.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | aiohttp | 3.14.3 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-5wr8-gcqf-gqf3 | aiohttp | 3.14.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-111064\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-111064](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-111064)**.\n\n## [GHSA-5wr8-gcqf-gqf3](https://osv.dev/GHSA-5wr8-gcqf-gqf3)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The keepalive timeout was not used during the initial portion of a request.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e An attacker could keep an idle connection open indefinitely before sending any data.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workaround\n\u003e \n\u003e Use a reverse proxy (as recommended for all production deployments) with sensible keepalive limits.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | aiohttp | 3.14.3 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-5wr8-gcqf-gqf3 | aiohttp | 3.14.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-111064\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
              },
              "id": "CVE-2026-111064",
              "name": "CVE-2026-111064",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.2"
