              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Impact\nAny application that validates a user-supplied string with `Joi.string().isoDate()` can be stalled by a single request. One of the regular expressions the rule runs over the input was unanchored, so a valid ISO date followed by a long run of fractional-second digits made the regex engine restart its search from every position in the string, costing time proportional to the square of the input length. 64 KB of digits costs about 1.4 s and 256 KB about 22 s.\n\n### Patches\nUpgrade to version 17.13.7 or 18.2.6 depending on your current major version.\n\n### Workarounds\nNone except capping the length of the string before it reaches joi.",
                "text": "### Impact\nAny application that validates a user-supplied string with `Joi.string().isoDate()` can be stalled by a single request. One of the regular expressions the rule runs over the input was unanchored, so a valid ISO date followed by a long run of fractional-second digits made the regex engine restart its search from every position in the string, costing time proportional to the square of the input length. 64 KB of digits costs about 1.4 s and 256 KB about 22 s.\n\n### Patches\nUpgrade to version 17.13.7 or 18.2.6 depending on your current major version.\n\n### Workarounds\nNone except capping the length of the string before it reaches joi."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-92599](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-92599)**.\n\n## [GHSA-6h2x-m376-mqjq](https://osv.dev/GHSA-6h2x-m376-mqjq)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e Any application that validates a user-supplied string with `Joi.string().isoDate()` can be stalled by a single request. One of the regular expressions the rule runs over the input was unanchored, so a valid ISO date followed by a long run of fractional-second digits made the regex engine restart its search from every position in the string, costing time proportional to the square of the input length. 64 KB of digits costs about 1.4 s and 256 KB about 22 s.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e Upgrade to version 17.13.7 or 18.2.6 depending on your current major version.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e None except capping the length of the string before it reaches joi.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | joi | 17.13.4 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | joi | 18.2.3 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | joi | 17.13.4 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | joi | 18.2.3 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-6h2x-m376-mqjq | joi | 17.13.7, 18.2.6 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-92599\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-92599\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-92599](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-92599)**.\n\n## [GHSA-6h2x-m376-mqjq](https://osv.dev/GHSA-6h2x-m376-mqjq)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e Any application that validates a user-supplied string with `Joi.string().isoDate()` can be stalled by a single request. One of the regular expressions the rule runs over the input was unanchored, so a valid ISO date followed by a long run of fractional-second digits made the regex engine restart its search from every position in the string, costing time proportional to the square of the input length. 64 KB of digits costs about 1.4 s and 256 KB about 22 s.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e Upgrade to version 17.13.7 or 18.2.6 depending on your current major version.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e None except capping the length of the string before it reaches joi.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | joi | 17.13.4 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | joi | 18.2.3 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | joi | 17.13.4 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | joi | 18.2.3 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-6h2x-m376-mqjq | joi | 17.13.7, 18.2.6 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-92599\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-92599\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
