              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Summary\n\nAn attacker sending an absolute-form request can spoof the scheme used.\n\n### Impact\n\nIf user code depends on the `Request.scheme` attribute for anything security related, an attacker may be able to circumvent this logic, tricking the application into thinking a connection is encrypted when it is not, or vice versa.\n\n### Workaround\n\nA WAF rule to reject absolute-form requests (legitimate requests should only use this form for proxies).",
                "text": "### Summary\n\nAn attacker sending an absolute-form request can spoof the scheme used.\n\n### Impact\n\nIf user code depends on the `Request.scheme` attribute for anything security related, an attacker may be able to circumvent this logic, tricking the application into thinking a connection is encrypted when it is not, or vice versa.\n\n### Workaround\n\nA WAF rule to reject absolute-form requests (legitimate requests should only use this form for proxies)."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-111748](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-111748)**.\n\n## [GHSA-f9xw-jh8m-3mwq](https://osv.dev/GHSA-f9xw-jh8m-3mwq)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e An attacker sending an absolute-form request can spoof the scheme used.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e If user code depends on the `Request.scheme` attribute for anything security related, an attacker may be able to circumvent this logic, tricking the application into thinking a connection is encrypted when it is not, or vice versa.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workaround\n\u003e \n\u003e A WAF rule to reject absolute-form requests (legitimate requests should only use this form for proxies).\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | aiohttp | 3.14.3 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-f9xw-jh8m-3mwq | aiohttp | 3.14.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-111748\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-111748](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-111748)**.\n\n## [GHSA-f9xw-jh8m-3mwq](https://osv.dev/GHSA-f9xw-jh8m-3mwq)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e An attacker sending an absolute-form request can spoof the scheme used.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e If user code depends on the `Request.scheme` attribute for anything security related, an attacker may be able to circumvent this logic, tricking the application into thinking a connection is encrypted when it is not, or vice versa.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workaround\n\u003e \n\u003e A WAF rule to reject absolute-form requests (legitimate requests should only use this form for proxies).\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | aiohttp | 3.14.3 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-f9xw-jh8m-3mwq | aiohttp | 3.14.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-111748\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
              },
