              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-115754](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-115754)**.\n\n## [GHSA-m5mm-p8h7-m29v](https://osv.dev/GHSA-m5mm-p8h7-m29v)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e `serialize-javascript` escapes its output so it is safe to embed inside a\n\u003e `\u003cscript\u003e` element. Before 7.1.3 that guarantee did not hold for a **function\n\u003e value whose source ends in a bare `\u003c/script`**.\n\u003e \n\u003e Each function body is escaped on its own, and a bare `\u003c/script` was only\n\u003e neutralized when followed — within the same body — by a character the HTML\n\u003e tokenizer treats as ending the tag name (TAB, LF, FF, CR, SPACE, `/` or `\u003e`).\n\u003e A body ending exactly at `\u003c/script` has no following character, so it was\n\u003e emitted unescaped. The delimiter is then supplied by the surrounding output\n\u003e (for example the newline the `space` option emits after the value), and a\n\u003e later serialized value can supply the closing `\u003e` followed by markup:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```js\n\u003e const serialize = require('serialize-javascript');\n\u003e function f() {} f.toString = () =\u003e 'function f(){ return 1 }//\u003c/script';\n\u003e function g() {} g.toString = () =\u003e 'function g(x){ return x } \u003e \u003cimg src=x onerror=alert(1)\u003e';\n\u003e serialize({ a: { f }, g }, { space: 2 });\n\u003e // {\n\u003e //   \"a\": {\n\u003e //     \"f\": function f(){ return 1 }//\u003c/script\n\u003e //   },\n\u003e //   \"g\": function g(x){ return x } \u003e \u003cimg src=x onerror=alert(1)\u003e\n\u003e // }\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Embedded in a `\u003cscript\u003e` element, the script ends at the injected tag and the\n\u003e `\u003cimg\u003e` becomes a live element in the page.\n\u003e \n\u003e Exploitation requires an attacker to control the **source text** of a\n\u003e serialized function, in practice through a spoofed `toString()`. Real\n\u003e functions always end in `}`, so ordinary function values are not affected,\n\u003e and non-function values (including strings containing `\u003c/script`) are\n\u003e escaped correctly.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e \n\u003e Fixed in **7.1.3** (#235). The bare `\u003c/script` form is now also matched at\n\u003e the end of the function body, so it is escaped regardless of what follows it\n\u003e in the output.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e \n\u003e Upgrade to **7.1.3**. If you cannot upgrade, do not serialize function values\n\u003e whose source text (or `toString()`) can be influenced by an attacker.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by **ha_kr25** via the Yahoo bug bounty program.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | serialize-javascript | 7.1.0 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | serialize-javascript | 4.0.0 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | serialize-javascript | 6.0.2 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-m5mm-p8h7-m29v | serialize-javascript | 7.1.3 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-115754\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-115754\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-115754](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-115754)**.\n\n## [GHSA-m5mm-p8h7-m29v](https://osv.dev/GHSA-m5mm-p8h7-m29v)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e `serialize-javascript` escapes its output so it is safe to embed inside a\n\u003e `\u003cscript\u003e` element. Before 7.1.3 that guarantee did not hold for a **function\n\u003e value whose source ends in a bare `\u003c/script`**.\n\u003e \n\u003e Each function body is escaped on its own, and a bare `\u003c/script` was only\n\u003e neutralized when followed — within the same body — by a character the HTML\n\u003e tokenizer treats as ending the tag name (TAB, LF, FF, CR, SPACE, `/` or `\u003e`).\n\u003e A body ending exactly at `\u003c/script` has no following character, so it was\n\u003e emitted unescaped. The delimiter is then supplied by the surrounding output\n\u003e (for example the newline the `space` option emits after the value), and a\n\u003e later serialized value can supply the closing `\u003e` followed by markup:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```js\n\u003e const serialize = require('serialize-javascript');\n\u003e function f() {} f.toString = () =\u003e 'function f(){ return 1 }//\u003c/script';\n\u003e function g() {} g.toString = () =\u003e 'function g(x){ return x } \u003e \u003cimg src=x onerror=alert(1)\u003e';\n\u003e serialize({ a: { f }, g }, { space: 2 });\n\u003e // {\n\u003e //   \"a\": {\n\u003e //     \"f\": function f(){ return 1 }//\u003c/script\n\u003e //   },\n\u003e //   \"g\": function g(x){ return x } \u003e \u003cimg src=x onerror=alert(1)\u003e\n\u003e // }\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Embedded in a `\u003cscript\u003e` element, the script ends at the injected tag and the\n\u003e `\u003cimg\u003e` becomes a live element in the page.\n\u003e \n\u003e Exploitation requires an attacker to control the **source text** of a\n\u003e serialized function, in practice through a spoofed `toString()`. Real\n\u003e functions always end in `}`, so ordinary function values are not affected,\n\u003e and non-function values (including strings containing `\u003c/script`) are\n\u003e escaped correctly.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e \n\u003e Fixed in **7.1.3** (#235). The bare `\u003c/script` form is now also matched at\n\u003e the end of the function body, so it is escaped regardless of what follows it\n\u003e in the output.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e \n\u003e Upgrade to **7.1.3**. If you cannot upgrade, do not serialize function values\n\u003e whose source text (or `toString()`) can be influenced by an attacker.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Credits\n\u003e \n\u003e Reported by **ha_kr25** via the Yahoo bug bounty program.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | serialize-javascript | 7.1.0 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | serialize-javascript | 4.0.0 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | serialize-javascript | 6.0.2 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-m5mm-p8h7-m29v | serialize-javascript | 7.1.3 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-115754\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-115754\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
