              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Summary\n\nnbconvert \u003c= v7.17.1 has an arbitrary file write vulnerability due to a path traversal in ipynb cell output metadata, more specifically on the filename attribute.\n\nVulnerable converters : `--to markdown`, `--to latex`, `--to rst`, `--to asciidoc`.\n\nIn `ExtractOutputPreprocessor`, `extractoutput.py:116-119` joins attacker-controlled  `path` to `output_files_dir` with no canonicalization check, enabling arbitrary file write.\n\nThis is a sibling vulnerability of https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4c99-qj7h-p3vg.\n\n### Impact\n\nIf a victim runs nbconvert on a malicious ipynb file, it can create some files with arbitrary data in arbitrary locations, i.e. override authorized_keys.\n\nNote that running the cell with jupyter overrides the output, so it would \"clean up\" malicious cells.\n\n### PoC\n\nIn a ipynb file:\n\n```json\n\n\"cells\": [{\n        \"cell_type\": \"code\", \"id\": \"abc123\", \"execution_count\": 1,\n        \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": \"# PoC\",\n        \"outputs\": [{\n            \"output_type\": \"display_data\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n                \"filename\": \"../../../tmp/PWNED.png\"  # ← traverses outside output_dir\n            },\n            \"data\": {\n                # minimal valid PNG (1×1 pixel)\n                \"image/png\": \"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+M9QDwADhgGAWjR9awAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\"\n            }\n        }]\n    }]\n\n```\n\n\n### Patches\n\nFixed in \n- https://github.com/jupyter/nbconvert/commit/ce4bd99aec31d81d759fa8eeb8643179392ec66f\n- [7.17.2](https://github.com/jupyter/nbconvert/releases/tag/v7.17.2)",
                "text": "### Summary\n\nnbconvert \u003c= v7.17.1 has an arbitrary file write vulnerability due to a path traversal in ipynb cell output metadata, more specifically on the filename attribute.\n\nVulnerable converters : `--to markdown`, `--to latex`, `--to rst`, `--to asciidoc`.\n\nIn `ExtractOutputPreprocessor`, `extractoutput.py:116-119` joins attacker-controlled  `path` to `output_files_dir` with no canonicalization check, enabling arbitrary file write.\n\nThis is a sibling vulnerability of https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4c99-qj7h-p3vg.\n\n### Impact\n\nIf a victim runs nbconvert on a malicious ipynb file, it can create some files with arbitrary data in arbitrary locations, i.e. override authorized_keys.\n\nNote that running the cell with jupyter overrides the output, so it would \"clean up\" malicious cells.\n\n### PoC\n\nIn a ipynb file:\n\n```json\n\n\"cells\": [{\n        \"cell_type\": \"code\", \"id\": \"abc123\", \"execution_count\": 1,\n        \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": \"# PoC\",\n        \"outputs\": [{\n            \"output_type\": \"display_data\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n                \"filename\": \"../../../tmp/PWNED.png\"  # ← traverses outside output_dir\n            },\n            \"data\": {\n                # minimal valid PNG (1×1 pixel)\n                \"image/png\": \"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+M9QDwADhgGAWjR9awAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\"\n            }\n        }]\n    }]\n\n```\n\n\n### Patches\n\nFixed in \n- https://github.com/jupyter/nbconvert/commit/ce4bd99aec31d81d759fa8eeb8643179392ec66f\n- [7.17.2](https://github.com/jupyter/nbconvert/releases/tag/v7.17.2)"
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-114140](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-114140)**.\n\n## [GHSA-pjvx-prjx-h659](https://osv.dev/GHSA-pjvx-prjx-h659)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e nbconvert \u003c= v7.17.1 has an arbitrary file write vulnerability due to a path traversal in ipynb cell output metadata, more specifically on the filename attribute.\n\u003e \n\u003e Vulnerable converters : `--to markdown`, `--to latex`, `--to rst`, `--to asciidoc`.\n\u003e \n\u003e In `ExtractOutputPreprocessor`, `extractoutput.py:116-119` joins attacker-controlled  `path` to `output_files_dir` with no canonicalization check, enabling arbitrary file write.\n\u003e \n\u003e This is a sibling vulnerability of https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4c99-qj7h-p3vg.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e If a victim runs nbconvert on a malicious ipynb file, it can create some files with arbitrary data in arbitrary locations, i.e. override authorized_keys.\n\u003e \n\u003e Note that running the cell with jupyter overrides the output, so it would \"clean up\" malicious cells.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e In a ipynb file:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```json\n\u003e \n\u003e \"cells\": [{\n\u003e         \"cell_type\": \"code\", \"id\": \"abc123\", \"execution_count\": 1,\n\u003e         \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": \"# PoC\",\n\u003e         \"outputs\": [{\n\u003e             \"output_type\": \"display_data\",\n\u003e             \"metadata\": {\n\u003e                 \"filename\": \"../../../tmp/PWNED.png\"  # ← traverses outside output_dir\n\u003e             },\n\u003e             \"data\": {\n\u003e                 # minimal valid PNG (1×1 pixel)\n\u003e                 \"image/png\": \"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+M9QDwADhgGAWjR9awAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\"\n\u003e             }\n\u003e         }]\n\u003e     }]\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e \n\u003e Fixed in \n\u003e - https://github.com/jupyter/nbconvert/commit/ce4bd99aec31d81d759fa8eeb8643179392ec66f\n\u003e - [7.17.2](https://github.com/jupyter/nbconvert/releases/tag/v7.17.2)\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | nbconvert | 7.17.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-pjvx-prjx-h659 | nbconvert | 7.17.2 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-114140\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
