              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Impact\n\nWhen `typographer: true` is enabled, specially crafted Markdown can cause quadratic processing time in the smartquotes rule, potentially leading to denial of service in applications processing untrusted input.\n\nMany opening double quotes followed by unmatched closing single quotes cause repeated scans of the entire opener stack. The same issue occurs with the quote types reversed.\n\nThe default configuration (`typographer: false`) is not affected, but this option is enabled with high probability.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```js\nimport MarkdownIt from 'markdown-it'\nimport { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'\n\nconst md = new MarkdownIt({ typographer: true })\n\nfor (const k of [2000, 4000, 8000, 16000, 32000]) {\n  const input = '\"a '.repeat(k) + \"b' \".repeat(k)\n  const start = performance.now()\n  md.render(input)\n  console.log(input.length, (performance.now() - start).toFixed(1), 'ms')\n}\n```\n\nResult:\n\n|input size|time|\n|-|-|\n|12000|18ms|\n|24000|47ms|\n|48000|115ms|\n|96000|428ms|\n|192000|1586ms|\n\n### Patches\n\nFixed in **15.0.2** and **14.3.2**.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nDisable typography with `typographer: false`, or disable only the smartquotes rule:\n\n```js\nmd.disable('smartquotes')\n```",
                "text": "### Impact\n\nWhen `typographer: true` is enabled, specially crafted Markdown can cause quadratic processing time in the smartquotes rule, potentially leading to denial of service in applications processing untrusted input.\n\nMany opening double quotes followed by unmatched closing single quotes cause repeated scans of the entire opener stack. The same issue occurs with the quote types reversed.\n\nThe default configuration (`typographer: false`) is not affected, but this option is enabled with high probability.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```js\nimport MarkdownIt from 'markdown-it'\nimport { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'\n\nconst md = new MarkdownIt({ typographer: true })\n\nfor (const k of [2000, 4000, 8000, 16000, 32000]) {\n  const input = '\"a '.repeat(k) + \"b' \".repeat(k)\n  const start = performance.now()\n  md.render(input)\n  console.log(input.length, (performance.now() - start).toFixed(1), 'ms')\n}\n```\n\nResult:\n\n|input size|time|\n|-|-|\n|12000|18ms|\n|24000|47ms|\n|48000|115ms|\n|96000|428ms|\n|192000|1586ms|\n\n### Patches\n\nFixed in **15.0.2** and **14.3.2**.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nDisable typography with `typographer: false`, or disable only the smartquotes rule:\n\n```js\nmd.disable('smartquotes')\n```"
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-111759](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-111759)**.\n\n## [GHSA-r7fv-28h4-cvq7](https://osv.dev/GHSA-r7fv-28h4-cvq7)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e When `typographer: true` is enabled, specially crafted Markdown can cause quadratic processing time in the smartquotes rule, potentially leading to denial of service in applications processing untrusted input.\n\u003e \n\u003e Many opening double quotes followed by unmatched closing single quotes cause repeated scans of the entire opener stack. The same issue occurs with the quote types reversed.\n\u003e \n\u003e The default configuration (`typographer: false`) is not affected, but this option is enabled with high probability.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Reproduction\n\u003e \n\u003e ```js\n\u003e import MarkdownIt from 'markdown-it'\n\u003e import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'\n\u003e \n\u003e const md = new MarkdownIt({ typographer: true })\n\u003e \n\u003e for (const k of [2000, 4000, 8000, 16000, 32000]) {\n\u003e   const input = '\"a '.repeat(k) + \"b' \".repeat(k)\n\u003e   const start = performance.now()\n\u003e   md.render(input)\n\u003e   console.log(input.length, (performance.now() - start).toFixed(1), 'ms')\n\u003e }\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Result:\n\u003e \n\u003e |input size|time|\n\u003e |-|-|\n\u003e |12000|18ms|\n\u003e |24000|47ms|\n\u003e |48000|115ms|\n\u003e |96000|428ms|\n\u003e |192000|1586ms|\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e \n\u003e Fixed in **15.0.2** and **14.3.2**.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e \n\u003e Disable typography with `typographer: false`, or disable only the smartquotes rule:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```js\n\u003e md.disable('smartquotes')\n\u003e ```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | markdown-it | 14.3.0 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | markdown-it | 14.3.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-r7fv-28h4-cvq7 | markdown-it | 14.3.2, 15.0.2 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-111759\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-111759\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-111759](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-111759)**.\n\n## [GHSA-r7fv-28h4-cvq7](https://osv.dev/GHSA-r7fv-28h4-cvq7)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e When `typographer: true` is enabled, specially crafted Markdown can cause quadratic processing time in the smartquotes rule, potentially leading to denial of service in applications processing untrusted input.\n\u003e \n\u003e Many opening double quotes followed by unmatched closing single quotes cause repeated scans of the entire opener stack. The same issue occurs with the quote types reversed.\n\u003e \n\u003e The default configuration (`typographer: false`) is not affected, but this option is enabled with high probability.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Reproduction\n\u003e \n\u003e ```js\n\u003e import MarkdownIt from 'markdown-it'\n\u003e import { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks'\n\u003e \n\u003e const md = new MarkdownIt({ typographer: true })\n\u003e \n\u003e for (const k of [2000, 4000, 8000, 16000, 32000]) {\n\u003e   const input = '\"a '.repeat(k) + \"b' \".repeat(k)\n\u003e   const start = performance.now()\n\u003e   md.render(input)\n\u003e   console.log(input.length, (performance.now() - start).toFixed(1), 'ms')\n\u003e }\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Result:\n\u003e \n\u003e |input size|time|\n\u003e |-|-|\n\u003e |12000|18ms|\n\u003e |24000|47ms|\n\u003e |48000|115ms|\n\u003e |96000|428ms|\n\u003e |192000|1586ms|\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e \n\u003e Fixed in **15.0.2** and **14.3.2**.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e \n\u003e Disable typography with `typographer: false`, or disable only the smartquotes rule:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```js\n\u003e md.disable('smartquotes')\n\u003e ```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | markdown-it | 14.3.0 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | markdown-it | 14.3.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-r7fv-28h4-cvq7 | markdown-it | 14.3.2, 15.0.2 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-111759\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-111759\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
