              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Summary\n\n`launch-editor` forwarded file paths directly to editors without sanitization. If a path resembles a CLI flag, editors like Vim may interpret it as a command, potentially causing unintended file overwrites or command execution.\n\n### Impact\n\n#### Direct `launch-editor` users\n\nOnly apps that match all of the following conditions are affected:\n\n- The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n- The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n  - Vim (including gVim)\n  - MacVim\n  - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n  - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n- The first argument of `launchEditor` can start with `+` or `-` or the user is using WSL\n\n#### `launch-editor-middleware` users\n\nOnly apps that match the following conditions are affected:\n\n- The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n- The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n  - Vim (including gVim)\n  - MacVim\n  - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n  - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n- launch-editor older than v2.2.0 is used, or the user is using WSL\n\n#### Vite users\n\nOnly apps that match the following conditions are affected:\n\n- The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n- The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n  - Vim (including gVim)\n  - MacVim\n  - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n  - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n- The user is using WSL\n\n### Details\n\n`launchEditor(file)` function passes the file name as-is to the editor if the file with that file name exists. If the file name starts with `-` (also `+` for Vim), the editor treats them as flags rather than positional arguments. For example, Vim treats arguments starting with `+` as an Ex command. As a result, an existing relative directory such as:\n```\n+call writefile([\"SAFE_MARKER\"],\"LAUNCH_EDITOR_MARKER\")|qa!\n```\nis not treated as a filename when passed to Vim. Vim executes the embedded Ex command.\n\nThe following editor has a potentially destructive operation exposed to the CLI arguments:\n- Vim (including gVim)\n- MacVim\n- Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n- Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\n`launch-editor-middleware` v2.2.0+ converts the passed file path to an absolute path so those are not affected as long as the user is not using WSL. For WSL, `launch-editor` converts the paths to relative paths internally, so those are still affected.\n\nVite 2.0.0+ uses `launch-editor-middleware` v2.2.0+ so the WSL users are only affected.",
                "text": "### Summary\n\n`launch-editor` forwarded file paths directly to editors without sanitization. If a path resembles a CLI flag, editors like Vim may interpret it as a command, potentially causing unintended file overwrites or command execution.\n\n### Impact\n\n#### Direct `launch-editor` users\n\nOnly apps that match all of the following conditions are affected:\n\n- The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n- The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n  - Vim (including gVim)\n  - MacVim\n  - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n  - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n- The first argument of `launchEditor` can start with `+` or `-` or the user is using WSL\n\n#### `launch-editor-middleware` users\n\nOnly apps that match the following conditions are affected:\n\n- The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n- The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n  - Vim (including gVim)\n  - MacVim\n  - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n  - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n- launch-editor older than v2.2.0 is used, or the user is using WSL\n\n#### Vite users\n\nOnly apps that match the following conditions are affected:\n\n- The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n- The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n  - Vim (including gVim)\n  - MacVim\n  - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n  - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n- The user is using WSL\n\n### Details\n\n`launchEditor(file)` function passes the file name as-is to the editor if the file with that file name exists. If the file name starts with `-` (also `+` for Vim), the editor treats them as flags rather than positional arguments. For example, Vim treats arguments starting with `+` as an Ex command. As a result, an existing relative directory such as:\n```\n+call writefile([\"SAFE_MARKER\"],\"LAUNCH_EDITOR_MARKER\")|qa!\n```\nis not treated as a filename when passed to Vim. Vim executes the embedded Ex command.\n\nThe following editor has a potentially destructive operation exposed to the CLI arguments:\n- Vim (including gVim)\n- MacVim\n- Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n- Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\n`launch-editor-middleware` v2.2.0+ converts the passed file path to an absolute path so those are not affected as long as the user is not using WSL. For WSL, `launch-editor` converts the paths to relative paths internally, so those are still affected.\n\nVite 2.0.0+ uses `launch-editor-middleware` v2.2.0+ so the WSL users are only affected."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-112944](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-112944)**.\n\n## [GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw](https://osv.dev/GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e `launch-editor` forwarded file paths directly to editors without sanitization. If a path resembles a CLI flag, editors like Vim may interpret it as a command, potentially causing unintended file overwrites or command execution.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e #### Direct `launch-editor` users\n\u003e \n\u003e Only apps that match all of the following conditions are affected:\n\u003e \n\u003e - The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n\u003e - The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n\u003e   - Vim (including gVim)\n\u003e   - MacVim\n\u003e   - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n\u003e   - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\u003e - The first argument of `launchEditor` can start with `+` or `-` or the user is using WSL\n\u003e \n\u003e #### `launch-editor-middleware` users\n\u003e \n\u003e Only apps that match the following conditions are affected:\n\u003e \n\u003e - The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n\u003e - The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n\u003e   - Vim (including gVim)\n\u003e   - MacVim\n\u003e   - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n\u003e   - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\u003e - launch-editor older than v2.2.0 is used, or the user is using WSL\n\u003e \n\u003e #### Vite users\n\u003e \n\u003e Only apps that match the following conditions are affected:\n\u003e \n\u003e - The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n\u003e - The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n\u003e   - Vim (including gVim)\n\u003e   - MacVim\n\u003e   - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n\u003e   - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\u003e - The user is using WSL\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e \n\u003e `launchEditor(file)` function passes the file name as-is to the editor if the file with that file name exists. If the file name starts with `-` (also `+` for Vim), the editor treats them as flags rather than positional arguments. For example, Vim treats arguments starting with `+` as an Ex command. As a result, an existing relative directory such as:\n\u003e ```\n\u003e +call writefile([\"SAFE_MARKER\"],\"LAUNCH_EDITOR_MARKER\")|qa!\n\u003e ```\n\u003e is not treated as a filename when passed to Vim. Vim executes the embedded Ex command.\n\u003e \n\u003e The following editor has a potentially destructive operation exposed to the CLI arguments:\n\u003e - Vim (including gVim)\n\u003e - MacVim\n\u003e - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n\u003e - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\u003e \n\u003e `launch-editor-middleware` v2.2.0+ converts the passed file path to an absolute path so those are not affected as long as the user is not using WSL. For WSL, `launch-editor` converts the paths to relative paths internally, so those are still affected.\n\u003e \n\u003e Vite 2.0.0+ uses `launch-editor-middleware` v2.2.0+ so the WSL users are only affected.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | launch-editor | 2.14.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | launch-editor | 2.14.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw | launch-editor | 2.14.2 |\n| GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw | vite | 6.4.4, 7.3.7, 8.1.6, 8.2.4, 8.3.3 |\n| GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw | vite-plus | 1.1.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112944\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112944\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-112944](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-112944)**.\n\n## [GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw](https://osv.dev/GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e `launch-editor` forwarded file paths directly to editors without sanitization. If a path resembles a CLI flag, editors like Vim may interpret it as a command, potentially causing unintended file overwrites or command execution.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e #### Direct `launch-editor` users\n\u003e \n\u003e Only apps that match all of the following conditions are affected:\n\u003e \n\u003e - The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n\u003e - The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n\u003e   - Vim (including gVim)\n\u003e   - MacVim\n\u003e   - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n\u003e   - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\u003e - The first argument of `launchEditor` can start with `+` or `-` or the user is using WSL\n\u003e \n\u003e #### `launch-editor-middleware` users\n\u003e \n\u003e Only apps that match the following conditions are affected:\n\u003e \n\u003e - The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n\u003e - The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n\u003e   - Vim (including gVim)\n\u003e   - MacVim\n\u003e   - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n\u003e   - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\u003e - launch-editor older than v2.2.0 is used, or the user is using WSL\n\u003e \n\u003e #### Vite users\n\u003e \n\u003e Only apps that match the following conditions are affected:\n\u003e \n\u003e - The attacker is able to create a file system entry (e.g. a file or directory) starting with `+` or `-` in the working directory\n\u003e - The user uses or the app specifies any of the following editors:\n\u003e   - Vim (including gVim)\n\u003e   - MacVim\n\u003e   - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n\u003e   - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\u003e - The user is using WSL\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e \n\u003e `launchEditor(file)` function passes the file name as-is to the editor if the file with that file name exists. If the file name starts with `-` (also `+` for Vim), the editor treats them as flags rather than positional arguments. For example, Vim treats arguments starting with `+` as an Ex command. As a result, an existing relative directory such as:\n\u003e ```\n\u003e +call writefile([\"SAFE_MARKER\"],\"LAUNCH_EDITOR_MARKER\")|qa!\n\u003e ```\n\u003e is not treated as a filename when passed to Vim. Vim executes the embedded Ex command.\n\u003e \n\u003e The following editor has a potentially destructive operation exposed to the CLI arguments:\n\u003e - Vim (including gVim)\n\u003e - MacVim\n\u003e - Emacs (including Emacsclient)\n\u003e - Notepad++ (only if using a plugin exposing dangerous operations via plugin messages)\n\u003e \n\u003e `launch-editor-middleware` v2.2.0+ converts the passed file path to an absolute path so those are not affected as long as the user is not using WSL. For WSL, `launch-editor` converts the paths to relative paths internally, so those are still affected.\n\u003e \n\u003e Vite 2.0.0+ uses `launch-editor-middleware` v2.2.0+ so the WSL users are only affected.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | launch-editor | 2.14.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | launch-editor | 2.14.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw | launch-editor | 2.14.2 |\n| GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw | vite | 6.4.4, 7.3.7, 8.1.6, 8.2.4, 8.3.3 |\n| GHSA-r825-w8mm-5pxw | vite-plus | 1.1.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112944\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112944\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
