              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Summary\n\nThe first 4 bytes of files outside of `server.fs` setting can be returned to the browser by a request containing `?vite-wasm-instance`.\n\n### Impact\n\n Only apps that match one of the following conditions are affected:\n\n- explicitly expose the Vite dev server to the network using `--host` or the [`server.host`](https://vite.dev/config/server-options#server-host) option\n- there's a file that has a sensitive information in **the first 4 bytes**\n- uses Node.js or Deno to run Vite (if Bun is used, it is not affected)\n\n### Details\nRequests containing the `?vite-wasm-instance` query are handled by the internal Wasm plugin's `load` hook. The hook removes the query and reads the resulting path directly from disk, but the `server.fs` checks were not applied.\n\nAfter reading the file, Vite attempts to parse it as WebAssembly. When that parse fails, Node and deno throws an error that contains the first 4 bytes of the file.\n\n### PoC\n\nCreate a denied file and start an affected Vite dev server:\n\n```bash\necho 'SECRET_KEY=abc123\\n' \u003e .env\nnpm run dev\ncurl 'http://localhost:5173/.env?vite-wasm-instance'\n```\n\nThis will show\n```\nFailed to parse WASM file \"\u003croot\u003e/.env\": WebAssembly.compile(): expected magic word 00 61 73 6d, found 53 45 43 52 @+0\n```",
                "text": "### Summary\n\nThe first 4 bytes of files outside of `server.fs` setting can be returned to the browser by a request containing `?vite-wasm-instance`.\n\n### Impact\n\n Only apps that match one of the following conditions are affected:\n\n- explicitly expose the Vite dev server to the network using `--host` or the [`server.host`](https://vite.dev/config/server-options#server-host) option\n- there's a file that has a sensitive information in **the first 4 bytes**\n- uses Node.js or Deno to run Vite (if Bun is used, it is not affected)\n\n### Details\nRequests containing the `?vite-wasm-instance` query are handled by the internal Wasm plugin's `load` hook. The hook removes the query and reads the resulting path directly from disk, but the `server.fs` checks were not applied.\n\nAfter reading the file, Vite attempts to parse it as WebAssembly. When that parse fails, Node and deno throws an error that contains the first 4 bytes of the file.\n\n### PoC\n\nCreate a denied file and start an affected Vite dev server:\n\n```bash\necho 'SECRET_KEY=abc123\\n' \u003e .env\nnpm run dev\ncurl 'http://localhost:5173/.env?vite-wasm-instance'\n```\n\nThis will show\n```\nFailed to parse WASM file \"\u003croot\u003e/.env\": WebAssembly.compile(): expected magic word 00 61 73 6d, found 53 45 43 52 @+0\n```"
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-112947](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-112947)**.\n\n## [GHSA-vfpm-58rq-9qcg](https://osv.dev/GHSA-vfpm-58rq-9qcg)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The first 4 bytes of files outside of `server.fs` setting can be returned to the browser by a request containing `?vite-wasm-instance`.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e  Only apps that match one of the following conditions are affected:\n\u003e \n\u003e - explicitly expose the Vite dev server to the network using `--host` or the [`server.host`](https://vite.dev/config/server-options#server-host) option\n\u003e - there's a file that has a sensitive information in **the first 4 bytes**\n\u003e - uses Node.js or Deno to run Vite (if Bun is used, it is not affected)\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e Requests containing the `?vite-wasm-instance` query are handled by the internal Wasm plugin's `load` hook. The hook removes the query and reads the resulting path directly from disk, but the `server.fs` checks were not applied.\n\u003e \n\u003e After reading the file, Vite attempts to parse it as WebAssembly. When that parse fails, Node and deno throws an error that contains the first 4 bytes of the file.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e Create a denied file and start an affected Vite dev server:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```bash\n\u003e echo 'SECRET_KEY=abc123\\n' \u003e .env\n\u003e npm run dev\n\u003e curl 'http://localhost:5173/.env?vite-wasm-instance'\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e This will show\n\u003e ```\n\u003e Failed to parse WASM file \"\u003croot\u003e/.env\": WebAssembly.compile(): expected magic word 00 61 73 6d, found 53 45 43 52 @+0\n\u003e ```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-vfpm-58rq-9qcg | vite | 8.2.4, 8.3.3 |\n| GHSA-vfpm-58rq-9qcg | vite-plus | 1.1.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112947\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112947\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-112947](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-112947)**.\n\n## [GHSA-vfpm-58rq-9qcg](https://osv.dev/GHSA-vfpm-58rq-9qcg)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e The first 4 bytes of files outside of `server.fs` setting can be returned to the browser by a request containing `?vite-wasm-instance`.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e  Only apps that match one of the following conditions are affected:\n\u003e \n\u003e - explicitly expose the Vite dev server to the network using `--host` or the [`server.host`](https://vite.dev/config/server-options#server-host) option\n\u003e - there's a file that has a sensitive information in **the first 4 bytes**\n\u003e - uses Node.js or Deno to run Vite (if Bun is used, it is not affected)\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e Requests containing the `?vite-wasm-instance` query are handled by the internal Wasm plugin's `load` hook. The hook removes the query and reads the resulting path directly from disk, but the `server.fs` checks were not applied.\n\u003e \n\u003e After reading the file, Vite attempts to parse it as WebAssembly. When that parse fails, Node and deno throws an error that contains the first 4 bytes of the file.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e Create a denied file and start an affected Vite dev server:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```bash\n\u003e echo 'SECRET_KEY=abc123\\n' \u003e .env\n\u003e npm run dev\n\u003e curl 'http://localhost:5173/.env?vite-wasm-instance'\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e This will show\n\u003e ```\n\u003e Failed to parse WASM file \"\u003croot\u003e/.env\": WebAssembly.compile(): expected magic word 00 61 73 6d, found 53 45 43 52 @+0\n\u003e ```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | vite | 8.2.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-vfpm-58rq-9qcg | vite | 8.2.4, 8.3.3 |\n| GHSA-vfpm-58rq-9qcg | vite-plus | 1.1.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112947\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112947\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
