              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Summary\n\nOn Windows, attacker-controlled content in a wheel's\n`.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt` can cause setuptools' legacy wheel\ninstallation path to create an `__init__.py` outside the requested\n`destination_eggdir`.\n\nThe attacker can influence the destination path, but not the contents of\nthe created file.\n\n### Details\n\nTested setuptools commit:\n\n`6ead555c5fb29bc57fe6105b1bffc163f56fd558`\n\nRelevant source:\n\n`setuptools/wheel.py`\n\nSHA-256:\n\n`359b7e0d5dd8c3135653abe08a8ed5dc0352eadfd7df22cb5e2b5303b7c3cafd`\n\nThe relevant call path is:\n\n`Wheel(wheel_path).install_as_egg(destination)`\n→ `_install_as_egg`\n→ `_convert_metadata`\n→ `_fix_namespace_packages`\n\nA wheel can provide attacker-controlled content in:\n\n`\u003cdistribution\u003e.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`\n\nThe namespace value is eventually used approximately as:\n\n```python\nmod_dir = os.path.join(destination_eggdir, *mod.split('.'))\nmod_init = os.path.join(mod_dir, '__init__.py')\n\nIf mod is a Windows drive-qualified absolute path containing no dots,\nmod.split('.') preserves it as a single component.\nOn Windows, os.path.join(destination_eggdir, absolute_component) discards\nthe original base directory and resolves to the attacker-supplied absolute\npath.\nThe existing wheel filename and ZIP traversal checks do not validate this\nmetadata value before it is subsequently interpreted as a filesystem path.\n\n```markdown\n### PoC\n\nThe reproduction was performed entirely inside a disposable temporary\ndirectory.\n\nLayout:\n\n```text\nsandbox/\n    destination/\n    outside/\n    input/\n    canary.txt\n```\n\nA synthetic wheel was created containing:\n\n`demo_pkg-1.0.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`\n\nwhose content was the absolute path of:\n\n`sandbox\\outside`\n\nThe real acquired setuptools implementation was then invoked:\n\n```python\nsetuptools.wheel.Wheel(synthetic_wheel).install_as_egg(\n    sandbox_destination\n)\n```\n\nThe operation completed without exception.\n\nExpected metadata was created under:\n\n`sandbox\\destination\\EGG-INFO`\n\nbut setuptools also created:\n\n`sandbox\\outside\\__init__.py`\n\nThe file did not exist before execution.\n\nIts contents were:\n\n```python\n__import__('pkg_resources').declare_namespace(__name__)\n```\n\nThe unrelated canary remained byte-identical.\n\nThe sandbox was deleted after recording the evidence.\n```\n\n\n### Impact\n\nA crafted wheel can cause setuptools to create a fixed-content\n`__init__.py` outside the intended installation directory at a\nfilesystem path influenced by the wheel, with the permissions of the\nprocess performing the installation.\n\nThe demonstrated reproduction required the target parent directory to\nalready exist.",
                "text": "### Summary\n\nOn Windows, attacker-controlled content in a wheel's\n`.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt` can cause setuptools' legacy wheel\ninstallation path to create an `__init__.py` outside the requested\n`destination_eggdir`.\n\nThe attacker can influence the destination path, but not the contents of\nthe created file.\n\n### Details\n\nTested setuptools commit:\n\n`6ead555c5fb29bc57fe6105b1bffc163f56fd558`\n\nRelevant source:\n\n`setuptools/wheel.py`\n\nSHA-256:\n\n`359b7e0d5dd8c3135653abe08a8ed5dc0352eadfd7df22cb5e2b5303b7c3cafd`\n\nThe relevant call path is:\n\n`Wheel(wheel_path).install_as_egg(destination)`\n→ `_install_as_egg`\n→ `_convert_metadata`\n→ `_fix_namespace_packages`\n\nA wheel can provide attacker-controlled content in:\n\n`\u003cdistribution\u003e.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`\n\nThe namespace value is eventually used approximately as:\n\n```python\nmod_dir = os.path.join(destination_eggdir, *mod.split('.'))\nmod_init = os.path.join(mod_dir, '__init__.py')\n\nIf mod is a Windows drive-qualified absolute path containing no dots,\nmod.split('.') preserves it as a single component.\nOn Windows, os.path.join(destination_eggdir, absolute_component) discards\nthe original base directory and resolves to the attacker-supplied absolute\npath.\nThe existing wheel filename and ZIP traversal checks do not validate this\nmetadata value before it is subsequently interpreted as a filesystem path.\n\n```markdown\n### PoC\n\nThe reproduction was performed entirely inside a disposable temporary\ndirectory.\n\nLayout:\n\n```text\nsandbox/\n    destination/\n    outside/\n    input/\n    canary.txt\n```\n\nA synthetic wheel was created containing:\n\n`demo_pkg-1.0.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`\n\nwhose content was the absolute path of:\n\n`sandbox\\outside`\n\nThe real acquired setuptools implementation was then invoked:\n\n```python\nsetuptools.wheel.Wheel(synthetic_wheel).install_as_egg(\n    sandbox_destination\n)\n```\n\nThe operation completed without exception.\n\nExpected metadata was created under:\n\n`sandbox\\destination\\EGG-INFO`\n\nbut setuptools also created:\n\n`sandbox\\outside\\__init__.py`\n\nThe file did not exist before execution.\n\nIts contents were:\n\n```python\n__import__('pkg_resources').declare_namespace(__name__)\n```\n\nThe unrelated canary remained byte-identical.\n\nThe sandbox was deleted after recording the evidence.\n```\n\n\n### Impact\n\nA crafted wheel can cause setuptools to create a fixed-content\n`__init__.py` outside the intended installation directory at a\nfilesystem path influenced by the wheel, with the permissions of the\nprocess performing the installation.\n\nThe demonstrated reproduction required the target parent directory to\nalready exist."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w](https://osv.dev/GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w)**.\n\n## [GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w](https://osv.dev/GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e On Windows, attacker-controlled content in a wheel's\n\u003e `.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt` can cause setuptools' legacy wheel\n\u003e installation path to create an `__init__.py` outside the requested\n\u003e `destination_eggdir`.\n\u003e \n\u003e The attacker can influence the destination path, but not the contents of\n\u003e the created file.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e \n\u003e Tested setuptools commit:\n\u003e \n\u003e `6ead555c5fb29bc57fe6105b1bffc163f56fd558`\n\u003e \n\u003e Relevant source:\n\u003e \n\u003e `setuptools/wheel.py`\n\u003e \n\u003e SHA-256:\n\u003e \n\u003e `359b7e0d5dd8c3135653abe08a8ed5dc0352eadfd7df22cb5e2b5303b7c3cafd`\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant call path is:\n\u003e \n\u003e `Wheel(wheel_path).install_as_egg(destination)`\n\u003e → `_install_as_egg`\n\u003e → `_convert_metadata`\n\u003e → `_fix_namespace_packages`\n\u003e \n\u003e A wheel can provide attacker-controlled content in:\n\u003e \n\u003e `\u003cdistribution\u003e.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`\n\u003e \n\u003e The namespace value is eventually used approximately as:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e mod_dir = os.path.join(destination_eggdir, *mod.split('.'))\n\u003e mod_init = os.path.join(mod_dir, '__init__.py')\n\u003e \n\u003e If mod is a Windows drive-qualified absolute path containing no dots,\n\u003e mod.split('.') preserves it as a single component.\n\u003e On Windows, os.path.join(destination_eggdir, absolute_component) discards\n\u003e the original base directory and resolves to the attacker-supplied absolute\n\u003e path.\n\u003e The existing wheel filename and ZIP traversal checks do not validate this\n\u003e metadata value before it is subsequently interpreted as a filesystem path.\n\u003e \n\u003e ```markdown\n\u003e ### PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e The reproduction was performed entirely inside a disposable temporary\n\u003e directory.\n\u003e \n\u003e Layout:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e sandbox/\n\u003e     destination/\n\u003e     outside/\n\u003e     input/\n\u003e     canary.txt\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e A synthetic wheel was created containing:\n\u003e \n\u003e `demo_pkg-1.0.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`\n\u003e \n\u003e whose content was the absolute path of:\n\u003e \n\u003e `sandbox\\outside`\n\u003e \n\u003e The real acquired setuptools implementation was then invoked:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e setuptools.wheel.Wheel(synthetic_wheel).install_as_egg(\n\u003e     sandbox_destination\n\u003e )\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e The operation completed without exception.\n\u003e \n\u003e Expected metadata was created under:\n\u003e \n\u003e `sandbox\\destination\\EGG-INFO`\n\u003e \n\u003e but setuptools also created:\n\u003e \n\u003e `sandbox\\outside\\__init__.py`\n\u003e \n\u003e The file did not exist before execution.\n\u003e \n\u003e Its contents were:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e __import__('pkg_resources').declare_namespace(__name__)\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e The unrelated canary remained byte-identical.\n\u003e \n\u003e The sandbox was deleted after recording the evidence.\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e A crafted wheel can cause setuptools to create a fixed-content\n\u003e `__init__.py` outside the intended installation directory at a\n\u003e filesystem path influenced by the wheel, with the permissions of the\n\u003e process performing the installation.\n\u003e \n\u003e The demonstrated reproduction required the target parent directory to\n\u003e already exist.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | setuptools | 84.0.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w | setuptools | 84.1.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w](https://osv.dev/GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w)**.\n\n## [GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w](https://osv.dev/GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e On Windows, attacker-controlled content in a wheel's\n\u003e `.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt` can cause setuptools' legacy wheel\n\u003e installation path to create an `__init__.py` outside the requested\n\u003e `destination_eggdir`.\n\u003e \n\u003e The attacker can influence the destination path, but not the contents of\n\u003e the created file.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e \n\u003e Tested setuptools commit:\n\u003e \n\u003e `6ead555c5fb29bc57fe6105b1bffc163f56fd558`\n\u003e \n\u003e Relevant source:\n\u003e \n\u003e `setuptools/wheel.py`\n\u003e \n\u003e SHA-256:\n\u003e \n\u003e `359b7e0d5dd8c3135653abe08a8ed5dc0352eadfd7df22cb5e2b5303b7c3cafd`\n\u003e \n\u003e The relevant call path is:\n\u003e \n\u003e `Wheel(wheel_path).install_as_egg(destination)`\n\u003e → `_install_as_egg`\n\u003e → `_convert_metadata`\n\u003e → `_fix_namespace_packages`\n\u003e \n\u003e A wheel can provide attacker-controlled content in:\n\u003e \n\u003e `\u003cdistribution\u003e.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`\n\u003e \n\u003e The namespace value is eventually used approximately as:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e mod_dir = os.path.join(destination_eggdir, *mod.split('.'))\n\u003e mod_init = os.path.join(mod_dir, '__init__.py')\n\u003e \n\u003e If mod is a Windows drive-qualified absolute path containing no dots,\n\u003e mod.split('.') preserves it as a single component.\n\u003e On Windows, os.path.join(destination_eggdir, absolute_component) discards\n\u003e the original base directory and resolves to the attacker-supplied absolute\n\u003e path.\n\u003e The existing wheel filename and ZIP traversal checks do not validate this\n\u003e metadata value before it is subsequently interpreted as a filesystem path.\n\u003e \n\u003e ```markdown\n\u003e ### PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e The reproduction was performed entirely inside a disposable temporary\n\u003e directory.\n\u003e \n\u003e Layout:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e sandbox/\n\u003e     destination/\n\u003e     outside/\n\u003e     input/\n\u003e     canary.txt\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e A synthetic wheel was created containing:\n\u003e \n\u003e `demo_pkg-1.0.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`\n\u003e \n\u003e whose content was the absolute path of:\n\u003e \n\u003e `sandbox\\outside`\n\u003e \n\u003e The real acquired setuptools implementation was then invoked:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e setuptools.wheel.Wheel(synthetic_wheel).install_as_egg(\n\u003e     sandbox_destination\n\u003e )\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e The operation completed without exception.\n\u003e \n\u003e Expected metadata was created under:\n\u003e \n\u003e `sandbox\\destination\\EGG-INFO`\n\u003e \n\u003e but setuptools also created:\n\u003e \n\u003e `sandbox\\outside\\__init__.py`\n\u003e \n\u003e The file did not exist before execution.\n\u003e \n\u003e Its contents were:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e __import__('pkg_resources').declare_namespace(__name__)\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e The unrelated canary remained byte-identical.\n\u003e \n\u003e The sandbox was deleted after recording the evidence.\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e A crafted wheel can cause setuptools to create a fixed-content\n\u003e `__init__.py` outside the intended installation directory at a\n\u003e filesystem path influenced by the wheel, with the permissions of the\n\u003e process performing the installation.\n\u003e \n\u003e The demonstrated reproduction required the target parent directory to\n\u003e already exist.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | setuptools | 84.0.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w | setuptools | 84.1.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
